{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730408Z","id":"b8aab2610f59a590ca413b5cd9fd9ca479849a735320deea10160a2155467fa0","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools here gets no upgrade-hold probe (with_upgrade_hold is never called), so status over the daemon-served MCP endpoint never carries upgrade_held (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1285-1290). The shim, the CLI and Pi report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"a25bc2b65e3c49b01b8458ea877c1bfa039ac0f80052a5a7d7e7d1450f8652e6"},"summary":"The daemon's own /mcp status does not report upgrade_held","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730968Z","id":"35baa8b0f265d09f864dd92ddd5918392c44ca0074f4c8ca9c750c6c90dfb0d8","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207526Z","id":"883584b3ad6905461c2178a9d2f613cbafef211ee0535b8d509519da776a6fe0","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools here gets no upgrade-hold probe (with_upgrade_hold is never called), so status over the daemon-served MCP endpoint never carries upgrade_held (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1285-1290). The shim, the CLI and Pi report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"bf718c5220791a2ab835891ca9f59556af6e625096c9dfa63042bde16d094a30"},"summary":"The daemon's own /mcp status does not report upgrade_held","supersedes":"b8aab2610f59a590ca413b5cd9fd9ca479849a735320deea10160a2155467fa0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207627Z","id":"3f206f41a6e6622d8ee312c392795dff19fa491a82e5981aba47e01580a9e799","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":346},"end":{"line":348},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"35baa8b0f265d09f864dd92ddd5918392c44ca0074f4c8ca9c750c6c90dfb0d8","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661400Z","id":"c20422c881c5477cc8c3cad8c4ba4fa548a42217e77edaa703fdb7ff38926c3d","body":{"detail":"for_asker() sets question.artifact.title to null for Caller::PersonAgent whatever its approvals: the title is an author field (spec §8.2) and no Visibility exists yet. The owner's GET /api/questions and GET /api/questions/{qid} leave out questions of sessions with a person (store questions.rs owners!()), but crate::inbox::views still renders them as items of the owner's inbox (spec §18 wants the per-person inbox).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"95fe0b615c046cbaa45b6cd1d490d59fcff730299fe894d98ab591a843574543"},"suggested_fix":"Replace for_asker with the visibility filter when questions are filtered, and scope the inbox's question items per person (migration 25's per-person inbox).","summary":"A person's agent's question view nulls the artifact title instead of filtering it, and its questions still reach the owner's inbox","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661648Z","id":"5f9d0c3719de303c1d4fa01a79067f54bcf54f066ef37945baaa6859804ccde8","body":{"detail":"Handlers used to test has_token(); they now match Caller::Owner { .. } | Caller::OwnerAgent { .. } (sees_sessions here, may_act_as_agent in routes/threads.rs:97). Caller::Owner { browser: true } is the same for an owner-cookie request with or without Authorization, so a cookie-only owner browser now gets owner_session_id and session_id fields, clip_path, and reopens or deletes threads without a display name. The golden (agent outputs) is unchanged; spec §19 lists the single-owner changes allowed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"42d94c9021c52275c4f0fed69144d8ebf1256cb93d4e433d48c7ebe76eb4e5d1"},"suggested_fix":"If the shell always sends the token, nothing changes; otherwise carry 'token presented' on Caller::Owner, or confirm this as one of spec §19's changes.","summary":"An owner browser without the token now counts as holding it for session IDs, clip paths and naming-free reopen and delete","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661875Z","id":"cca46f70442d60b2e4f8aa28b8770c585f21e7568aad38e1e0523415e567ed09","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":413},"end":{"line":413},"content_hash":"6f454b38ce15c8406225a3dc6f372035a2fc1b9cfd6cd1f0ed4745a1e42acbd6"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.662289Z","id":"2b60c45840e14af3c85c7654b59d52fd1a0d9d04870fd80070765919a17ca139","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1273},"end":{"line":1289},"content_hash":"4cb1fe9c2f23e827cfe65137e29b2bdf9ec189af81cd7552c358da87cb9c462a"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.662516Z","id":"425281edaf48edda6779e6e5024f24ded118ed103d17dffddfad761e4fb747d4","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1627},"end":{"line":1653},"content_hash":"83ed7864ba2897d0ff8421cfe185f069945dfbf2b21b7f774ccc58438abe14d5"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:52:59.949688Z","id":"bc65306f1ff4cad943f3cf43ebf3917faf1f9980f6ab900fd96b57c5abfdf894","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"fdef32ef55ec060aeebfe4fd3b77d7814bf6706887dea024f0f20ef0a60067d3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:53:00.002015Z","id":"f58112a5282ca4d26a7acd7758b5d6ded066572274d348275d83b35dee3a3d9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:428c611","summary":"Fixed: Agent::holds_token() (the daemon token alone) now decides session IDs, clip paths and the name check (routes/artifacts.rs, routes/threads.rs may_act_as_agent). Test api_canary::the_owners_cookie_alone_is_not_the_token passes; with holds_token() widened to Caller::Owner it fails.","supersedes":"5f9d0c3719de303c1d4fa01a79067f54bcf54f066ef37945baaa6859804ccde8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970234Z","id":"c5595c22e7fafbf59719371cde3020e684786a794501fdcd325869c5c05fefb9","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"6f454b38ce15c8406225a3dc6f372035a2fc1b9cfd6cd1f0ed4745a1e42acbd6"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","supersedes":"cca46f70442d60b2e4f8aa28b8770c585f21e7568aad38e1e0523415e567ed09","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970489Z","id":"bd6301a402ac7d7fbb6f04b75a0c875b289ee6167f0af811d68bd7d0b7a3260d","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1640},"end":{"line":1666},"content_hash":"83ed7864ba2897d0ff8421cfe185f069945dfbf2b21b7f774ccc58438abe14d5"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"425281edaf48edda6779e6e5024f24ded118ed103d17dffddfad761e4fb747d4","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970811Z","id":"4055a6f8cca3f3235a912b745deaa277c7a99ddfeee284a25843c847a4b1f21f","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"2f6f9f83cb96b2053f47df36762060ba5f55db77755bc5da57e3e4b355b18b25"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971085Z","id":"12bc834768f3652b24d3ae4fe8e18ecc8ec1680362b55c2f079451833ce926f2","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":452},"end":{"line":453},"content_hash":"d616bfd5a1a1a480f8733a7c3467b538a639ad6eea8827c4f32a507f9d48cc9c"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971229Z","id":"b4bf1f08d4c561fd1512fcb8d8c99cf70ccc391bdbe1b4739980e5c82bfc1ad3","body":{"detail":"mint now refuses the owner's agents (not_for_agents). clax native-host builds its Client with channel::from_process, so if Chrome inherited CLAUDECODE, CODEX_* or PI_CODING_AGENT from a shell it was launched from, the native host marks itself an agent channel and pairing fails with 403.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"0a3ac3d0f6add4915352c4d6de1a82da7fc50c6e21fb44f0a2bb7bd80c378596"},"summary":"The native host cannot pair when Chrome was started from a harness's shell","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:55.332167Z","id":"2da84c9808d4ea68fc9560c9f7826c6a6d78a134c253a5d73ebb8a01c9b716a2","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1280},"end":{"line":1296},"content_hash":"4cb1fe9c2f23e827cfe65137e29b2bdf9ec189af81cd7552c358da87cb9c462a"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"2b60c45840e14af3c85c7654b59d52fd1a0d9d04870fd80070765919a17ca139","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.121417Z","id":"46b66c438abc789d07535844e30bd174eae3d7c86b7b129d11516320ca728eba","body":{"detail":"launch.sh execs `ensure-clax.sh exec native-host`, which exports CLAX_CHANNEL=agent (scripts/ensure-clax.sh:123-127). Inherited harness variables are a second path: Chrome started from LaunchServices (Dock, Finder, `open`) gets launchd's environment and inherits none, but Chromium launched by Playwright inherits the test runner's environment (CLAUDECODE=1 when an agent runs the e2e suite), and on Linux a browser started by xdg-open from an agent's shell or a daemon the agent started inherits it too. See the blocker on crates/clax-cli/src/commands/native_host.rs:151:161.","kind":"comment","references":"b4bf1f08d4c561fd1512fcb8d8c99cf70ccc391bdbe1b4739980e5c82bfc1ad3","summary":"Pairing fails on every install, not only when Chrome inherited a harness variable: the launcher itself sets CLAX_CHANNEL=agent","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122092Z","id":"53fb2aa29244e7bbf63af637b5dbb4a290f786326c806723500aa7b221d50666","body":{"detail":"Names are unique only among live sessions (spec section 11), so when the owner's 'web' ends, a person's agent may PATCH its name to 'web' and the owner's next '@web' goes to it, moving the thread's untargeted rows with it (send_to_named). Until section 10's routing request lands, nothing tells the commenter. Task 14's routing request should name the person, and the thread answer could carry the reached agent's person.","kind":"comment","references":"4055a6f8cca3f3235a912b745deaa277c7a99ddfeee284a25843c847a4b1f21f","summary":"The answer to an @name does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:19.217929Z","id":"fe4cc7e23a1330d29919b8f6e59b7d3e4c976a34a1402dac6366eea1469f95e3","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"06daa4ae0ef0c442599343c9806d45c351cbd0676bbba21224ef6710a3447895"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.467773Z","id":"f51cf67b4248787c334981292ccc02f1a713d385f42bf2c2a532424de92c6660","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:868fdf4","summary":"Fixed in 868fdf4: native_host::pair mints through Client::owner_channel whatever its environment, and ensure-clax.sh exempts native-host. crates/clax-cli/tests/extension.rs the_installed_launcher_pairs_as_the_owner_under_a_harness_environment pairs through the installed launch.sh with CLAUDECODE=1 and CLAX_CHANNEL=agent (it fails with owner_channel removed); scripts/test-ensure-clax.sh checks the exemption; web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts 18 passed with CLAUDECODE=1 in the runner's environment. The remaining path (an owner's agent running clax native-host itself) is the waiver on crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:497:500.","supersedes":"b4bf1f08d4c561fd1512fcb8d8c99cf70ccc391bdbe1b4739980e5c82bfc1ad3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:22:00.597663Z","id":"fe25c4c98063afe51301915e4dbe71a0e7c16ceaa38e8180be6d4e4585356ed0","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1641},"end":{"line":1667},"content_hash":"83ed7864ba2897d0ff8421cfe185f069945dfbf2b21b7f774ccc58438abe14d5"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"bd6301a402ac7d7fbb6f04b75a0c875b289ee6167f0af811d68bd7d0b7a3260d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619473Z","id":"ac364ac2059f0ee2dc92654f01f42a4582499a29ea0a9740237baf8f9f6b1516","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools here gets no upgrade-hold probe (with_upgrade_hold is never called), so status over the daemon-served MCP endpoint never carries upgrade_held (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1285-1290). The shim, the CLI and Pi report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"bf718c5220791a2ab835891ca9f59556af6e625096c9dfa63042bde16d094a30"},"summary":"The daemon's own /mcp status does not report upgrade_held","supersedes":"883584b3ad6905461c2178a9d2f613cbafef211ee0535b8d509519da776a6fe0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619624Z","id":"7523c83deb06ab9dc479c839ba6f5915a6b82c8d8fe409beca1377e4b5c36645","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":382},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"3f206f41a6e6622d8ee312c392795dff19fa491a82e5981aba47e01580a9e799","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619748Z","id":"b06bed237f3b537af0f88836053b031be9043224da85365727412c2d8d40da46","body":{"detail":"for_asker() sets question.artifact.title to null for Caller::PersonAgent whatever its approvals: the title is an author field (spec §8.2) and no Visibility exists yet. The owner's GET /api/questions and GET /api/questions/{qid} leave out questions of sessions with a person (store questions.rs owners!()), but crate::inbox::views still renders them as items of the owner's inbox (spec §18 wants the per-person inbox).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"b532c1383250d597fa64b1cda0b14d94c3c2f0e35de1d852fec34ed13cc7ba69"},"suggested_fix":"Replace for_asker with the visibility filter when questions are filtered, and scope the inbox's question items per person (migration 25's per-person inbox).","summary":"A person's agent's question view nulls the artifact title instead of filtering it, and its questions still reach the owner's inbox","supersedes":"c20422c881c5477cc8c3cad8c4ba4fa548a42217e77edaa703fdb7ff38926c3d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619882Z","id":"3bf940526e34b0fd1a6e732658e8e653c02e63b14e87ad6a8e61b3a2a523aae3","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"07bc579aa3d6c39071fe1fc44810958f2c325dcf43dea3e4644ce9c84ea27758"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","supersedes":"c5595c22e7fafbf59719371cde3020e684786a794501fdcd325869c5c05fefb9","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620011Z","id":"2258489355e69e74bc84e69888fea096ddd7bb2991eb66052ea5779821cd4225","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"15860d8f518a31f559dec4b3f1bdef653fbc2027d4c55e5c6558d41250d245d2"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","supersedes":"4055a6f8cca3f3235a912b745deaa277c7a99ddfeee284a25843c847a4b1f21f","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620159Z","id":"21254c3d3f666f2683916104e51ddbe215c6824b70094076a923d921b746f355","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":452},"end":{"line":453},"content_hash":"951ad5f5efc1832ae06efe1d11fb5641065e27f2b7f937c01e21d4e7863a0c5a"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","supersedes":"12bc834768f3652b24d3ae4fe8e18ecc8ec1680362b55c2f079451833ce926f2","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620305Z","id":"279fa7ff6e009034cc996251bb6fd8b63fe261ce62e891fa50cfa33b9f314766","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1240},"end":{"line":1256},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"2da84c9808d4ea68fc9560c9f7826c6a6d78a134c253a5d73ebb8a01c9b716a2","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620433Z","id":"393bc16d1befd9c1564927c1d0e452f20355dd3f08e380683b67f6f63feb02d4","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"d2dc2d626b0b84978ec419e54713d3b4a62263bd38afcf8aebf3f3849cd7ff37"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"fe4cc7e23a1330d29919b8f6e59b7d3e4c976a34a1402dac6366eea1469f95e3","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620576Z","id":"7a293c3073fb3f9fd49db2b3318ddc28e337ebd14433cf0b6179ea4cc2a97256","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1601},"end":{"line":1627},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"fe25c4c98063afe51301915e4dbe71a0e7c16ceaa38e8180be6d4e4585356ed0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:16.069318Z","id":"7249e30bf73fb1bd9dc61ff481d29b95847aaeea45c663e2fbcc75e291f98d58","body":{"detail":"POST /api/sessions/{id}/tool-calls (here) and POST /api/sessions/{id}/tool-call-ids (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs:534:540) take DeniedToGrants and RequireToken, so a shim or Claude Code hook on another machine (a Clax-Grant caller) gets 403 forbidden when it reports a call. The events its requests make still carry the x-clax-call header's call (audit spec §5.2, amended 2026-10-10), so the call's name, argument hash and start time are kept; its end, outcome, produced list and harness call ID are not. Spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5 lists neither route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":385},"content_hash":"e662e3e5e230ae2bbd36b754c7184d915e95a24ff1b77f4ef25b95d367e16b3c"},"suggested_fix":"Declare both as Own agent routes (need!(…, None, Own, DEFAULT_LIMIT), agent::ROUTES, agent::ROUTE_NEEDS, a §7.5 row), record the call as the session's agent (its actor already carries grant_id and person), and drop a report's artifact_id that names an artifact the grant may not read or a live page, so the call never lands in a path the agent cannot see.","summary":"A person's agents' tool calls are never recorded as tool.call or tool.call_id: the report routes refuse grants","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:16.069391Z","id":"ae067b6726e53a0c7e9e580511bd9737ad86a0ed1b64ced57e21234c55ccd788","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"c999e8def53d154c4c3b3e4130701a6ba8fd9b6ed4134f44a7686b641ea38f24"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:16.069462Z","id":"a2b6e191dc6cac2d78641134026793ad76606da49673b52f97a1a6dbd3d09df3","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259372Z","id":"45e409e64fbce6a95683f139b5754353db2950da018ac45789b2009373d1cc66","body":{"detail":"LAN viewers are *unconnected authors (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person M14): their comment bodies and names in the export are the same untrusted input for the owner's agents on a single-owner install as a person's are, and the owner can withdraw the *unconnected approval. So: (1) now, admit the owner's agents (OwnerAgent) to GET /api/toolpath/export with no_text and no_names forced (refuse an agent request that asks for text or names with 403 not_for_agents naming the flags), since the redacted export holds hashes in place of free text and no names; (2) with Task 8, filter the export per reader as the visibility filter does elsewhere (per-field placeholders for authors the reader's person has not approved) and drop the forced redaction. PersonAgent stays refused (owner only, audit spec section 8.3).","kind":"comment","references":"ae067b6726e53a0c7e9e580511bd9737ad86a0ed1b64ced57e21234c55ccd788","summary":"Recommendation: refuse only while people exist is not enough; give owner agents the redacted export now and a per-reader filtered export with Task 8","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259392Z","id":"942acc31df151b72ed8dafeaf1bdadee059e299988c185df01dd39a0f580da63","body":{"detail":"Today a grant reaches no content route (POST /api/artifacts and the rest answer 503 not_yet for a Clax-Grant caller), so a person's agent's calls produce almost nothing; the call's name, hash and start time still ride each event's x-clax-call. Once Task 8 opens the content routes, a call with no tool.call loses its end, outcome, produced list and harness call ID. Land the suggested Own routes in the task that opens the first content route to grants, with the produced list scoped to the reporting session.","kind":"comment","references":"7249e30bf73fb1bd9dc61ff481d29b95847aaeea45c663e2fbcc75e291f98d58","summary":"Deferring is right for now, but this must land before a person's agents can reach routes that make events","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259409Z","id":"f42947cd08b22b1aa6769f583298015bc37b8e8578996a27b8d30419f97f897e","body":{"detail":"The watch.start is under the commenter's audit context with the agent's session, so who caused it is kept; what is missing is that @name, not the agent, asked. A mention cause (with the comment's ID) fits audit spec section 6.4 beside scope and move; it belongs with the @name routing work (thread.take cause mention, multi-person spec section 20.2).","kind":"comment","references":"a2b6e191dc6cac2d78641134026793ad76606da49673b52f97a1a6dbd3d09df3","summary":"Deferring is right: the watch is recorded with the right actor and session, only its cause is missing","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:50:05.979621Z","id":"d489b55ea13f9c96eb29d489ca65d2326ff27bc5fc4e603ca8502934e3bc27d2","body":{"detail":"for_asker() sets question.artifact.title to null for Caller::PersonAgent whatever its approvals: the title is an author field (spec §8.2) and no Visibility exists yet. The owner's GET /api/questions and GET /api/questions/{qid} leave out questions of sessions with a person (store questions.rs owners!()), but crate::inbox::views still renders them as items of the owner's inbox (spec §18 wants the per-person inbox).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"b532c1383250d597fa64b1cda0b14d94c3c2f0e35de1d852fec34ed13cc7ba69"},"suggested_fix":"Replace for_asker with the visibility filter when questions are filtered, and scope the inbox's question items per person (migration 25's per-person inbox).","summary":"A person's agent's question view nulls the artifact title instead of filtering it, and its questions still reach the owner's inbox","supersedes":"b06bed237f3b537af0f88836053b031be9043224da85365727412c2d8d40da46","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:44:32.567217Z","id":"64e893ef41776eb7b4107de37f382cb261e9c704943c32b6d53fa8338cda998e","body":{"detail":"Store::add_asset_by takes via_page and records every author of the page in page_authors (kind asset), as spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §8.2 now requires for a page's upload. web/shell/src/caps/assets.ts posts uploads with the owner token and no x-clax-via header, and this route calls add_asset (no person, no page), so the route cannot yet tell a page's upload from the owner agent's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"baf1d71bb6638c06f37c00b53a257bbfb740e5adb611ef23682e62241b5ab067"},"suggested_fix":"When the asset routes are filtered and opened to grants, have the shell send x-clax-via: page on a page's upload, pass the uploader's person and via_page to add_asset_by, and test that a carried script's upload counts its author.","summary":"The upload route never says a page uploads: an asset a page uploads through the shell's assets capability counts only its uploader, not the page's authors","tags":["visibility","revisit:when the asset routes are filtered per field","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.377983Z","id":"b08df854476dcd76ccd848fb3623777a63b666968abf1f47674c65db7a8e4399","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":255},"end":{"line":286},"content_hash":"15860d8f518a31f559dec4b3f1bdef653fbc2027d4c55e5c6558d41250d245d2"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","supersedes":"2258489355e69e74bc84e69888fea096ddd7bb2991eb66052ea5779821cd4225","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.378163Z","id":"eb546abc5a62240980c52734427a0101d3dc46b036fe942d8a9e7d723e346e67","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":293},"end":{"line":323},"content_hash":"d2dc2d626b0b84978ec419e54713d3b4a62263bd38afcf8aebf3f3849cd7ff37"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"393bc16d1befd9c1564927c1d0e452f20355dd3f08e380683b67f6f63feb02d4","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.378340Z","id":"558e23dbdb2b8b7105481fb6afe33cc9b5688c8bf56342997bab1a912c880dbb","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":317},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"a2b6e191dc6cac2d78641134026793ad76606da49673b52f97a1a6dbd3d09df3","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.378513Z","id":"9b9010123ca7e6e924509f811fb098834ffc13e5d6487efbfc841df4e17416ea","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":521},"end":{"line":521},"content_hash":"07bc579aa3d6c39071fe1fc44810958f2c325dcf43dea3e4644ce9c84ea27758"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","supersedes":"3bf940526e34b0fd1a6e732658e8e653c02e63b14e87ad6a8e61b3a2a523aae3","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:05:45.164663Z","id":"c2e7b7d5683f1da36e0ddeacb5c4ff1c7cab80d1b808bd83cf47b5fb9f5a4da1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b142bd6","summary":"Fixed: web/shell/src/caps/assets.ts sends x-clax-via: page on its uploads and deletes, and the upload route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs upload) reads it and calls add_asset_by with via_page (and a person's agent's person). Evidence: api_assets::a_pages_upload_carries_every_author_of_the_page passes at b142bd6 (Mia's carried app.js page uploads from the owner's browser; the upload's authors are [Owner, Mia]) and fails with via_page forced false; web/shell/src/audit-headers.test.ts now requires the marker in caps/assets.ts; cargo nextest run --workspace at b142bd6, 1902 passed.","supersedes":"64e893ef41776eb7b4107de37f382cb261e9c704943c32b6d53fa8338cda998e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:56:33.606769Z","id":"f289f0be001d302174789179713a9e3eb684658a5cb5712238dc5c279313d746","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"951ad5f5efc1832ae06efe1d11fb5641065e27f2b7f937c01e21d4e7863a0c5a"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","supersedes":"21254c3d3f666f2683916104e51ddbe215c6824b70094076a923d921b746f355","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:56:33.607057Z","id":"c94ac7b090adff41694497c19c9fa47b656021ac6da7861c94a44b90af34ba4d","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":528},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"07bc579aa3d6c39071fe1fc44810958f2c325dcf43dea3e4644ce9c84ea27758"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","supersedes":"9b9010123ca7e6e924509f811fb098834ffc13e5d6487efbfc841df4e17416ea","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.887432Z","id":"61730b017f4030268779c7cff9a14a33502627ea777c02990bf7a247ac4e801d","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1603},"end":{"line":1629},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"7a293c3073fb3f9fd49db2b3318ddc28e337ebd14433cf0b6179ea4cc2a97256","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.887660Z","id":"0c7982f6a670711eace6832cc0ec7fd8e9bc5a8967d0ac1bddd1b5bc8187e4f8","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"15860d8f518a31f559dec4b3f1bdef653fbc2027d4c55e5c6558d41250d245d2"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","supersedes":"b08df854476dcd76ccd848fb3623777a63b666968abf1f47674c65db7a8e4399","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.887871Z","id":"ac68e05355cdc2528cf943fc1073385e7939276d054eb7a1993570148bb786a5","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":359},"end":{"line":389},"content_hash":"d2dc2d626b0b84978ec419e54713d3b4a62263bd38afcf8aebf3f3849cd7ff37"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"eb546abc5a62240980c52734427a0101d3dc46b036fe942d8a9e7d723e346e67","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.888075Z","id":"d1de8dd975d3d652fd72c847ada41c9d12056d2ef010bde386c1ddc318380282","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":383},"end":{"line":383},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"558e23dbdb2b8b7105481fb6afe33cc9b5688c8bf56342997bab1a912c880dbb","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.888282Z","id":"591b42b8e96be7d14bfd583fa75f6fa9f613e65ddcf089e8c17ff793dc7f7d91","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":276},"end":{"line":283},"content_hash":"c999e8def53d154c4c3b3e4130701a6ba8fd9b6ed4134f44a7686b641ea38f24"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"ae067b6726e53a0c7e9e580511bd9737ad86a0ed1b64ced57e21234c55ccd788","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889101Z","id":"30bee48d2ef635937fc4b1dfdfdf2ae6f7f2d6daed8c1256c276101255825fe6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9bf6584","summary":"viewer::author and viewer::acting_viewer take a Clax-Grant caller's person (viewer_of_grant), so its threads, viewer comments and sessionless resolves are its person's. Tests: api_visibility::write_routes_return_filtered_threads, a_persons_agent_comments_from_a_session_as_its_person and an_agents_resolve_is_its_persons pass.","supersedes":"c94ac7b090adff41694497c19c9fa47b656021ac6da7861c94a44b90af34ba4d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889269Z","id":"bd14e212073764b2880333f235d0d9b34841a6f3457a14c04c5490db5c4ac707","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d2c9f13","summary":"POST /api/sessions/{id}/tool-calls and /tool-call-ids take TokenOrAgent with Own needs (agent::ToolCallReport, ToolCallIdReport), produced scoped per 3c67161a. Test: api_visibility::a_persons_agent_reports_its_own_tool_calls passes.","supersedes":"7249e30bf73fb1bd9dc61ff481d29b95847aaeea45c663e2fbcc75e291f98d58","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T21:18:23.621133Z","id":"12e6d1ad009a3d3a3de386377581cabf702b2ee31e98a7a62beb80ec053cce0d","body":{"detail":"Failure: once Tasks 10 and 11 open these routes to grants, Sam's agent sends x-clax-via: page and its write is recorded as a page's (page_authors, by_page, doc page authors) though no browser ran a page. The comment routes already refuse via_page from a person's agent (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:119, 400 invalid_via_page); the header is also read at crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:571 and :665 and crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs:182. These routes answer person's agents 503 not_yet today, so nothing is reachable yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"75b0c344ed3bac9496f9e768ab58dd17e15aa1827a082583f9329fa7c775a121"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse x-clax-via: page from a PersonAgent (400 invalid_via_page) on every route that reads it, in the task that adds each to FILTERED_LIVE, with a test per route.","summary":"x-clax-via: page is honoured for a person's agent on uploads, documents and artifact writes","tags":["review","people","depends:task-10","depends:task-11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T21:33:56.538338Z","id":"899a94656117198f40ed20f00c19cbf0a8d2210cab96f5a95c4e9c20c12b6f07","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"15860d8f518a31f559dec4b3f1bdef653fbc2027d4c55e5c6558d41250d245d2"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","supersedes":"0c7982f6a670711eace6832cc0ec7fd8e9bc5a8967d0ac1bddd1b5bc8187e4f8","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T21:33:56.538622Z","id":"25a8d9870bd87fb31c187ad10c4be2151855c4690e881c7adeb30c214567e848","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":364},"end":{"line":394},"content_hash":"d2dc2d626b0b84978ec419e54713d3b4a62263bd38afcf8aebf3f3849cd7ff37"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"ac68e05355cdc2528cf943fc1073385e7939276d054eb7a1993570148bb786a5","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T21:33:56.538835Z","id":"8c032571fb63f438e87e7a2a5bd246327747427c682854ef1db5568d4b3ef810","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":388},"end":{"line":388},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"d1de8dd975d3d652fd72c847ada41c9d12056d2ef010bde386c1ddc318380282","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:14:39.268316Z","id":"ac9d6db6b4a11dd2d1991ecea224f3a0f9bae714934d56fc42ac326754654f64","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbb6943","summary":"Fixed: agent::page_marker (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs) answers x-clax-via: page from a PersonAgent 400 invalid_via_page on asset upload, PATCH and publish, and CallerParts (crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs:171) refuses it for every docs route. Evidence: api_visibility::a_persons_agent_writes_artifacts_from_a_session_and_never_as_a_page passes (PATCH, publish and upload with the marker are 400 invalid_via_page, nothing written); making page_marker honour the marker fails it. The docs routes' test is Task 11's, recorded on db_caller.rs.","supersedes":"12e6d1ad009a3d3a3de386377581cabf702b2ee31e98a7a62beb80ec053cce0d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:14:39.268607Z","id":"4b39168898e9f4253128ffb11b166cbbb255c0302008c19c6e3001721ffde948","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent, with artifacts update at Mia's artifact, publishes a version that puts or removes a guessed name: when the name is one of Mia's withheld files, the new version's files_withheld drops by one; and a put of '<name>/x' collides with a withheld file '<name>' and is refused naming the path (check_collisions, crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1061). Reads, the file content route and thread creation answer withheld and missing names alike; this write path does not. It needs the update right, and a hit replaces or removes the file (visible to people). Options: accept (update means writing over another's files, and files_withheld is a count the spec gives), or answer collisions with withheld paths as invalid_path without the name and count carried-over withheld files without revealing replaced ones.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":693},"end":{"line":721},"content_hash":"6cfca5f0a34619515b63a9a1037ef24d37ea3d87a9c2638e70e00da1eb83218d"},"summary":"A person's agent that may update an artifact can learn whether a guessed file name is among the files withheld from it","tags":["visibility","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:14:39.268653Z","id":"0bc541586df7ede6fd9199a5698850c327ab8e529fedce07a717f7b5727bb20d","body":{"detail":"publish skips Store::retarget_untargeted for a grant's session, so the owner's agents' untargeted feedback on an artifact a person's agent publishes to does not move to that agent's session. PUT /api/sessions/{id}/watches/{aid} still retargets for a person's agent (routes/watches.rs), and spec M23 has the first session to take a delivery own an untargeted send. Task 12 decides for both, so they agree: retarget only rows the session may see, or never for a person's agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":721},"end":{"line":747},"content_hash":"0bf13ee01b959f3cfabbb2cc4037111fc41bbc3f728ff4f32d9455f4e1331be5"},"summary":"A person's agent's publish leaves untargeted feedback untargeted; a watch PUT of a person's agent still retargets it","tags":["people","depends:task-12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.538941Z","id":"b2ca0c8e2ef0835aedc6200c055a86ca5841591e72b9b992949bcc561774ce0f","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1250},"end":{"line":1266},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"279fa7ff6e009034cc996251bb6fd8b63fe261ce62e891fa50cfa33b9f314766","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.539201Z","id":"5990a9fedfde3eae0ffab87bf7dbc2edc1bd151b1e76b36b3a4db40bf7228a9e","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1613},"end":{"line":1639},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"61730b017f4030268779c7cff9a14a33502627ea777c02990bf7a247ac4e801d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.539454Z","id":"158d289f59d3b212795709c11a09a674bea149b7031c70016ac9e86dc48589f8","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"15860d8f518a31f559dec4b3f1bdef653fbc2027d4c55e5c6558d41250d245d2"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","supersedes":"899a94656117198f40ed20f00c19cbf0a8d2210cab96f5a95c4e9c20c12b6f07","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.539701Z","id":"4667761c02fddf70795619b3d6c3206ed723176c5827bf886d70264044b0c970","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":349},"end":{"line":379},"content_hash":"d2dc2d626b0b84978ec419e54713d3b4a62263bd38afcf8aebf3f3849cd7ff37"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"25a8d9870bd87fb31c187ad10c4be2151855c4690e881c7adeb30c214567e848","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.539940Z","id":"d5f9dc75105801ccd27825e740ebc9f7388320d7aa4eeff545c9e47d2342da98","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"8c032571fb63f438e87e7a2a5bd246327747427c682854ef1db5568d4b3ef810","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:32:57.060600Z","id":"6f3daa793444c4596d0fdb17b4c02e367bc7932bf5abcc082efbf025b8e36d88","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent with clax:full sends DELETE /api/artifacts/{aid}/assets/{id} and DELETE /api/artifacts/{aid} with no X-Clax-Session: both answer 204 and the artifact or asset is gone. Create, PATCH, publish, upload (agent::person_agent_session, whose doc says a person's agent writes artifacts, versions and assets only from a session) and thread delete (§7.5) answer 400 no_session; §6.7 lists no remote delete command. The delete handlers (here and crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs:130-143) never call person_agent_session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":662},"content_hash":"3be61a83cd6af2c1de9e48d4a03dc56584df4d2d4e5198bf2a8c9ba1e8bf347b"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether a sessionless person's agent may delete; if not, call agent::person_agent_session in both delete handlers, say so in the §7.5 rows, and test both.","summary":"A person's agent deletes artifacts and assets without a session, unlike every other artifact write and thread delete","tags":["review","visibility","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:32:57.060631Z","id":"7c9e5b8ef65ba0514029fb211a94f25750f96a65f056bda0db79d4093d36c089","body":{"detail":"Probe (Sam's agent, clax:full, on an artifact Mia's agent published with MIAXname.js and MIAXdir/MIAXnested.css, all withheld from Sam): each publish carries if_version 1, index.html, one extra path and addresses [\"01JZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZ\"] (no such thread). Put 'miaxname.js' answers 400 invalid_path 'two paths differ only by letter case'; put 'MIAXname.js/x' answers 400 \"'miaxname.js' is both a file and a directory\"; put 'MIAXdir' answers 400 \"'miaxdir' is both a file and a directory\"; each guess that misses answers 400 unknown_thread; the artifact stays at version 1 throughout. check_collisions (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:702-722, called at :1061) runs before the transaction and link_version's unknown_thread rolls a miss back, so the oracle is free, silent and repeatable, and finds withheld directory names too. The remove variant does write: removing a guessed 'zzz.js' leaves files_withheld at 2, removing 'MIAXname.js' drops it to 1, each in a new version credited to Sam.","kind":"comment","references":"4b39168898e9f4253128ffb11b166cbbb255c0302008c19c6e3001721ffde948","summary":"The collision variant needs neither a write nor a hit's destruction, and it confirms names case-insensitively and by directory","tags":["review","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:51:37.714199Z","id":"9138b2f08206bf16babbbc8f537dda405632264cba03174406ebc70e4fe3d351","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e056b7","summary":"Fixed, on the coordinator's ruling that a person's agent deletes from a session as it writes (for consistency with create, PATCH, publish, upload and thread delete): artifacts::delete and assets::delete call agent::person_agent_session (400 no_session); spec §7.5's DELETE rows say so. Evidence: api_visibility::a_persons_agent_writes_artifacts_from_a_session_and_never_as_a_page passes (sessionless DELETE of an asset and of the artifact answer 400 no_session, both remain); removing the call from assets::delete fails it.","supersedes":"6f3daa793444c4596d0fdb17b4c02e367bc7932bf5abcc082efbf025b8e36d88","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:51:37.714489Z","id":"edf514a4b872d42f6eb83ba9aadbd526d4426979ab8a8816d43d5589a50dd4fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e056b7","summary":"Fixed, on the coordinator's ruling following the review (reply 7c9e5b8e): the silent collision path is closed and the destructive path accepted. Paths of the previous version the publisher's reader may not see never constrain a publish: a put colliding with one (letter case, a file beneath it, a file over its directory) drops it as a remove would (ValidatedPublish::hidden, filled in routes/artifacts.rs publish; collide() in crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs), so a hit and a miss take the same path. Replacing or removing a withheld file still lowers files_withheld, a visible, destructive version credited to the person, which spec §21.7 now states. Evidence: api_visibility::a_publish_never_tells_whether_a_guessed_name_is_withheld (identical answers for case, file-under and file-over hits and misses) and store::artifacts::tests::a_put_over_a_hidden_path_drops_it_where_a_visible_one_is_refused pass; not filling hidden fails the first.","supersedes":"4b39168898e9f4253128ffb11b166cbbb255c0302008c19c6e3001721ffde948","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:52:02.688169Z","id":"9744a16f1dde8c2c4e7cf8fcd751eb5e989e2cda71c968bbe73151d2b9c4f2ee","body":{"detail":"publish skips Store::retarget_untargeted for a grant's session, so the owner's agents' untargeted feedback on an artifact a person's agent publishes to does not move to that agent's session (tested: api_visibility::a_persons_agents_publish_leaves_untargeted_feedback_untargeted). PUT /api/sessions/{id}/watches/{aid} still retargets for a person's agent (routes/watches.rs), and spec M23 has the first session to take a delivery own an untargeted send. Task 12 decides for both, so they agree: retarget only rows the session may see, or never for a person's agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":728},"end":{"line":763},"content_hash":"9773f43dfde0f1de10067893d619b3008aae740a3fbfe526195c995090450e72"},"summary":"A person's agent's publish leaves untargeted feedback untargeted; a watch PUT of a person's agent still retargets it","supersedes":"0bc541586df7ede6fd9199a5698850c327ab8e529fedce07a717f7b5727bb20d","tags":["people","depends:task-12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T23:45:17.865664Z","id":"fa2db4fe5e108ea3f1328dfc97872e65757d5b899212682bf341bd1944657ee8","body":{"detail":"announce publishes Event::Doc {artifact_id, path, version} for every change, whoever may see the document. /api/events and /api/stream* are Denied (not_for_agents for the owner's agents, 403 for a person's agent), and the shell's db onSnapshot runs in a browser, which §8.5 leaves unfiltered, so no agent channel receives it now. If Task 12 lets any agent channel (feedback tiers, notices, Claude Code's channel, Pi) relay doc events, a withheld document's path and version would reach the agent; spec §8.3 lists withheld paths as never listed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"f6755ddf74053f12298e6babea666114650bbe6b049011284e6a98c093cdbe91"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 12, keep doc events off every agent channel, or filter each by the document's authors (doc_authors) for the channel's reader before relaying it, with a canary-sweep case that writes Mia's document while the agent waits.","summary":"Each doc event names the changed path, a withheld document's included; only people's channels carry it today","tags":["people","depends:task-12","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T00:52:12.706009Z","id":"6f8b39ea8d214104964c56e7aa3075c10d4cd9847a0e26385810c63dbf151ac5","body":{"detail":"announce publishes Event::Doc {artifact_id, path, version} for every change, whoever may see the document. /api/events and /api/stream* are Denied (not_for_agents for the owner's agents, 403 for a person's agent), and the shell's db onSnapshot runs in a browser, which §8.5 leaves unfiltered, so no agent channel receives it now. If Task 12 lets any agent channel (feedback tiers, notices, Claude Code's channel, Pi) relay doc events, a withheld document's path and version would reach the agent; spec §8.3 lists withheld paths as never listed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"f6755ddf74053f12298e6babea666114650bbe6b049011284e6a98c093cdbe91"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 12, keep doc events off every agent channel, or filter each by the document's authors (doc_authors) for the channel's reader before relaying it, with a canary-sweep case that writes Mia's document while the agent waits.","summary":"Each doc event names the changed path, a withheld document's included; only people's channels carry it today","supersedes":"fa2db4fe5e108ea3f1328dfc97872e65757d5b899212682bf341bd1944657ee8","tags":["people","depends:task-12","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.794237Z","id":"a3ced6c11417e2e03a7dfec357bc4ae5f3dc1dc7b69ff515e1cdf27e2bea9165","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 asks every Filtered handler to pass its response through vis.filter_. feedback::poll and feedback::notices hand over what Store::take_feedback_readable and Store::take_notices built under the session's Visibility; the guard now accepts either call by name. clax-core's delivery guard (feedback.rs feedback_items_are_built_only_under_visibility) checks that every FeedbackItem and Notice is built inside a function taking a Visibility. Amend §8.6's wording, or route the takes through a Vis method, if the spec text is to stay literal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1704},"end":{"line":1716},"content_hash":"402a2958e1b63e07626784004c364e318df4e018aaef33fbfd9efac8a19b41cb"},"summary":"The Filtered-route guard accepts a filtered store take in place of vis.filter_ for the feedback and notices polls","tags":["people","spec:8.6","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.795476Z","id":"7f48e93ff616edf4a0b17a3bba84d8ae82a057cb38346010a59d9452019fb767","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ccb76c","summary":"Fixed: a person's agent's watch PUT now leaves the owner's agents' untargeted feedback untargeted, as its publish does (routes/watches.rs put, retarget only without a grant); a person's agent receives a thread when it is sent to it (spec §10). Test: api_visibility::a_persons_agent_gets_placeholders_and_never_takes_untargeted_feedback_by_watching passes, and fails with the retarget forced.","supersedes":"9744a16f1dde8c2c4e7cf8fcd751eb5e989e2cda71c968bbe73151d2b9c4f2ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.795733Z","id":"c161c6c1c459aa7faf54dbbe5efae8f14eb2622ba32daef54fe781f136bbd496","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ccb76c","summary":"Doc events stay off every agent channel: no feedback tier, notice, hook, shim or Pi path relays events, and /api/events and /api/stream refuse the owner's agents (not_for_agents) and a person's agent (403). Test: api_visibility::no_doc_event_reaches_a_waiting_agent writes Mia's document while the owner's agent waits in wait_for_feedback and finds neither its path nor its field in the answer.","supersedes":"6f8b39ea8d214104964c56e7aa3075c10d4cd9847a0e26385810c63dbf151ac5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.167292Z","id":"d767378147ee975f0f44c69dd12c6028b580e2cb050adb4ef130830d955242cf","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":391},"end":{"line":393},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"7523c83deb06ab9dc479c839ba6f5915a6b82c8d8fe409beca1377e4b5c36645","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.167606Z","id":"ae07eb4c0413f61b77025716e9bee8040a0c52fb3a7ce2524b6c3d0519955cbe","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1264},"end":{"line":1280},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"b2ca0c8e2ef0835aedc6200c055a86ca5841591e72b9b992949bcc561774ce0f","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.167910Z","id":"6c16dc1190d502fef4d6bf7cd29882c899362d4dbf569dbf36b0c7561867592d","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1627},"end":{"line":1653},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"5990a9fedfde3eae0ffab87bf7dbc2edc1bd151b1e76b36b3a4db40bf7228a9e","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:01.627016Z","id":"04982e94ceb81c6d8970bde018946972faeb04d01422b2babcca94b2242bc925","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dfc9b9a","summary":"Spec §8.6 now names the filtered store takes (Store::take_feedback_readable, Store::take_notices) as the feedback routes' filter, so the guard's widening matches the spec; the delivery guard also covers Placeholder and refuses Visibility::all() in non-test code (clax-core feedback.rs feedback_items_are_built_only_under_visibility passes).","supersedes":"a3ced6c11417e2e03a7dfec357bc4ae5f3dc1dc7b69ff515e1cdf27e2bea9165","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.075944Z","id":"39c7d396556271d0eeb58f5b54add89836682cd51c35567c091290bba8f01eab","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1300},"end":{"line":1316},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"ae07eb4c0413f61b77025716e9bee8040a0c52fb3a7ce2524b6c3d0519955cbe","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.076282Z","id":"d9d9a5c03ed9fe2dde004b67b517eb542a08f7b78fe3dd0f07348635dd251f1b","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1663},"end":{"line":1689},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"6c16dc1190d502fef4d6bf7cd29882c899362d4dbf569dbf36b0c7561867592d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.076581Z","id":"a019511b518cb16829fabb974b5c002d966efa2762ae6422ce17c7c67342702c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aabf45f","summary":"Fixed: an agent's question view filters the artifact title through its Visibility (Vis::filter_question, routes/questions.rs for_asker), and a person's agent's question is an item of that person's inbox only (clax-core inbox::note_question). Passing: api_questions::a_persons_agent_sees_its_questions_title_once_its_person_approves_the_author, store::inbox::tests::items_go_to_their_recipient, api_inbox::a_person_sees_only_their_inbox.","supersedes":"d489b55ea13f9c96eb29d489ca65d2326ff27bc5fc4e603ca8502934e3bc27d2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.110689Z","id":"f0f3481a334f47de7c9c4988a4ed5b5d53bc27709a23f23c6e55d1ff42463e69","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":404},"end":{"line":406},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"d767378147ee975f0f44c69dd12c6028b580e2cb050adb4ef130830d955242cf","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.111102Z","id":"85047e9dda3555b841102f4042fb78ba711ee3550a767d62910ecf759189cf18","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1321},"end":{"line":1337},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"39c7d396556271d0eeb58f5b54add89836682cd51c35567c091290bba8f01eab","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.111505Z","id":"a9bbf76684f4e42805888342d546d1631df1acf28cc3d7283ee40f0b56b7e5a3","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1698},"end":{"line":1724},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"d9d9a5c03ed9fe2dde004b67b517eb542a08f7b78fe3dd0f07348635dd251f1b","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.111928Z","id":"de5b2c0629cceb850f9e3f5828a266df5556d221d54f4f3f11a9f04229ced5e1","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":433},"end":{"line":433},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"d5f9dc75105801ccd27825e740ebc9f7388320d7aa4eeff545c9e47d2342da98","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.114019Z","id":"811a60c86d57be605eca88b08c8f0d5e22454b1bd83b1c9e7385e5a150893391","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":412},"end":{"line":447},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"4667761c02fddf70795619b3d6c3206ed723176c5827bf886d70264044b0c970","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.114342Z","id":"fc63ed11fc201726ffc19961b2c0e1c41d19168a92a0efe7e3f96b8c38d5a61a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bba24eb","summary":"@name to a person's agent now makes the routing request (send_to_named routes through approvals::route_in) and @name or to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read before anything is written: api_approvals::naming_another_persons_agent_makes_a_request, api_approvals::a_send_to_an_agent_that_cannot_read_is_refused and api_threads::at_name_reaches_a_persons_agent_only_where_its_rights_allow pass.","supersedes":"158d289f59d3b212795709c11a09a674bea149b7031c70016ac9e86dc48589f8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.115901Z","id":"028e2091f749c304a8a266246591ac9dd93cbad5feb071cac4be25c079997eb8","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.2 gives ask's result status as approved, declined or open. A request can also be withdrawn (its thread resolved or deleted, its artifact deleted, the asking session ended, a person revoked), and the poll then returns status withdrawn rather than waiting out its time on a request no one can decide. The MCP ask (plan Task 19) should say so to the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":407},"end":{"line":412},"content_hash":"d24b959a857d61f7159814522aca62e4b5a8621517080c32c17ca9c180ba5f4c"},"summary":"The ask poll answers status withdrawn, which spec §9.2 does not list","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:05:16.919223Z","id":"ccd70d956fd4b22cac0000b4fff275ff0377c6c2079210a80a7cea37981c3501","body":{"detail":"GET /api/approvals/requests (and the ask poll's `request`) serve every request of the agent's person, so an agent narrowed away from an artifact still learns its ID, its threads' IDs, the authors' names and how many comments wait there (scratch probe against 2f10f67: a narrowed agent of Sam's listed the request for an artifact it may not read). Spec §7.5 says Own, the person's own requests, so this matches the text; no content leaks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"8a4bd0bf1fef1b750435d753ee29378a577c3ce14c3c1461cae43e6ed0374d7e"},"suggested_fix":"For an agent caller, list only requests at artifacts its effective rights allow it to read, or record a ruling that Own includes them.","summary":"An agent's request list is not narrowed by its own rights: it names artifacts and threads its narrowing excludes","tags":["review","people","spec:7.5","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.244534Z","id":"a9d11ae87a0598c4441bb9f4022a6245ae1789b8e54cfda09df9ecc58b86a578","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.2 gives ask's result status as approved, declined or open. A request can also be withdrawn (its thread resolved or deleted, its artifact deleted, the asking session ended, a person revoked), and the poll then returns status withdrawn rather than waiting out its time on a request no one can decide. The MCP ask (plan Task 19) should say so to the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":441},"content_hash":"75fb306564fcdecdeb3200d8a59920b83f2f0ba73a7dd2769d7dccf7dfce9aed"},"summary":"The ask poll answers status withdrawn, which spec §9.2 does not list","supersedes":"028e2091f749c304a8a266246591ac9dd93cbad5feb071cac4be25c079997eb8","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.245259Z","id":"b6b42767217a0cd34bf4855d947b6d6f2be543c32ea0d085d42e4e3c5550af5b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e08870b","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator (not the owner): a person's agent's GET /api/approvals, GET /api/approvals/requests and its poll leave out requests and approvals about artifacts its read rights exclude, stricter than §7.5's Own as first written; §7.5 amended. api_approvals::an_agents_lists_leave_out_artifacts_it_may_not_read passes.","supersedes":"ccd70d956fd4b22cac0000b4fff275ff0377c6c2079210a80a7cea37981c3501","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:41.797441Z","id":"50045297a38762912e5f743d02a189e249ae0fa2ea94b13cc1254120d9d8a33f","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":408},"end":{"line":410},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"f0f3481a334f47de7c9c4988a4ed5b5d53bc27709a23f23c6e55d1ff42463e69","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:41.797889Z","id":"c67b5bc4757a91893f0b8b973f32eed50874ce7b21c3cefd74549962a5517641","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1326},"end":{"line":1342},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"85047e9dda3555b841102f4042fb78ba711ee3550a767d62910ecf759189cf18","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:41.798318Z","id":"24d296e37fef35ef0264fb63026fa153e036a5dd53395cbeb61449e373e3ac6d","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1709},"end":{"line":1735},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"a9bbf76684f4e42805888342d546d1631df1acf28cc3d7283ee40f0b56b7e5a3","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.885298Z","id":"6d102df2119fc73dc639b69fe8eaaa9eda560bacd04677cefcf253e65dfa47a2","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":409},"end":{"line":411},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"50045297a38762912e5f743d02a189e249ae0fa2ea94b13cc1254120d9d8a33f","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.885840Z","id":"066946b69a3b274803f983ed8afbf11f0f0236079c547baf5a194a340669c975","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1328},"end":{"line":1344},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"c67b5bc4757a91893f0b8b973f32eed50874ce7b21c3cefd74549962a5517641","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.886399Z","id":"920bb4618905222b85e3fd9dcbdbf5c975205ed4c21089951f850f351f6c7ec1","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1712},"end":{"line":1738},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"24d296e37fef35ef0264fb63026fa153e036a5dd53395cbeb61449e373e3ac6d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.819581Z","id":"a85b57f21058a1916e2cbc245683920df85e69bc3e8f528027a360bc8254ec1d","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":430},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"6d102df2119fc73dc639b69fe8eaaa9eda560bacd04677cefcf253e65dfa47a2","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.820200Z","id":"b3768606271bd380607bf3197a84556cee7a55c281de3d08307c56d8729ef074","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1356},"end":{"line":1372},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"066946b69a3b274803f983ed8afbf11f0f0236079c547baf5a194a340669c975","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.820808Z","id":"83e5a82d7f4de9122c0b162e16fdb3617319f1892487120904e36d6ebb8f4fea","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1751},"end":{"line":1777},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"920bb4618905222b85e3fd9dcbdbf5c975205ed4c21089951f850f351f6c7ec1","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:31.923284Z","id":"3e216908110497b8d1c0da1ba07b65afbf37e816ebe74190633529dd99bbe00d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bc65306f1ff4cad943f3cf43ebf3917faf1f9980f6ab900fd96b57c5abfdf894","summary":"Since 3808ae28 the names this route serves the owner's agents are marked: a viewer who is neither the owner nor a person reads '<name> (not connected)' (spec §9.6; api_people::unconnected_authors_are_marked_not_connected). Whether the owner's agents should reach the search at all is unchanged.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:42.612161Z","id":"52dfbde6b019fe6a5ee6066932f9afa8c15f394339d29cb476138147b7611250","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"fdef32ef55ec060aeebfe4fd3b77d7814bf6706887dea024f0f20ef0a60067d3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"bc65306f1ff4cad943f3cf43ebf3917faf1f9980f6ab900fd96b57c5abfdf894","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:45:13.519775Z","id":"3bb28d4470be474104ee0f0c4ee7138a537e1f05f92c973bf364c6140bd43795","body":{"detail":"lookup reads the file's bytes through ContentStore::read_file (Vec<u8>) inside store_call, and file/raw_file answer Body::from(bytes) (lines 262, 337); before ContentStore they opened the file with tokio::fs and streamed it. Responses are the same, but each request holds the whole file in memory and spends a store worker on the read. A streaming read on the interface (a body or chunk stream per backend) would restore streaming natively.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"89998f6c91d500b5e7c4179a2bfd07c06999233114010e709788cdbe09660e3e"},"summary":"Version files are read whole into memory on a store worker before they are served, where they were streamed from disk","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:45:13.519864Z","id":"af94e07800d1cc3c93fa922ba5a5ffb02ad1a77d6ee2d272859b88f34159b86e","body":{"detail":"blob calls Store::read_asset inside store_call and answers Body::from(bytes); before ContentStore it streamed the file with tokio::fs. Same response, more memory per request and a store worker held for the read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"138eb76d6d5a1aeda24ae626655bea56a2700bb7f81d9f9cba865a13023da601"},"summary":"An asset's bytes (up to MAX_ASSET_BYTES, 20 MiB) are read whole on a store worker before /_blob serves them","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.606180Z","id":"0fa30e43333d659b2e5cf92e931c72070182060ae5f8e545eaea15f03b2a6725","body":{"detail":"Before ContentStore the route looked up the row, ran sees.check, then opened the file. Now Store::read_asset reads up to MAX_ASSET_BYTES (20 MiB) inside the store call and the visibility check runs after, so a refused caller costs a whole read before its 404, and that 404's timing differs more from a missing asset's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"d581931ef3815d1ec71ed194b3d3c4e5e3dbb2693422244e27381e147e3eb47e"},"suggested_fix":"Look up the row (get_asset), check, then read the bytes; or check inside the store call.","summary":"/_blob reads the asset's bytes before checking that the caller may see live pages","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.606362Z","id":"5c69ea3174b4aea0b9690c0696b567919d6871a27dae094d40225d10894d26ed","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3bb28d4470be474104ee0f0c4ee7138a537e1f05f92c973bf364c6140bd43795","summary":"The memory is held per response, not per store worker: the Vec lives until the client has received the body, so N slow clients hold N files of up to MAX_FILE_BYTES (16 MiB, publish.rs:9) at once, where ReaderStream held one buffer each. A hosted backend has the same need (a Worker isolate's memory is small), so a streaming read (a body stream, with read_file as its default) suits both backends.","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:03:27.819313Z","id":"8ee38b360bf19e99e46899124a6c3b2686db0694aa2f042db5e104aec88ac59d","body":{"detail":"The shell's PresenceReporter (web/shell/src/view/presence-reporter.ts) keeps sending PUT /api/viewers/me/presence while the view is a spectator. The report only touches a seat the viewer holds, but it still lists the spectator in the artifact's presence (clax_core::presence::MAX_PEOPLE is 64), which seated people's top bar shows as chips. Spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.3 shows chips for seated people and counts everyone else in a viewing number; the native top bar has no viewing count yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"c5c18b401eea4dca6aaca642f192064643cfb079b780288048732677e3502566"},"suggested_fix":"Stop presence reports while spectating (the snapshot's viewing count already counts the spectator), and show the snapshot's or a stream's viewing count beside the chips.","summary":"Spectators keep reporting presence, so seated people see them as here and an artifact past 64 viewers answers 429 limit_reached","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.277231Z","id":"279de868104645c25af8c10a992b7af382111eb70730552646800f167c7749c9","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":430},"end":{"line":432},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"a85b57f21058a1916e2cbc245683920df85e69bc3e8f528027a360bc8254ec1d","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.278916Z","id":"4dbe625b0ce9a7e2fa46b1894376359738f584f62f4d32f23d9c7ff02ac8aea2","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1359},"end":{"line":1375},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"b3768606271bd380607bf3197a84556cee7a55c281de3d08307c56d8729ef074","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.280449Z","id":"14a489a4f6b9e9e07b9c4fe4c26f81dc80ed918c7e123db26ff2a8c64359bbdc","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1754},"end":{"line":1780},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"83e5a82d7f4de9122c0b162e16fdb3617319f1892487120904e36d6ebb8f4fea","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.282011Z","id":"e0f2887128d6142f7c20ca14994e36b73e728e3d1fe985794e297b2c67af76b9","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":417},"end":{"line":452},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"811a60c86d57be605eca88b08c8f0d5e22454b1bd83b1c9e7385e5a150893391","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.283493Z","id":"1898978522d1096c3958c0340b6f777e2f2d26163ad535ac6ce86cc7bd58b140","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"de5b2c0629cceb850f9e3f5828a266df5556d221d54f4f3f11a9f04229ced5e1","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.010443Z","id":"08120a521c065b61aa402b023e773a8284009d9314146533447a067f3583f317","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8ee38b360bf19e99e46899124a6c3b2686db0694aa2f042db5e104aec88ac59d","summary":"Decided by the owner's requirement for live seats: \"the degraded users are read only and get a perhaps delayed cached version\". Spectators are not shown as here to seated people: presence lists seated people, and the top bar counts everyone viewing (\"N viewing\").","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.010502Z","id":"e4bc14a39e3f6417e6e31c7dcccc3cd11e52d1893fa5965f4217966890934f93","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e266dc6d","summary":"Fixed in ae98d606, e266dc6d and 5cfb8765. A spectator's PUT /api/viewers/me/presence is not listed, drops a listing made while they were unnamed or seated (Presence::leave), and counts them as viewing; GET and PUT presence answer viewing; the top bar shows 'N viewing' once more than one is viewing (web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte). Evidence: cargo test api_seats::spectators_are_counted_as_viewing_and_never_listed_as_here ok; web/e2e/seats.spec.ts passes with the spectator's top bar reading '2 viewing' and one chip; screenshots at 1280 and 390, light and dark, show the count beside the roster.","supersedes":"8ee38b360bf19e99e46899124a6c3b2686db0694aa2f042db5e104aec88ac59d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.017219Z","id":"6fa3e8857ffc961d4c0f80ce39ef8b4d10fce374e4d0abb778c437bd056c43ac","body":{"detail":"Emits are nacked and presence is dropped for a spectator, but session() enters the lobby for every socket, so peers lists and peer frames on seated pages include spectators (with empty presence). A page that renders its peers shows spectators that the top bar does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":364},"end":{"line":364},"content_hash":"65443499bf5c59a241c5ab4f860cd305225d42129e1ebf8c2a447b67fae3b629"},"summary":"A spectator's room socket still enters the lobby, so seated peers hear a peer frame for them","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.017602Z","id":"908047fd1cffc177d4b96b00191213d8acbeae36c5798d3431428a7be54633e8","body":{"detail":"Each request takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two requests add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other request's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":281},"end":{"line":300},"content_hash":"1308fb1b8efcece6e063633ebd481cfec2ed30c693976a277e47c449adee54dc"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.017970Z","id":"54a094bac923d1c120730ceb85aa55b7bc08e7d13ddcfbfd5a542bb54bf63ade","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":654},"end":{"line":654},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122151Z","id":"af92a5c2c3d75fdd2781cd5b782cda569ad2eeaebb7bae91879b9b310bd7fc34","body":{"detail":"ChunkWriter (toolpath.rs:146-160) blocks the store job's thread on the response body's room (Handle::block_on), and on a Worker the store job runs inline on the only thread, so ChunkWriter, stream_export, export and the route are cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")). A hosted export needs a writer that buffers within a bound or an async export in clax-core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"e1be6dcc3808fd8eeee4556f4bec26441db83a04790990b10fc950f28a9e3f4e"},"summary":"The audit export is native only: no /api/toolpath/export on wasm32","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122340Z","id":"bc5b18cfa5b7ed65f354f292196beaf3c34948ee1f81007327a889da67d39c09","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122447Z","id":"72b9eb1ea8ff51f2439caac2d5ac5b2fbfad145bf2af1ca154d6e5e35e13f6db","body":{"detail":"disk_body (content.rs:23-39) opens files from the home with tokio::fs natively and answers 404 on wasm32, where there are no files; the content index (std::fs::read in lookup) and clip images (routes/threads.rs, std::fs::read) fail as I/O errors there. These routes are meant to read through an async content store; until that lands on this branch, a Worker serves no version file, asset or clip.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"42d0fbfce3cb20affd9317433b8ed1c11507d1547065d97f0194769cdade1ae3"},"summary":"Stored version files and assets answer 404 on wasm32","tags":["wasm","revisit:the content store merges","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/perf.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122535Z","id":"829e3168dd15e98163aeea968931cb6619e17b32c7588b9c0945edd40bec5132","body":{"detail":"POST /api/admin/perf/calibrate runs clax_core::perf, which times with std::time::Instant::now (crates/clax-core/src/perf.rs:81); that panics on wasm32-unknown-unknown. The route is still registered on wasm32. Either clax-core's perf reads web_time or the route is native only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"b1c4e50c7dbe11ec4a3d2583dd42614e56656b00776bc985d20ad67f45fa97af"},"summary":"The perf calibration route panics on wasm32","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.472071Z","id":"ccd21da28f36b1e6c811a1e06da3500b8ad4ed9e6cf95c2a7f2ba44df868e814","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":289},"end":{"line":296},"content_hash":"c999e8def53d154c4c3b3e4130701a6ba8fd9b6ed4134f44a7686b641ea38f24"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"591b42b8e96be7d14bfd583fa75f6fa9f613e65ddcf089e8c17ff793dc7f7d91","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.473915Z","id":"d7f989d4c06fbde92f64dcaed3022cd3a24af9860b3d1cbb3f814e9d5757f7c2","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":440},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"279de868104645c25af8c10a992b7af382111eb70730552646800f167c7749c9","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.475728Z","id":"17c0ef037e71fc5b70052ff7ae524d85e6733924d6ba126e3c86d75170cb0817","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1384},"end":{"line":1400},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"4dbe625b0ce9a7e2fa46b1894376359738f584f62f4d32f23d9c7ff02ac8aea2","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.477544Z","id":"58b6ed134d42050cc9333409f72e70e39acef82c1e182e8f05bb3b8a8f4e55f7","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1779},"end":{"line":1805},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"14a489a4f6b9e9e07b9c4fe4c26f81dc80ed918c7e123db26ff2a8c64359bbdc","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.479370Z","id":"9d320f016f628cd8fdec2aac0fb8111f10bb0b0f9a11554c497859a1e7b5f227","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"bc5b18cfa5b7ed65f354f292196beaf3c34948ee1f81007327a889da67d39c09","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.482915Z","id":"1eeb8d8793264e88c18e9e3c72034307f12ac3c8f3aa6ec8ab4f86c12ff774ab","body":{"detail":"lookup (content.rs:170-226) and routes/assets.rs blob read through the store's content store inside store_call with clax_core::content::wait (content.rs:185, and Store::read_asset). wait panics on wasm32 when the future is pending (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs wait), which a Worker backend whose reads are JavaScript promises (R2, a Durable Object's storage) always is; only MemContent-like backends that finish on first poll work there. On wasm32 these handlers need to await Store::read_file_async / read_asset_async (wrapped with clax_rt::sendable for axum) outside store_call; the wrap cache's synchronous get_or_wrap closure is what keeps lookup synchronous. Clip images (routes/threads.rs:288) still read the home with std::fs::read, which fails on wasm32.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"e1c1ce7213c764ee64910cdc838584a7f0fc75e99f0879cb61b859c033955d68"},"summary":"On wasm32 version files and assets panic for a content store whose reads are pending","tags":["wasm","content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.482958Z","id":"2a4def7ad0fc9d0ce878b79eb74e2de8197cb946421f2ea9b9b7c96e19a0f088","body":{"detail":"POST /api/stream/<id> (routes/stream.rs update, lines 184-277) checks topic counts, live-only and SeesLive visibility, owner-only and connected-person topics (questions, inbox, agents, people, site), artifact existence and db declaration, and computes each live artifact's seat claim with crate::seats::claim_for from the request's Identity, all reading axum extractors. Only the step after them, taking seats and changing the hub's subscriptions with rollback, is a plain function (crate::seats::subscribe). On wasm32 /api/stream is not routed: the Durable Object receives subscription changes as socket messages and must apply the same rules before calling seats::subscribe, so they need to become a function of (AppState, Identity, SeesLive, extension credential, add, remove) that both the handler and the object call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":277},"content_hash":"c90cb3b7b5398db7cda6e8e2de3a58b47857c9bf134911ca13d2104f42a40d9c"},"summary":"A subscription's admission rules live in the axum handler, so a Durable Object's socket subscriptions cannot apply them","tags":["wasm","live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:23.902892Z","id":"d268ca3f8f697390176b1cc51b836947619b1b2d8632c983db8e49d3588c4cec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5b81b140","summary":"The seat-taking lines moved into crate::seats::subscribe; the same concern is re-recorded on crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs:383-404. Evidence: `grep -n 'seats.take' crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs` prints nothing and crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs:374 defines subscribe; `cargo test -p clax-server` passed (669 integration, 178 unit) and e2e/seats.spec.ts passed at 5b81b140.","supersedes":"908047fd1cffc177d4b96b00191213d8acbeae36c5798d3431428a7be54633e8","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:23.904907Z","id":"0558806203b59dd82f7c938d2606eb237a1e97ab4f90e49f72c921e7f6722c61","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5b81b140","summary":"disk_body is gone: version files and assets read through the store's content store (content.rs lookup, assets.rs blob), so they no longer answer 404 on wasm32 for want of files; what remains on wasm32 (wait on a pending read, clip images) is re-recorded on crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:170-226. Evidence: `grep -rn disk_body crates/` prints nothing; `scripts/check-wasm.sh` reports zero errors and zero warnings, and `cargo test -p clax-server` passed at 5b81b140.","supersedes":"72b9eb1ea8ff51f2439caac2d5ac5b2fbfad145bf2af1ca154d6e5e35e13f6db","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.877897Z","id":"744e9a2553cd1fc862d4ab9ec7114f609a6790dfa8b8c985b5ccbe0a5195b1b8","body":{"detail":"put computes the base version's files hidden from the drafting agent (Vis::filter_hidden_files) once per revision and stores them in NewDraft.withheld; the marks are computed against the visible base files at the same time. An approval revoked while a draft lives takes effect at the agent's next revision, or when the draft ends (at most clax_core::drafts::DRAFT_IDLE_SECS without a revision). The hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts draftFile) re-reads the drafting person's visibility on every view instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":211},"content_hash":"524885053eb0739690c5f8cc1ea0b5fdf9cd2af80e5b17c37b8603bd076a8a98"},"suggested_fix":"End or re-mark live drafts when the visibility generation (AppState::vis_gen) moves, or check the base path against a fresh Visibility in routes/drafts.rs serve.","summary":"A draft's withheld base paths are fixed when the revision is stored","tags":["drafts","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.878081Z","id":"e8e391ff9c59d16b44872f002e2719257788b33062920b0b60e0d0ab4a06dc8c","body":{"detail":"The base file a drafted page is compared with is read from disk inside the store call, as routes/content.rs reads pages to wrap. When version files move behind the async content-store interface this read moves with them; a read failure is treated as no base (every element with text is marked).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":220},"end":{"line":229},"content_hash":"7e8492088ebe73767d9da3b42d4cbf122174d8eb77f0cd278c7ad8c03cfc5f66"},"summary":"Draft marking reads base files with std::fs::read through Store::file_path","tags":["drafts","content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.878566Z","id":"b8c12603f25e7960e9ef1ea91dfff2c7d5aebfcc2318dad388c8135d1c4b7774","body":{"detail":"serve sends drafted HTML marked and tinted but not wrapped (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page), so a draft never greets the shell: no pins, no comment mode, and no window capabilities (db, comments, room, sample). A page that needs a capability to render shows its fallback in a draft. Wrapping it would make the shell treat the draft as the base version's page (its hello names a version).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":354},"end":{"line":354},"content_hash":"eca1e26d7d420907fa242391f29ad9e801264b3909753b325e2d537ad065d5dd"},"summary":"A draft page is served without the bridge, so its page capabilities do not run in a draft","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.878604Z","id":"af15072fca3c079ac889bbbc9497afa58a9d2dbdce5c09a7b8db4799636062bc","body":{"detail":"The hosted prototype's draft tool watches the artifact (hosted/src/mcp/tools.ts draft) and marks the drafting agent seen so it does not go idle (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts draft, dir.seeAgent). Here a draft changes neither the session's watches nor its working record, so the top bar can say `claude idle` while the banner says `claude is drafting…`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"43358b878bf3f99a49d89f7bd0a7ad9c407135e1201b691e4f4ac8b5b20cb659"},"suggested_fix":"Renew the session's working records in put (Working::renew), and ensure_watch as publish does.","summary":"Drafting neither watches the artifact nor marks its agent active","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.649052Z","id":"47790e6e37cb7f1860992b2ad4a74e23df90c221660e1df6f9339dc88ee7350f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:37b5fb6b","summary":"Marking fixed in 37b5fb6b: put calls Working::mark(actor, aid, []) and settles it (working.start for a new record); the integration test above asserts ts.working.for_artifact lists the drafting agent's handle, and e2e/drafts.spec.ts sees the top bar read `claude working` with no `idle`. Watching is recorded apart as an alternative at routes/drafts.rs:315:318","supersedes":"af15072fca3c079ac889bbbc9497afa58a9d2dbdce5c09a7b8db4799636062bc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.650481Z","id":"073881e1c9442220ad5417bbe645a147fa11572d312cd1f1b5791d82fe28a622","body":{"detail":"The hosted prototype's draft tool also watches the artifact (hosted/src/mcp/tools.ts draft), so comments made while a draft shows route to the drafting session. Here only the working record is kept: a draft precedes a publish, and publishing watches. A comment made during a draft on an artifact no session watches waits untargeted until a session publishes or watches it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":315},"end":{"line":318},"content_hash":"11dca45825b6518377b30bd0c37721ded9f6e082f99a30fdb5b76e7c058146e4"},"summary":"Drafting marks the session working but does not watch the artifact","tags":["drafts","revisit:people comment on an artifact while it is drafted and the comments wait untargeted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.650579Z","id":"3d1b719a751b5fddd62832a063418871308afe9e0ef5a79b2429655fb913f014","body":{"detail":"This branch's base (66d2a8f3) predates rust-content-store, so drafts read version files with std::fs::read through Store::file_path, in one helper, base_file (and base_text, which takes the size from file_path's FileMeta). On akesling/clax-artifacts (85a072d0) Store::file_path is gone (content/fs.rs file_path is a free function over a Home) and the build fails here. At the merge: base_file's body becomes `st.read_file(id, n, path)` (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs, which already answers None for a missing file or bytes), and base_text takes the size from `st.file_meta(id, n, path)?` instead of file_path. serve's Served::Base arm already calls base_file inside store_call and needs no change. No std::fs remains in routes/drafts.rs after that.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"04f41f361c2c7c88f1319665c31e5f26e93b221bf302d260b96bc474277a9aa6"},"summary":"Merge into akesling/clax-artifacts: base_file must read through the content store; Store::file_path no longer exists there","supersedes":"e8e391ff9c59d16b44872f002e2719257788b33062920b0b60e0d0ab4a06dc8c","tags":["drafts","content-store","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.652773Z","id":"d2d47debfef5b90705897a2681667eb540d702e64f82bae8278afb95eb165278","body":{"detail":"serve refuses agents but checks no cookie: a frame on the artifact origin (<id>.localhost) carries none. So a token that reached a person later revoked, or that the draft page itself leaks (its own <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"unsafe-url\"> overrides the Referrer-Policy: no-referrer header, and the content policy limits no connections), reads the revision from any client that reaches the daemon, for at most DRAFT_IDLE_SECS after its last revision. The token is 128 random bits, compared in constant time (clax_core::drafts::Drafts::file), and logged nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"3510e463f7e585045febf9fa4c60eb57b2b98552150c7c73f6968301db30a977"},"summary":"A draft URL is its token alone: whoever holds a revision's token reads the draft until it is revised or ends","tags":["drafts","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.653132Z","id":"7fed8161725d890908e6babcb42a64e95750c7c472dcff12c95e0dbff3bf764c","body":{"detail":"Visibility filters agent channels only (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs header): a person's browser reads every file at /c/<id>/v/<n>/, ACAO *, and the content policy (routes/content.rs content_policy) restricts no connections. A drafting agent's page script can fetch the base version's files withheld from that agent (which the draft URL itself never serves) and send them to a host the agent reads. A published page can do the same; a draft adds that its script runs for viewers with no version recorded (drafts::delete is unaudited, put records only working.start). The shell no longer welcomes a draft page's greeting (ec3d3724), so it gets no page capability.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"3510e463f7e585045febf9fa4c60eb57b2b98552150c7c73f6968301db30a977"},"summary":"A draft page's script runs in people's browsers unrecorded and can carry files withheld from its agent off the machine","tags":["drafts","visibility","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.653470Z","id":"d181fde507ce090d2bad72c7421595f6ea21d93101544ea6140a1b6bdc694955","body":{"detail":"clax_core::draft_diff counts at most 3.8 steps per input byte on adversarial input (deep nesting past MAX_DEPTH, unclosed quotes and tags, 1 MiB attribute values, end tags popping a 510-deep stack, implied li ends under 600 open elements, 90k unique elements). Wall time measured in a release build on a machine at load average 73 on 12 cores: 3 to 35 ms for most 1 MiB cases, 490 to 590 ms for the end-tag and implied-end cases, 700 ms for 90k unique elements over a 1.2 MiB base, and 6.3 s for a small draft over a 16 MiB base before MAX_BASE_COMPARED (2 MiB) bounded the base. At DRAFT_RATE 2/s per session and artifact that is a store worker kept busy per drafting agent; the cost per element (a String per tag name, SipHash counts) is the lever, or marking outside the store call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":249},"end":{"line":252},"content_hash":"d3fe5da74d3562dbfe8d50962e50f7e4f7113170246579ad68c5b85a6354ae6a"},"summary":"Marking runs inside store_call: a revision holds a store worker while it reads and marks up to 1 MiB of draft against 2 MiB of base","tags":["drafts","perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.658709Z","id":"b397b7ae415a757be02963114620d3ef1d6b5fcb63e507dcdc75ac3fcb0475b2","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1352},"end":{"line":1368},"content_hash":"9b03a0a18c341e360605021ba38bbd66094daa97c0093f0e5095699d098efe5e"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"b3768606271bd380607bf3197a84556cee7a55c281de3d08307c56d8729ef074","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.663799Z","id":"5a4dc0d806be62eeafbb18f58e8241991f3b3e464681d3e3d2c5492b4cbb1f40","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1747},"end":{"line":1773},"content_hash":"7da1c417131a685ec4bc69dfd16cce096417abbdb7780b5eb69906b8a1fe27fa"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"83e5a82d7f4de9122c0b162e16fdb3617319f1892487120904e36d6ebb8f4fea","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.665348Z","id":"d90acfc3b276b8bc1ac06c1eb58da01efdb6d5a8322bc057f1bd5e4b104cf7df","body":{"detail":"put computes the base version's files hidden from the drafting agent (Vis::filter_hidden_files) once per revision and stores them in NewDraft.withheld; the marks are computed against the visible base files at the same time. An approval revoked while a draft lives takes effect at the agent's next revision, or when the draft ends (at most clax_core::drafts::DRAFT_IDLE_SECS without a revision). The hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts draftFile) re-reads the drafting person's visibility on every view instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":277},"content_hash":"524885053eb0739690c5f8cc1ea0b5fdf9cd2af80e5b17c37b8603bd076a8a98"},"suggested_fix":"End or re-mark live drafts when the visibility generation (AppState::vis_gen) moves, or check the base path against a fresh Visibility in routes/drafts.rs serve.","summary":"A draft's withheld base paths are fixed when the revision is stored","supersedes":"744e9a2553cd1fc862d4ab9ec7114f609a6790dfa8b8c985b5ccbe0a5195b1b8","tags":["drafts","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.666855Z","id":"e02f415119f5211a50a485fdcf3a3024887788e424a2f503ff8cd9235378c931","body":{"detail":"serve sends drafted HTML marked and tinted but not wrapped (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page), so a draft never greets the shell: no pins, no comment mode, and no window capabilities (db, comments, room, sample). A page that needs a capability to render shows its fallback in a draft. Wrapping it would make the shell treat the draft as the base version's page (its hello names a version).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"eca1e26d7d420907fa242391f29ad9e801264b3909753b325e2d537ad065d5dd"},"summary":"A draft page is served without the bridge, so its page capabilities do not run in a draft","supersedes":"b8c12603f25e7960e9ef1ea91dfff2c7d5aebfcc2318dad388c8135d1c4b7774","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
