{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:07.882171Z","id":"44fe2c0eea3a2035855c6a58bb1b4d9c57fc6fde0af73f864ae65406f39eabc2","body":{"detail":"serve sends drafted HTML marked and tinted but not wrapped (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page), so a draft never greets the shell: no pins, no comment mode, and no window capabilities (db, comments, room, sample). A page that needs a capability to render shows its fallback in a draft. Wrapping it would make the shell treat the draft as the base version's page (its hello names a version).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":431},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"eca1e26d7d420907fa242391f29ad9e801264b3909753b325e2d537ad065d5dd"},"summary":"A draft page is served without the bridge, so its page capabilities do not run in a draft","supersedes":"e02f415119f5211a50a485fdcf3a3024887788e424a2f503ff8cd9235378c931","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:07.884587Z","id":"11ad71c70e016ac1c1e672ba0a7a35539b8f9919e6d4f4902b93b2ec5b10a241","body":{"detail":"serve refuses agents but checks no cookie: a frame on the artifact origin (<id>.localhost) carries none. So a token that reached a person later revoked, or that the draft page itself leaks (its own <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"unsafe-url\"> overrides the Referrer-Policy: no-referrer header, and the content policy limits no connections), reads the revision from any client that reaches the daemon, for at most DRAFT_IDLE_SECS after its last revision. The token is 128 random bits, compared in constant time (clax_core::drafts::Drafts::file), and logged nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":431},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"3510e463f7e585045febf9fa4c60eb57b2b98552150c7c73f6968301db30a977"},"summary":"A draft URL is its token alone: whoever holds a revision's token reads the draft until it is revised or ends","supersedes":"d2d47debfef5b90705897a2681667eb540d702e64f82bae8278afb95eb165278","tags":["drafts","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:08.570770Z","id":"85e6817969e356be28c44f3df558931ecf81c5fd3c99cefbc68924ef0bf7e526","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:83ad7424","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"1264ea66b6fb3b7d2d6153ee17c839a5caa189e75693d44c5d0f3e9f4f15a60e"},"summary":"base_file is Store::read_file (the content store) and base_text sizes a file from Store::file_meta; no std::fs remains in routes/drafts.rs. cargo build --workspace --all-targets, scripts/check-wasm.sh (0 warnings) and cargo test -p clax-server (tests/api_drafts.rs) pass","supersedes":"3d1b719a751b5fddd62832a063418871308afe9e0ef5a79b2429655fb913f014","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.912628Z","id":"e0960f595ded81592e375d390ad33890028376a8ce28dfffa88467390b42b309","body":{"detail":"session() checks the seat and the viewer when the socket opens and then only watches for the artifact's deletion and the daemon's shutdown. Revoking a person (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs person_revoked_at) does not close it, unlike their /api/stream streams (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs listen ends them at the visibility generation's bump). In this daemon that grants nothing new: a revoked person is a LAN viewer, who may still read and comment on every artifact (docs/usage.md, 'LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them'), and could reopen the socket at once. Relay::clear_text (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs), meant for a person who may no longer comment, has no caller for the same reason. A port where access is per artifact (the hosted design's shares, spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.1) must re-admit on each visibility bump and close the socket (4403) when the check fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"458c04441ddbd150d6d95a6e6797b9cc1b646b640fc2168b64facea3d4e60f1a"},"suggested_fix":"In session(), wait on s.vis_gen.wait_after(seen) in the select loop and re-run the upgrade's admission (the viewer, the artifact, seated()); close 4403 when it fails.","summary":"A live socket is admitted once, at its upgrade, and not again when the viewer's access changes","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:35.898013Z","id":"3c356619efd99fe185520b2160cee6f1501e7dbded35bcb51b0e01de311d404c","body":{"detail":"session() checks the viewer and takes the seat when the socket opens, and then only watches for the seat's release for want of input, the artifact's deletion and the daemon's shutdown. Revoking a person (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs person_revoked_at) does not close it, unlike their /api/stream streams (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs listen ends them at the visibility generation's bump). In this daemon that grants nothing new: a revoked person is a LAN viewer, who may still read and comment on every artifact (docs/usage.md, 'LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them'), and could reopen the socket at once. Relay::clear_text (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs), meant for a person who may no longer comment, has no caller for the same reason. A port where access is per artifact (the hosted design's shares, spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.1) must re-admit on each visibility bump and close the socket (4403) when the check fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"c13c732764b6ad9b801cb07dc0810fd6684f07256f4cd83c2f1d31b060819ec4"},"summary":"A live socket is admitted once, at its upgrade, and not again when the viewer's access changes","supersedes":"e0960f595ded81592e375d390ad33890028376a8ce28dfffa88467390b42b309","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/perf.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:17.549982Z","id":"e953cad76795911c4c2777c945f092a9f9dd5e11254a39e64ae6e5adc582dbb0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ba638d42","summary":"Fixed: crates/clax-core/src/perf.rs now times the read with web_time::Instant (grep Instant crates/clax-core/src/perf.rs: line 14 'use web_time::Instant;', line 84 'Instant::now()'), the only clock the calibrate route reads; scripts/check-wasm.sh passes and cargo test -p clax-core passes (799 passed, 0 failed) at that commit","supersedes":"829e3168dd15e98163aeea968931cb6619e17b32c7588b9c0945edd40bec5132","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:23:33.189022Z","id":"c1995631e9cdaf61ad548cad2cec10cff5dae353269bf9847044ab3a9bfcd4ff","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":289},"end":{"line":296},"content_hash":"c999e8def53d154c4c3b3e4130701a6ba8fd9b6ed4134f44a7686b641ea38f24"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"591b42b8e96be7d14bfd583fa75f6fa9f613e65ddcf089e8c17ff793dc7f7d91","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.530800Z","id":"e4cfda8a878da7151e391778932eef2782112034f89d30f7b08f9171301395bc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4e9ca8f0","summary":"/_blob reads the row, runs SeesLive's check, then reads the bytes (Store::asset_bytes). api_live::a_live_pages_blob_is_refused_before_its_bytes_are_read passes: with a directory in the bytes' place the loopback gets 500 (it reads) and the LAN gets 404 (refused without a read).","supersedes":"0fa30e43333d659b2e5cf92e931c72070182060ae5f8e545eaea15f03b2a6725","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.810192Z","id":"4a50b0608e3d9974747d5d408a1e15ae417a66f91e9e76747d097250cd7f3900","body":{"detail":"blob reads the bytes with Store::asset_bytes inside store_call and answers Body::from(bytes); before ContentStore it streamed the file with tokio::fs. Same response, more memory per request and a store worker held for the read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"b741e43aff7c5ce56f37238e67b8a173b2079451f9455b29bb280cd23ab1d459"},"summary":"An asset's bytes (up to MAX_ASSET_BYTES, 20 MiB) are read whole on a store worker before /_blob serves them","supersedes":"af94e07800d1cc3c93fa922ba5a5ffb02ad1a77d6ee2d272859b88f34159b86e","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.346778Z","id":"69c49fe9d9211d57816020b92e27adc6289220d1f28c6729dc41551f14448922","body":{"detail":"blob reads the bytes with Store::asset_bytes inside store_call and answers Body::from(bytes); before ContentStore it streamed the file with tokio::fs. Same response, more memory per request and a store worker held for the read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":169},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"b0bceb440a27349c53fc6b900e603075c22b7957ab45d8ca558e69e49915cf06"},"summary":"An asset's bytes (up to MAX_ASSET_BYTES, 20 MiB) are read whole on a store worker before /_blob serves them","supersedes":"4a50b0608e3d9974747d5d408a1e15ae417a66f91e9e76747d097250cd7f3900","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.348853Z","id":"2d169581a09d437727ee60e95516d7cffadd41e60b2693feb33a6660dcc5ee14","body":{"detail":"lookup reads the file's bytes through ContentStore::read_file (Vec<u8>) inside store_call, and file/raw_file answer Body::from(bytes) (lines 262, 337); before ContentStore they opened the file with tokio::fs and streamed it. Responses are the same, but each request holds the whole file in memory and spends a store worker on the read. A streaming read on the interface (a body or chunk stream per backend) would restore streaming natively.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":193},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"9235976499b9515bbe2a53744bf1881463b983c8f62b3d2f24f87d397d3250e3"},"summary":"Version files are read whole into memory on a store worker before they are served, where they were streamed from disk","supersedes":"3bb28d4470be474104ee0f0c4ee7138a537e1f05f92c973bf364c6140bd43795","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.350942Z","id":"425a80b2db5bcfd2355481b215252a0860405bc8125aecd1fcb6c67b8d05170a","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":464},"end":{"line":465},"content_hash":"951ad5f5efc1832ae06efe1d11fb5641065e27f2b7f937c01e21d4e7863a0c5a"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","supersedes":"f289f0be001d302174789179713a9e3eb684658a5cb5712238dc5c279313d746","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.356370Z","id":"385dc53437f86805d38b0a35549718afcf3e668ffd86cddb36c0a72fc872a56e","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":416},"end":{"line":451},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"811a60c86d57be605eca88b08c8f0d5e22454b1bd83b1c9e7385e5a150893391","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.358260Z","id":"03ea4e12df4bbdf7e3e4b8db6d688c683b8ad37180b1e60d234fc02ae24940c1","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":437},"end":{"line":437},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"de5b2c0629cceb850f9e3f5828a266df5556d221d54f4f3f11a9f04229ced5e1","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.069868Z","id":"272212e0cc7d013c08e2bb9385138304f30821fc646629015be2a118ec618eb2","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":421},"end":{"line":456},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"385dc53437f86805d38b0a35549718afcf3e668ffd86cddb36c0a72fc872a56e","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.072008Z","id":"53f30e89212eeb56ea22479c46a6a50955e240093769643e4fd0d0937bbad2d9","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 385dc53437f86805d38b0a35549718afcf3e668ffd86cddb36c0a72fc872a56e, the other head of the same record (both supersede 811a60c86d57be605eca88b08c8f0d5e22454b1bd83b1c9e7385e5a150893391); that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:421:456.","supersedes":"e0f2887128d6142f7c20ca14994e36b73e728e3d1fe985794e297b2c67af76b9","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.074183Z","id":"81aaaf6be9ce835f54139e36d50a33cf76cbc8d87fb6c3fcddcbf416d996abce","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":442},"end":{"line":442},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"03ea4e12df4bbdf7e3e4b8db6d688c683b8ad37180b1e60d234fc02ae24940c1","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.076266Z","id":"f277969870c8c90241ea7ecaff73d9facf53811014b51548bf5e94a9add3f90a","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 03ea4e12df4bbdf7e3e4b8db6d688c683b8ad37180b1e60d234fc02ae24940c1, the other head of the same record (both supersede de5b2c0629cceb850f9e3f5828a266df5556d221d54f4f3f11a9f04229ced5e1); that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:442:442.","supersedes":"1898978522d1096c3958c0340b6f777e2f2d26163ad535ac6ce86cc7bd58b140","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.078614Z","id":"633749096d181675349e3d771970d9552d6b3db7c28599b25f3ae491a97c5caa","body":{"detail":"blob reads the bytes with Store::asset_bytes inside store_call and answers Body::from(bytes); before ContentStore it streamed the file with tokio::fs. Same response, more memory per request and a store worker held for the read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"b0bceb440a27349c53fc6b900e603075c22b7957ab45d8ca558e69e49915cf06"},"summary":"An asset's bytes (up to MAX_ASSET_BYTES, 20 MiB) are read whole on a store worker before /_blob serves them","supersedes":"69c49fe9d9211d57816020b92e27adc6289220d1f28c6729dc41551f14448922","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:35:43.404959Z","id":"1e692bcdfde57ca854ea359608aac1f60ecda7b761200953e62595db2205900a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1b0bb056","summary":"Fixed by the rust-core-hosted-paths merge (1b0bb056): content.rs lookup and the raw file read await read_file_async inside AppState::store_call_async (content.rs:181, 332-343), assets.rs blob awaits asset_bytes_async (assets.rs:172-178), and the clip route awaits read_clip_async (threads.rs:279-290); store_call_async wraps its future with clax_rt::sendable, and on wasm32 Store::call_async awaits the job inline, so no content::wait is left on these paths. Evidence: scripts/check-wasm.sh exits 0 with no errors or warnings at 039d6048, and cargo test -p clax-server passes there, including the_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor (CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred).","supersedes":"1eeb8d8793264e88c18e9e3c72034307f12ac3c8f3aa6ec8ab4f86c12ff774ab","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.222800Z","id":"edc995c2ebd8d752ba70443c523ee2c74410227f88500af6b27591b73e731ee7","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of ccd21da28f36b1e6c811a1e06da3500b8ad4ed9e6cf95c2a7f2ba44df868e814, the other head of the same record; that one stays at crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs:289:296.","supersedes":"c1995631e9cdaf61ad548cad2cec10cff5dae353269bf9847044ab3a9bfcd4ff","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.260912Z","id":"c2ae626c7eede5d0891b7f43024b0adfcf9ad487b531f9cd93db8535a0dca1b0","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":449},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"d7f989d4c06fbde92f64dcaed3022cd3a24af9860b3d1cbb3f814e9d5757f7c2","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.298322Z","id":"a88d88be43978531ddfec0255084e7b3cc03b1ee7cb2c6075a542118655682f7","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1408},"end":{"line":1424},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"17c0ef037e71fc5b70052ff7ae524d85e6733924d6ba126e3c86d75170cb0817","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.313037Z","id":"61a1a8eef6faddea7a3a19e0504f71dd10aa320c5ea52ec6652f76060ebb677f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 17c0ef037e71fc5b70052ff7ae524d85e6733924d6ba126e3c86d75170cb0817, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1408:1424.","supersedes":"b397b7ae415a757be02963114620d3ef1d6b5fcb63e507dcdc75ac3fcb0475b2","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.371678Z","id":"c05bf6c12fdb62591383a75a2f306372b662ed3e4462765a7f89a8c712191289","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1816},"end":{"line":1842},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"58b6ed134d42050cc9333409f72e70e39acef82c1e182e8f05bb3b8a8f4e55f7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.374658Z","id":"950572386c2f50e9aba568b171c25b70a0b4b36ad06e88bcda8bce5ae56aa5d5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 58b6ed134d42050cc9333409f72e70e39acef82c1e182e8f05bb3b8a8f4e55f7, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1816:1842.","supersedes":"5a4dc0d806be62eeafbb18f58e8241991f3b3e464681d3e3d2c5492b4cbb1f40","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.377653Z","id":"e4da739748d3778a23996a5b4cbd3ace91b6316423e6d03a5d71d8541f8221d1","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"9d320f016f628cd8fdec2aac0fb8111f10bb0b0f9a11554c497859a1e7b5f227","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.445758Z","id":"46af97db53c784df9c05ff48fba58ab2900ab925b01b80d590088aee387cdb14","body":{"detail":"POST /api/stream/<id> (routes/stream.rs update, lines 184-277) checks topic counts, live-only and SeesLive visibility, owner-only and connected-person topics (questions, inbox, agents, people, site), artifact existence and db declaration, and computes each live artifact's seat claim with crate::seats::claim_for from the request's Identity, all reading axum extractors. Only the step after them, taking seats and changing the hub's subscriptions with rollback, is a plain function (crate::seats::subscribe). On wasm32 /api/stream is not routed: the Durable Object receives subscription changes as socket messages and must apply the same rules before calling seats::subscribe, so they need to become a function of (AppState, Identity, SeesLive, extension credential, add, remove) that both the handler and the object call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"c90cb3b7b5398db7cda6e8e2de3a58b47857c9bf134911ca13d2104f42a40d9c"},"summary":"A subscription's admission rules live in the axum handler, so a Durable Object's socket subscriptions cannot apply them","supersedes":"2a4def7ad0fc9d0ce878b79eb74e2de8197cb946421f2ea9b9b7c96e19a0f088","tags":["wasm","live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.484443Z","id":"21895bd1b0d4589961a5323c287ce0f01b968884ee8552499dcbac026560a0ee","body":{"detail":"put computes the base version's files hidden from the drafting agent (Vis::filter_hidden_files) once per revision and stores them in NewDraft.withheld; the marks are computed against the visible base files at the same time. An approval revoked while a draft lives takes effect at the agent's next revision, or when the draft ends (at most clax_core::drafts::DRAFT_IDLE_SECS without a revision). The hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts draftFile) re-reads the drafting person's visibility on every view instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":273},"end":{"line":278},"content_hash":"524885053eb0739690c5f8cc1ea0b5fdf9cd2af80e5b17c37b8603bd076a8a98"},"summary":"A draft's withheld base paths are fixed when the revision is stored","supersedes":"9fe8165e9433375d579c012511dcdc376b20b5c6618bbb0962304bbafb618d47","tags":["drafts","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.487565Z","id":"2ef49c04c84143a27b72a3d81074658e03ab739cd6dad7d0a2f718656e2c494d","body":{"detail":"The hosted prototype's draft tool also watches the artifact (hosted/src/mcp/tools.ts draft), so comments made while a draft shows route to the drafting session. Here only the working record is kept: a draft precedes a publish, and publishing watches. A comment made during a draft on an artifact no session watches waits untargeted until a session publishes or watches it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":323},"content_hash":"11dca45825b6518377b30bd0c37721ded9f6e082f99a30fdb5b76e7c058146e4"},"summary":"Drafting marks the session working but does not watch the artifact","supersedes":"72f59f04906485e7d9922754b5633c5a8c379aefa711faeeb75c5bd2e9b546d8","tags":["drafts","revisit:people comment on an artifact while it is drafted and the comments wait untargeted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.490653Z","id":"b90606f46b83665a842986a7292ff6beacb3f6ac4752495d4d6055476421f1a1","body":{"detail":"serve sends drafted HTML marked and tinted but not wrapped (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page), so a draft never greets the shell: no pins, no comment mode, and no window capabilities (db, comments, room, sample). A page that needs a capability to render shows its fallback in a draft. Wrapping it would make the shell treat the draft as the base version's page (its hello names a version).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":448},"content_hash":"eca1e26d7d420907fa242391f29ad9e801264b3909753b325e2d537ad065d5dd"},"summary":"A draft page is served without the bridge, so its page capabilities do not run in a draft","supersedes":"44fe2c0eea3a2035855c6a58bb1b4d9c57fc6fde0af73f864ae65406f39eabc2","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.493770Z","id":"b15a1a6c9ae31145c09ffc651bd5c9b053485c78545638e66b63d54ef9e53be4","body":{"detail":"lookup reads the file's bytes through ContentStore::read_file (Vec<u8>) inside store_call, and file/raw_file answer Body::from(bytes) (lines 262, 337); before ContentStore they opened the file with tokio::fs and streamed it. Responses are the same, but each request holds the whole file in memory and spends a store worker on the read. A streaming read on the interface (a body or chunk stream per backend) would restore streaming natively.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"9235976499b9515bbe2a53744bf1881463b983c8f62b3d2f24f87d397d3250e3"},"summary":"Version files are read whole into memory on a store worker before they are served, where they were streamed from disk","supersedes":"2d169581a09d437727ee60e95516d7cffadd41e60b2693feb33a6660dcc5ee14","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.093386Z","id":"96bb7dfc2d9d6b912a69fc10d3bf959771845e285781349b8e530711d43fbbec","body":{"detail":"clax_core::draft_diff counts at most 3.8 steps per input byte on adversarial input (deep nesting past MAX_DEPTH, unclosed quotes and tags, 1 MiB attribute values, end tags popping a 510-deep stack, implied li ends under 600 open elements, 90k unique elements). Wall time measured in a release build on a machine at load average 73 on 12 cores: 3 to 35 ms for most 1 MiB cases, 490 to 590 ms for the end-tag and implied-end cases, 700 ms for 90k unique elements over a 1.2 MiB base, and 6.3 s for a small draft over a 16 MiB base before MAX_BASE_COMPARED (2 MiB) bounded the base. At DRAFT_RATE 2/s per session and artifact that is a store worker kept busy per drafting agent; the cost per element (a String per tag name, SipHash counts) is the lever, or marking outside the store call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":249},"end":{"line":253},"content_hash":"2f7401ba35374d48e150cde15f3950678cee3cf9d582c50f17d2f3f813eda549"},"summary":"Marking runs inside store_call: a revision holds a store worker while it reads and marks up to 1 MiB of draft against 2 MiB of base","supersedes":"1ede4d68076c520e9ca7b45548f1c86cb8194c152c953e93e58c0bce7f8962e9","tags":["drafts","perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.096520Z","id":"a909b194a6ef8b30f72805f726c81d325a6cf208d114206be6cb05bcbace7301","body":{"detail":"Visibility filters agent channels only (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs header): a person's browser reads every file at /c/<id>/v/<n>/, ACAO *, and the content policy (routes/content.rs content_policy) restricts no connections. A drafting agent's page script can fetch the base version's files withheld from that agent (which the draft URL itself never serves) and send them to a host the agent reads. A published page can do the same; a draft adds that its script runs for viewers with no version recorded (drafts::delete is unaudited, put records only working.start). The shell no longer welcomes a draft page's greeting (ec3d3724), so it gets no page capability.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":498},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"A draft page's script runs in people's browsers unrecorded and can carry files withheld from its agent off the machine","supersedes":"07af484e34aeb7c08c46508062aac160703577738e3edc1a5a28495ea633baca","tags":["drafts","visibility","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.099632Z","id":"2528170171e3ee76a8ad8b3efc7073f38e805da5d41088b02107a63824b92ac6","body":{"detail":"serve refuses agents but checks no cookie: a frame on the artifact origin (<id>.localhost) carries none. So a token that reached a person later revoked, or that the draft page itself leaks (its own <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"unsafe-url\"> overrides the Referrer-Policy: no-referrer header, and the content policy limits no connections), reads the revision from any client that reaches the daemon, for at most DRAFT_IDLE_SECS after its last revision. The token is 128 random bits, compared in constant time (clax_core::drafts::Drafts::file), and logged nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":498},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"A draft URL is its token alone: whoever holds a revision's token reads the draft until it is revised or ends","supersedes":"11ad71c70e016ac1c1e672ba0a7a35539b8f9919e6d4f4902b93b2ec5b10a241","tags":["drafts","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:51.117994Z","id":"75888b64b1f150ac593ea17324eb0e82fb666195024048107badad95ab6b4eeb","body":{"detail":"The token reaches only people who may read the artifact: the listing and the live socket answer 404 to a member without read (the member gate) and 401 sign_in_required to a visitor who gave no name, and the drafts events ride the working topic of streams opened for a person or a hosted guest (Hub::open_with in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs). Tested by api_hosted::drafts_and_live_layers_reach_signed_in_people_who_may_read_the_page and web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts 'a guest on a page shared by link sees an agent drafting and shows the draft at its URL'. As with a content key (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:404:406), a person who loses the right keeps reading a revision whose token they hold, here until it is revised or ends.","kind":"comment","references":"2528170171e3ee76a8ad8b3efc7073f38e805da5d41088b02107a63824b92ac6","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":498},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"On a hosted daemon too the draft URL is its token alone: the gate (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs content_path, Content::Draft) passes /c/<aid>/draft/… to these routes with Referrer-Policy: no-referrer and no content key","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:33.964370Z","id":"74f801ae20548de7789ec043136319e4a70fa22b731c4202742912691bd77a8c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2a4def7ad0fc9d0ce878b79eb74e2de8197cb946421f2ea9b9b7c96e19a0f088","summary":"rust-worker-host keeps subscriptions off the socket: on wasm32 POST /api/stream/<id> stays routed, and the shell's hub keeps using it with a WebSocket stream (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts), so every admission rule in the handler applies unchanged. Only the stream's body moved to the socket. If socket subscriptions are ever wanted, the extraction this record describes is still needed; until then proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.891183Z","id":"a608680dfe9d82f68ccf917ad69e96edc4855dddf90372973caa5d66ebcb9d20","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1388},"end":{"line":1404},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"17c0ef037e71fc5b70052ff7ae524d85e6733924d6ba126e3c86d75170cb0817","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.893201Z","id":"52de04cccce4425be90e725f3a7c009560bc0f47c8eef9439afafa1096dbdff4","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1784},"end":{"line":1810},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"58b6ed134d42050cc9333409f72e70e39acef82c1e182e8f05bb3b8a8f4e55f7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.895150Z","id":"0e5282487453aec5c96b5fa9f7bed720965326c5b4f6faf621642c920dd1fb01","body":{"detail":"POST /api/stream/<id> (routes/stream.rs update, lines 184-277) checks topic counts, live-only and SeesLive visibility, owner-only and connected-person topics (questions, inbox, agents, people, site), artifact existence and db declaration, and computes each live artifact's seat claim with crate::seats::claim_for from the request's Identity, all reading axum extractors. Only the step after them, taking seats and changing the hub's subscriptions with rollback, is a plain function (crate::seats::subscribe). On wasm32 /api/stream is not routed: the Durable Object receives subscription changes as socket messages and must apply the same rules before calling seats::subscribe, so they need to become a function of (AppState, Identity, SeesLive, extension credential, add, remove) that both the handler and the object call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":268},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"c90cb3b7b5398db7cda6e8e2de3a58b47857c9bf134911ca13d2104f42a40d9c"},"summary":"A subscription's admission rules live in the axum handler, so a Durable Object's socket subscriptions cannot apply them","supersedes":"2a4def7ad0fc9d0ce878b79eb74e2de8197cb946421f2ea9b9b7c96e19a0f088","tags":["wasm","live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.468797Z","id":"dc8cc4d4d86eef45af114d27f18e9bcf5d8b02eef90f7a332b8163fdd141b066","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":441},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"d7f989d4c06fbde92f64dcaed3022cd3a24af9860b3d1cbb3f814e9d5757f7c2","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.474253Z","id":"8e2e715687cf241001920b399a9fdf454f903bb9b9c0232082d85817028e8b7e","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1401},"end":{"line":1417},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"17c0ef037e71fc5b70052ff7ae524d85e6733924d6ba126e3c86d75170cb0817","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.480418Z","id":"59e4b83ae52c1de0cfb95c3fcf1fd4562755b60bf0f3f9900ae772f007c98059","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1800},"end":{"line":1826},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"58b6ed134d42050cc9333409f72e70e39acef82c1e182e8f05bb3b8a8f4e55f7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.486409Z","id":"c678aa7739871c2ac4c52196ef70a95bb08e9a22290dada8d53c64a7b7f6223c","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"9d320f016f628cd8fdec2aac0fb8111f10bb0b0f9a11554c497859a1e7b5f227","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.454886Z","id":"5bb8f7ff3347580a07c1908afad20fc505eda1ec3ed8e64def3b4331894e972e","body":{"detail":"The adapter's gate is /mcp's (DeniedToGrants and RequireToken; crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs checks the two are the same text), so a person's agent is refused 403 forbidden on both (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs a_persons_agent_is_refused_on_both_endpoints) and the tools run as the owner's sessionless agent. The hosted prototype's /mcp (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) admits each person's agent token and acts within that person's rights. Serving people's agents needs the tools to act under the caller's grant (the in-process client carrying the caller's credential instead of the daemon token) and the gate to admit grants; which one hosted takes is open.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"eec372db2acd5395339615de53dae0f698d52fcf46e039e79907a176aea46d78"},"summary":"On a Durable Object the adapter is still the owner's only: hosted agents are persons' grants","tags":["worker","mcp","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.448731Z","id":"48609991bb01a09e50ae690009a529e185615379ab9f9d68c9be76479cba38c9","body":{"detail":"The adapter's gate is /mcp's (DeniedToGrants and RequireToken; crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs checks the two are the same text), so a person's agent is refused 403 forbidden on both (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs a_persons_agent_is_refused_on_both_endpoints) and the tools run as the owner's sessionless agent. The hosted prototype's /mcp (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) admits each person's agent token and acts within that person's rights. Serving people's agents needs the tools to act under the caller's grant (the in-process client carrying the caller's credential instead of the daemon token) and the gate to admit grants; which one hosted takes is open.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"eec372db2acd5395339615de53dae0f698d52fcf46e039e79907a176aea46d78"},"summary":"On a Durable Object the adapter is still the owner's only: hosted agents are persons' grants","supersedes":"5bb8f7ff3347580a07c1908afad20fc505eda1ec3ed8e64def3b4331894e972e","tags":["worker","mcp","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.943895Z","id":"b32f7dae85476e96590a4029de93a74e59f51ffeb88d58c62e26345d7f9b0c4d","body":{"detail":"Direction for this record: the adapter is to admit the credentials native /mcp admits (the daemon token) plus a person's agent token once hosted sign-in lands, where an agent token is a bearer grant (Authorization: Bearer cxa_..., resolved by Store::bearer_grant then Store::grant_caller into Caller::PersonAgent with that person's rights). The forwarding half is in place (git:74708bc9): the adapter's tool set holds no token (routes/mcp_http.rs tools() builds its DaemonClient with an empty one), and each request's tools carry the MCP caller's own Authorization (loopback::caller_credential, ClaxTools::for_caller, DaemonClient::as_caller), into the full router with no connection info, so a tool call has exactly its caller's rights (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs an_in_process_request_has_only_its_callers_rights and the_adapters_tools_act_with_the_callers_credential). What remains once bearer grants are on main: the gate (require_token here, whose text routes/mod.rs l10 pins equal to /mcp's) admits a bearer grant as Agent does, and a test runs a grant with narrower rights through a tool. Open until that path is wired and tested; the owner confirms the direction.","kind":"comment","references":"48609991bb01a09e50ae690009a529e185615379ab9f9d68c9be76479cba38c9","summary":"Direction: the adapter admits what /mcp admits plus a person's bearer grant; the tools already forward the caller's credential","tags":["worker","mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.952808Z","id":"4755b796a684ead028e48839cf22947be93611b3f29f90e65740875013f6e588","body":{"detail":"The tool set here is built with DaemonClient::new(self_base, state.token, None) and calls the daemon over HTTP with the owner's token whoever the MCP caller is. Today require_token admits only that token, so the caller and the tools hold the same rights. If /mcp ever admits another credential (a person's bearer grant), its tools must act for the caller as the adapter's do (ClaxTools::for_caller with the request's Authorization, crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs), or they would act as the owner for that person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"94539e9a29982392443f38feba68ea990fb4d43ac3be42d0b4589b58f9a4e949"},"summary":"rmcp's /mcp tools act with the daemon token, so /mcp is safe only while its gate admits the token alone","tags":["security","mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.915857Z","id":"0c1afd487ae5bb71452802ad4bd2ca762605eba8795fe1a562ea72beb8e2af6d","body":{"detail":"live_layers::live is registered only in the cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")) block with the other connection-holding routes. The Worker serves the stream and rooms' sockets through the instance object's hibernation API (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs) but has no path for live layers, which would need the object to accept the socket, keep LiveLayers' seats across a wake, and drive the flush timers (live_layers.rs flush, a clax_rt::spawn + sleep per edit) from the object. Seen in node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs after commit cfe9fdaa: each browser logs 'WebSocket connection to ws://localhost:<port>/api/artifacts/<id>/live failed: ... Unexpected response code: 404' several times; the e2e checks still pass.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":467},"end":{"line":479},"content_hash":"6ffe343eee534f34df57c31a063e585a37fd89594c3a94171622631aeb7b588c"},"summary":"The live-layers socket (/api/artifacts/{aid}/live) is native-only: on the Worker the shell's live-layers client gets 404 handshakes and retries","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.729736Z","id":"fac763b25b0a111e5f2933310d5d2faf8ea414d6a00e4c2656cd9780572cf70a","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"e4da739748d3778a23996a5b4cbd3ace91b6316423e6d03a5d71d8541f8221d1","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
