{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.014878Z","id":"cd6ec52c5e4a965ff03542dae4dcdbc4703a284e731e2ee282ec145977252a08","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":87},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"fac763b25b0a111e5f2933310d5d2faf8ea414d6a00e4c2656cd9780572cf70a","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.019102Z","id":"e15f195fdba3d6a472d996f5634456849d425f85e0c45694756036017b9bd4f7","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"ebaea2779b076d94c9786ec994f3eed67cf18b0ce4dcf9ba241e129df56809e7"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"dc8cc4d4d86eef45af114d27f18e9bcf5d8b02eef90f7a332b8163fdd141b066","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.023375Z","id":"151d8b1caf89a4b706e0c8c731074150c2c3798a1abb22ec6836638200d12043","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":457},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"c00c5e7b86d60f892695273253c402c40e563674205783ee10f09a84d1756770","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.027683Z","id":"9611159af60f119c23dfd9e17ab3aac0e91fba61811c8387c0daf5787bfe5223","body":{"detail":"live_layers::live is registered only in the cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")) block with the other connection-holding routes. The Worker serves the stream and rooms' sockets through the instance object's hibernation API (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs) but has no path for live layers, which would need the object to accept the socket, keep LiveLayers' seats across a wake, and drive the flush timers (live_layers.rs flush, a clax_rt::spawn + sleep per edit) from the object. Seen in node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs after commit cfe9fdaa: each browser logs 'WebSocket connection to ws://localhost:<port>/api/artifacts/<id>/live failed: ... Unexpected response code: 404' several times; the e2e checks still pass.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"6ffe343eee534f34df57c31a063e585a37fd89594c3a94171622631aeb7b588c"},"summary":"The live-layers socket (/api/artifacts/{aid}/live) is native-only: on the Worker the shell's live-layers client gets 404 handshakes and retries","supersedes":"0c1afd487ae5bb71452802ad4bd2ca762605eba8795fe1a562ea72beb8e2af6d","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.031980Z","id":"c3e2a4ae7bc7f4e17201fa53ee94754c0827ab001372fd58aa0f2d2e30f792eb","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1407},"end":{"line":1423},"content_hash":"76651d24828660a7d3bb64c92bf8d8077380ab28420f9a790b98852a356afc2b"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"a608680dfe9d82f68ccf917ad69e96edc4855dddf90372973caa5d66ebcb9d20","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.036285Z","id":"b1ee7abcb567f6850ff5d7bf7eac6a3e9f9df282e607cd3e1af7b27f62b54a28","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1420},"end":{"line":1436},"content_hash":"64a08b01559eedc1ee17e852ba4bffa4d7555c5839c4005152b247de86288e2e"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"8e2e715687cf241001920b399a9fdf454f903bb9b9c0232082d85817028e8b7e","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.040548Z","id":"6f2e0d47b5216c0439c1c27e86ef0d6a29e88bd057009e420f94a07221db93ef","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1448},"end":{"line":1464},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"e8ce83068d03336153daeeb9e41b3c0fe6a3ffe31b843e0a924cc0a79ec8a48b","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.044857Z","id":"ba8bae3f212ea0012d728748c48427ff00860b86ac02c98625c78d47c5a038d2","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1809},"end":{"line":1835},"content_hash":"d03d23fa7f80203f956af08e021396af3f9b71efd9df4ff0b436054636778585"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"52de04cccce4425be90e725f3a7c009560bc0f47c8eef9439afafa1096dbdff4","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.049236Z","id":"d2bcafb4ad83f9843a69fe99f3675305e9ccbd103ce079e99d3f15c9208d3ddc","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1825},"end":{"line":1851},"content_hash":"cadf69a63453bf5e9dfec912640fa516a22880889ca21caa782e5c633ef705f6"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"59e4b83ae52c1de0cfb95c3fcf1fd4562755b60bf0f3f9900ae772f007c98059","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.053647Z","id":"f9973cbc23cf8f9782e3134577bb46246e40cf5da694c41d7d6c92d42a8ee1cf","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1867},"end":{"line":1893},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"8c98ec0845ea2daa8c58472b4d607a33cdfdb8e1d6add332489ea2b26f554877","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:44:32.465338Z","id":"269abbf745878e651f9941f53181ce003fe3df953f4c614863f27e8d10b00bd3","body":{"detail":"Evidence: crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs an_agent_token_acts_through_the_mcp_adapter_within_its_persons_rights: an agent of Sam (rights: read, comment and watch on Budget only) gets not_permitted reading Plan and publishing a version of Budget or a new artifact, invalid_args for file_path /etc/hosts, a working entry on Budget in its session, 404 after DELETE of its session, and 401 once the token is revoked. `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration -- api_hosted api_mcp`: 53 passed, 0 failed.","kind":"comment","references":"48609991bb01a09e50ae690009a529e185615379ab9f9d68c9be76479cba38c9","summary":"Done in git:7c2c595e: the adapter's gate (McpCaller, routes/mcp_http.rs) admits the daemon token or an agent token that agent::authenticate resolved with Store::bearer_grant; on the API verify_layer makes the bearer grant the request's VerifiedGrant, so Identity::caller gives Caller::PersonAgent via Store::grant_caller with the person's rights. Signed Clax-Grant requests stay refused (tests/api_mcp_http.rs a_persons_agent_is_refused_on_both_endpoints passes). An agent token's tools are ClaxTools::for_remote_agent (no local files, no opener) and get a harness session per initialize.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:44:32.465446Z","id":"904be19134acba9c9b6b97006ca333e9bdbf9dd0c53659f555ee470124f5b114","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c2c595e","summary":"The adapter admits a person's bearer grant and its tools act within that grant (McpCaller, agent::verify_bearer); tests/api_hosted.rs an_agent_token_acts_through_the_mcp_adapter_within_its_persons_rights passes (cargo test -p clax-server --test integration -- api_hosted api_mcp: 53 passed)","supersedes":"48609991bb01a09e50ae690009a529e185615379ab9f9d68c9be76479cba38c9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:44:32.467765Z","id":"7becb10ee78d4d1fb6527bebb3f15b7516992bfb5b43309f20824c35360e0af9","body":{"detail":"serve_agent registers a session per initialize (Store::register_session_restoring through POST /api/sessions) and ends it only on DELETE with its Mcp-Session-Id. A client that reconnects without DELETE (a crash, Claude Code restarting) leaves its old session live, holding watches, working entries and an agent seat, with no pid for the reaper to probe. Sessions need an idle end (no request on the session for a while), or the registration should join a live session of the same grant and client name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"062af621d756f6b32fb38f6f6018bddeec37cf102a9e96da850faeaf033d2534"},"summary":"Every initialize from an agent token registers a new harness session that only DELETE ends","tags":["mcp","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:44:32.467801Z","id":"12bc8dc2ee3b47c03da389b3177e083687ce2fafc8338589519130521a9e4e59","body":{"detail":"Only agent tokens get a harness session per initialize; the daemon token's clients stay the sessionless agent, as on rmcp's /mcp, so the recorded Claude Code exchange and the shared /mcp suite keep answering alike. The owner's remote agents on a hosted daemon therefore cannot use working or wait_for_feedback through the daemon token; with an agent token of the owner's they can.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"394ef6e86a9937e7641b3e5136d3f4c9983315afcaa835d84d195ead19fdf57b"},"summary":"Sessions for the daemon token's MCP clients on the adapter too","tags":["mcp","revisit:the owner's agents on a Durable Object connect with the daemon token rather than an agent token","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:19:33.546761Z","id":"9db7e298b766d523a15dd8feea022cb15b7935ecc384ef589d29ff2ba4e78c39","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7d2c381d","summary":"Each adapter request in a session now heartbeats it (DaemonClient::heartbeat_session), the reaper ends one unseen for Store::REMOTE_SESSION_IDLE_SECS, and a bearer grant keeps at most Store::BEARER_SESSION_CAP live sessions (Store::end_bearer_sessions_beyond, called by routes/sessions.rs register). Evidence: crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs an_agent_tokens_sessions_are_its_own_end_when_left_and_are_capped (in use across 60 minutes the reaper leaves it; unseen past the idle time it is reaped and answers 404; 18 initializes leave 16 live, the two least recently seen ended; another token's session ID answers 404). `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration -- api_hosted`: 26 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"7becb10ee78d4d1fb6527bebb3f15b7516992bfb5b43309f20824c35360e0af9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.153835Z","id":"a68a93d70e41809f796690d55f0de036795c22eb985b23fd08bfa3f81a77198b","body":{"detail":"put computes the base version's files hidden from the drafting agent (Vis::filter_hidden_files) once per revision and stores them in NewDraft.withheld; the marks are computed against the visible base files at the same time. An approval revoked while a draft lives takes effect at the agent's next revision, or when the draft ends (at most clax_core::drafts::DRAFT_IDLE_SECS without a revision). The hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts draftFile) re-reads the drafting person's visibility on every view instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"524885053eb0739690c5f8cc1ea0b5fdf9cd2af80e5b17c37b8603bd076a8a98"},"summary":"A draft's withheld base paths are fixed when the revision is stored","supersedes":"21895bd1b0d4589961a5323c287ce0f01b968884ee8552499dcbac026560a0ee","tags":["drafts","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.158189Z","id":"37d30892699a4e25ea3c350e57ef8e649af977934c982eadd8b874b154508b04","body":{"detail":"The hosted prototype's draft tool also watches the artifact (hosted/src/mcp/tools.ts draft), so comments made while a draft shows route to the drafting session. Here only the working record is kept: a draft precedes a publish, and publishing watches. A comment made during a draft on an artifact no session watches waits untargeted until a session publishes or watches it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"11dca45825b6518377b30bd0c37721ded9f6e082f99a30fdb5b76e7c058146e4"},"summary":"Drafting marks the session working but does not watch the artifact","supersedes":"2ef49c04c84143a27b72a3d81074658e03ab739cd6dad7d0a2f718656e2c494d","tags":["drafts","revisit:people comment on an artifact while it is drafted and the comments wait untargeted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.162557Z","id":"34da92851974e18a31fe4e026d33299c8f297bf4fb9c15080b089893959baae1","body":{"detail":"Visibility filters agent channels only (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs header): a person's browser reads every file at /c/<id>/v/<n>/, ACAO *, and the content policy (routes/content.rs content_policy) restricts no connections. A drafting agent's page script can fetch the base version's files withheld from that agent (which the draft URL itself never serves) and send them to a host the agent reads. A published page can do the same; a draft adds that its script runs for viewers with no version recorded (drafts::delete is unaudited, put records only working.start). The shell no longer welcomes a draft page's greeting (ec3d3724), so it gets no page capability.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":449},"end":{"line":499},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"A draft page's script runs in people's browsers unrecorded and can carry files withheld from its agent off the machine","supersedes":"a909b194a6ef8b30f72805f726c81d325a6cf208d114206be6cb05bcbace7301","tags":["drafts","visibility","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.166800Z","id":"e425401487e4deb34fcb9c95063cc69dbe9ea3af919991b44475fdf07cfb7264","body":{"detail":"serve sends drafted HTML marked and tinted but not wrapped (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page), so a draft never greets the shell: no pins, no comment mode, and no window capabilities (db, comments, room, sample). A page that needs a capability to render shows its fallback in a draft. Wrapping it would make the shell treat the draft as the base version's page (its hello names a version).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":449},"end":{"line":449},"content_hash":"eca1e26d7d420907fa242391f29ad9e801264b3909753b325e2d537ad065d5dd"},"summary":"A draft page is served without the bridge, so its page capabilities do not run in a draft","supersedes":"b90606f46b83665a842986a7292ff6beacb3f6ac4752495d4d6055476421f1a1","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.170979Z","id":"1895c9b55a6a878db96a5fd76e5e6273b894e2d7095dae4d1dddc2c143fa63af","body":{"detail":"serve refuses agents but checks no cookie: a frame on the artifact origin (<id>.localhost) carries none. So a token that reached a person later revoked, or that the draft page itself leaks (its own <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"unsafe-url\"> overrides the Referrer-Policy: no-referrer header, and the content policy limits no connections), reads the revision from any client that reaches the daemon, for at most DRAFT_IDLE_SECS after its last revision. The token is 128 random bits, compared in constant time (clax_core::drafts::Drafts::file), and logged nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":449},"end":{"line":499},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"A draft URL is its token alone: whoever holds a revision's token reads the draft until it is revised or ends","supersedes":"2528170171e3ee76a8ad8b3efc7073f38e805da5d41088b02107a63824b92ac6","tags":["drafts","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.220120Z","id":"8d52a4baf46eca896648c0e8c35a487b0a93cca3350c54e18ce2ec81a32c725e","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":922},"end":{"line":960},"content_hash":"7693c4df4615731751c4af05990a46d8953679703556241c78896827d043ad56"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.230413Z","id":"b5c268e6b3ed570862c1003e9e139a9179a341de20b523fbc4dd4b98cec2947e","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"c2ae626c7eede5d0891b7f43024b0adfcf9ad487b531f9cd93db8535a0dca1b0","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.233909Z","id":"ec6b03b0fe26872d471ae58b3c1a56eae6120dd21d32d798584a9cfe879bbcd4","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1415},"end":{"line":1431},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"a88d88be43978531ddfec0255084e7b3cc03b1ee7cb2c6075a542118655682f7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.237452Z","id":"31b0d5146e5ad5355d15bc42ff3445fc8ba0886cbc2fb50f83be420b46aafa8b","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1823},"end":{"line":1849},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"c05bf6c12fdb62591383a75a2f306372b662ed3e4462765a7f89a8c712191289","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:12:40.331023Z","id":"39e7ea887339101b87d0432e04a4627966991261922048a95057644b0ab9ac99","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":979},"end":{"line":1017},"content_hash":"7693c4df4615731751c4af05990a46d8953679703556241c78896827d043ad56"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","supersedes":"8d52a4baf46eca896648c0e8c35a487b0a93cca3350c54e18ce2ec81a32c725e","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.919982Z","id":"3bb78c5604c2a74284c3854b5c35670a474ad1aa46ff25451a171318c91e6f12","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:77bb5c7f","summary":"GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/live is routed on wasm32 (routes::live_layers::live_socket), its LiveSocket held and drained by the Durable Object. Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs prints 'ok   the guest's pointer reaches the owner over the live socket', 'ok   the owner's pointer reaches the guest over the live socket', 'ok   a spectator holds no live socket: it is closed unwelcomed' and 'ok   after the wake the guest's pointer still reaches the owner'.","supersedes":"0c1afd487ae5bb71452802ad4bd2ca762605eba8795fe1a562ea72beb8e2af6d","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.930307Z","id":"3c5380910226801534dda888af58a80fb0a8815c4711baef417a6220ee4f6315","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9b39d68a","summary":"The adapter admits the daemon token as /mcp does, or a verified agent token (TokenOrBearer; authenticate resolves Bearer cxa_... by Store::bearer_grant and verify_layer applies the agents' route rules), its calls acting in one session of the grant. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted::an_agent_token_reaches_the_tool_adapter_with_its_persons_rights_and_no_more passes (publish as Sam's agent, delete of the owner's page refused, a read-one-page person's agent publishes nothing, a revoked token 401); node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs prints 'ok   the agent publishes with Sam's token' and 'ok   the agent may not delete the owner's page (Sam's rights do not allow it)'.","supersedes":"48609991bb01a09e50ae690009a529e185615379ab9f9d68c9be76479cba38c9","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.947731Z","id":"2a31c22923d8fe89d278f9e9abd49218df598ba92676615d33addedf4d8485ad","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3c356619efd99fe185520b2160cee6f1501e7dbded35bcb51b0e01de311d404c","summary":"On the Worker a live socket is admitted again at each wake (routes::live_layers::reopen: the hosted session must still be live and still read the page, hosted::session_reads), so a revoked reader's socket ends at the next wake; between wakes the rule this record names is unchanged.","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.947907Z","id":"0e23d200c7f54157ae8d9c0c926e1e9bde3769a38a6453c29fb24ed6584a7ae2","body":{"detail":"bearer_session calls Store::register_session_restoring with harness_session_id mcp:<grant> on each adapter request, so each tool call of a hosted agent costs a transaction even when the session is live. A per-grant cache (checked against the session's ended_at) would make it a read. The session also never ends while its token lives: the Worker runs no session reaper (record 14d2d0a0).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"2e622c3e0adf9cfefb68ecaed58124bf3fb0a3a76f20a4ca920d296fce64d2b3"},"summary":"Every tool call of an agent token registers (or restores) its grant's session: a store write per call","tags":["worker","mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.947947Z","id":"e71a21f9af8f5f49c908a5fa9361d1247ad8821ca4c5270cf418bb3fff5b48e7","body":{"detail":"The JSON-RPC adapter keeps no MCP session, so initialize's clientInfo is not at hand on a tools/call; harness_of reads User-Agent instead. A Grok or Pi agent on a token is shown as Claude. Recording the harness at mint time (People's token form) or from initialize would name it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"a81651dab90d8cacfea4861ed842c8e89d0af0b11cc2fa9054ee12f6f6e5e624"},"summary":"An agent token's session harness is guessed from the client's User-Agent: codex when it names Codex, else claude","tags":["worker","mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.948080Z","id":"e71e01f57b4e4bfbebf4c1ef3616ae13f79f436c1ae86c14740dcac8adf0af8d","body":{"detail":"RoomSocket::drain flushes presence the send budget held back, but drains run only after a request, socket message or alarm, so the last presence of a burst can wait for the next event. After a wake routes::room::reopen enters the lobby and the kept named rooms with empty presence; peers see each other again only once their pages send presence. No browser check covers the room capability on the Worker yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":612},"end":{"line":660},"content_hash":"4b32645d0befe2a421baa2ce73228bdf416eafbe691400bf1b0112cb5107d6c4"},"summary":"On the Worker a room's held-back presence goes out at the next drain, not on the 25 ms tick, and a woken room socket's presence and named rooms' state start empty","tags":["worker","room","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.948131Z","id":"9c8bb1fb775799ac23d1c9d8eac02b15f624c4173e202bdf729f2de3ca300fa6","body":{"detail":"routes::live_layers::reopen joins the hub afresh (Relay::resend gives the rejoined socket everyone else's state at the next flush), but what this socket had shown others is gone with the old hub: a peer's arrow disappears after a wake until that person moves. Persisting the relay is not worth it; the page could resend its state on a second welcome.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"21ab902cfa32c71f68a12682b318721ca3cf69feb80b82b751655b927b4e6849"},"summary":"A woken live socket rejoins with nothing of its person's pointer, selection or draft, until the page sends again","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.088055Z","id":"6c1b5a90aec2231d0e308e6f0ad7a434b0eb17bd296b7070d0bd3c2357302522","body":{"detail":"Emits are nacked and presence is dropped for a spectator, but session() enters the lobby for every socket, so peers lists and peer frames on seated pages include spectators (with empty presence). A page that renders its peers shows spectators that the top bar does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":403},"content_hash":"65443499bf5c59a241c5ab4f860cd305225d42129e1ebf8c2a447b67fae3b629"},"summary":"A spectator's room socket still enters the lobby, so seated peers hear a peer frame for them","supersedes":"6fa3e8857ffc961d4c0f80ce39ef8b4d10fce374e4d0abb778c437bd056c43ac","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.092367Z","id":"2cd3748f963ec6473b53b6a8e979f3695aede1f24f324ac79ba222ac40916ad6","body":{"detail":"session() checks the viewer and takes the seat when the socket opens, and then only watches for the seat's release for want of input, the artifact's deletion and the daemon's shutdown. Revoking a person (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs person_revoked_at) does not close it, unlike their /api/stream streams (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs listen ends them at the visibility generation's bump). In this daemon that grants nothing new: a revoked person is a LAN viewer, who may still read and comment on every artifact (docs/usage.md, 'LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them'), and could reopen the socket at once. Relay::clear_text (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs), meant for a person who may no longer comment, has no caller for the same reason. A port where access is per artifact (the hosted design's shares, spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.1) must re-admit on each visibility bump and close the socket (4403) when the check fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"c13c732764b6ad9b801cb07dc0810fd6684f07256f4cd83c2f1d31b060819ec4"},"summary":"A live socket is admitted once, at its upgrade, and not again when the viewer's access changes","supersedes":"3c356619efd99fe185520b2160cee6f1501e7dbded35bcb51b0e01de311d404c","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.096718Z","id":"3d651998b825490fc2e0a24e5347b0e9e81666525ba86f0a06f258caf94904f2","body":{"detail":"lookup reads the file's bytes through ContentStore::read_file (Vec<u8>) inside store_call, and file/raw_file answer Body::from(bytes) (lines 262, 337); before ContentStore they opened the file with tokio::fs and streamed it. Responses are the same, but each request holds the whole file in memory and spends a store worker on the read. A streaming read on the interface (a body or chunk stream per backend) would restore streaming natively.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":202},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"9235976499b9515bbe2a53744bf1881463b983c8f62b3d2f24f87d397d3250e3"},"summary":"Version files are read whole into memory on a store worker before they are served, where they were streamed from disk","supersedes":"b15a1a6c9ae31145c09ffc651bd5c9b053485c78545638e66b63d54ef9e53be4","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.101093Z","id":"3c66503a5ac3b23baa6e2d7e046005168396f3faef27b8778b061d629dc7c0df","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1402},"end":{"line":1418},"content_hash":"76651d24828660a7d3bb64c92bf8d8077380ab28420f9a790b98852a356afc2b"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"a608680dfe9d82f68ccf917ad69e96edc4855dddf90372973caa5d66ebcb9d20","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.105504Z","id":"553a0fc27682789e1fdc1158387115dad805100c64b63996356e9cbefc2d90a2","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1798},"end":{"line":1824},"content_hash":"d03d23fa7f80203f956af08e021396af3f9b71efd9df4ff0b436054636778585"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"52de04cccce4425be90e725f3a7c009560bc0f47c8eef9439afafa1096dbdff4","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.109948Z","id":"21546ee1037d06fa153e5a46eb5abb0254519a69267ef27e663819404c0ef75d","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":437},"end":{"line":439},"content_hash":"ebaea2779b076d94c9786ec994f3eed67cf18b0ce4dcf9ba241e129df56809e7"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"dc8cc4d4d86eef45af114d27f18e9bcf5d8b02eef90f7a332b8163fdd141b066","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.114412Z","id":"6bb376ba303774e51e3db5a176da4fcb11fcb04c41248229c33b273ebb370ff4","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1415},"end":{"line":1431},"content_hash":"64a08b01559eedc1ee17e852ba4bffa4d7555c5839c4005152b247de86288e2e"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"8e2e715687cf241001920b399a9fdf454f903bb9b9c0232082d85817028e8b7e","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.119800Z","id":"f5c55d68d1206576d48fd34dd19078d7d4ec76a14b4b0d8827b26dfed815961c","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"2c519585ddd948407c0110c3ddc12bca77623c1e20274bbaddcad65b6bd19af1"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"c678aa7739871c2ac4c52196ef70a95bb08e9a22290dada8d53c64a7b7f6223c","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.124400Z","id":"af78a92dd16e1eb884d83f5227ab413121349fd95dc5b07225209df4561a5876","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"fac763b25b0a111e5f2933310d5d2faf8ea414d6a00e4c2656cd9780572cf70a","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.128995Z","id":"e6255af9749840a6f79c164e65adbd0324df7a2bff4366682d1a52f552d936d4","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":448},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"c00c5e7b86d60f892695273253c402c40e563674205783ee10f09a84d1756770","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.133651Z","id":"12f6df5372c9ade6f8bf95075c3bcc1ce1e10e09dd2222c432ec5b56739ed3d3","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1443},"end":{"line":1459},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"e8ce83068d03336153daeeb9e41b3c0fe6a3ffe31b843e0a924cc0a79ec8a48b","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.138248Z","id":"a39659971aede4d14fc09e78986540cfe5def150ddf68692d5315f9a363f0971","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1863},"end":{"line":1889},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"8c98ec0845ea2daa8c58472b4d607a33cdfdb8e1d6add332489ea2b26f554877","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.348993Z","id":"33767b64b574d6640a74c378204284bde69dabd93b4d10d38b14a9ba7f3899ae","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1814},"end":{"line":1836},"content_hash":"eac2783db1f2a9070a15fcc7963a355d5c37efde8a0c9f14cd43a138d0c0b4b4"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"59e4b83ae52c1de0cfb95c3fcf1fd4562755b60bf0f3f9900ae772f007c98059","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:20:28.276086Z","id":"e4a94dc1a3d0784dffdef1ffbf8f1b5dec830247d159c64b90e23b179c91e62a","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a hosted daemon (Hosted set, native build), an agent token minted by any member calls tools/call publish {\"file_path\": \"/any/path/on/the/daemon/host\"} on /mcp/json, and the file is read from the daemon's disk and published as that member's artifact. Evidence: a probe test in crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs (Site::new, a member's token from POST /api/hosted/agent-tokens, adapter_tool publish with file_path of a temp file) printed err=false and found the artifact. The tools here are tools_of(&tools).for_caller_in(authorization, session) (line 244), which keep ClaxTools::local_path reading the process's files. On the Worker std::fs is unavailable on wasm32, so the read fails there. rust-demo's ClaxTools::for_remote_agent (7c2c595e) refuses every path for an agent of another machine; taking it at merge (record on crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs) fixes this.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":247},"content_hash":"bb228161adcd64c3f368d57d931b0c0916bc21568b635cdf4ddc6d4ff7970438"},"suggested_fix":"Serve agent tokens with rust-demo's serve_agent(tools.for_remote_agent(), ...) at merge, or call a local-files refusal on the tools before handle().","summary":"An agent token on a native hosted daemon's /mcp/json publishes any file of the daemon's machine","tags":["security","agent-token","rust-demo","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:21:25.582724Z","id":"16e07edce5685bec1491f8275813782fd622c55ef3a3abf4c8ca9e06e10f31be","body":{"detail":"routes::live_layers::reopen joins the hub afresh (Relay::resend gives the rejoined socket everyone else's state at the next flush), but what this socket had shown others is gone with the old hub: a peer's arrow disappears after a wake until that person moves. Persisting the relay is not worth it; the page could resend its state on a second welcome.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"da512fe9ab15e01a892bcf3192aa2284b5df5e249a8fe3c844b51fc1fb1d2a39"},"summary":"A woken live socket rejoins with nothing of its person's pointer, selection or draft, until the page sends again","supersedes":"9c8bb1fb775799ac23d1c9d8eac02b15f624c4173e202bdf729f2de3ca300fa6","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:01:07.837892Z","id":"25f2f770b6ac5343ff2e13693d7024d92e8c5fabc5741e7d89f12e41bf8bea7c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:878d299f","summary":"Fixed by the merge of rust-worker-hosted into rust-int (878d299f), which keeps rust-int's agent token adapter: an agent token's tools are ClaxTools::for_remote_agent (crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs serve_agent), which refuse every local path. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server, 957 passed, including api_hosted::an_agent_token_acts_through_the_mcp_adapter_within_its_persons_rights, whose publish {file_path: /etc/hosts} on a native hosted daemon (Site::new, TestServer::spawn_hosted) answers invalid_args; node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs, 47 ok, including 'the agent's tools read no file of the Worker's machine'.","supersedes":"e4a94dc1a3d0784dffdef1ffbf8f1b5dec830247d159c64b90e23b179c91e62a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:21:53.833235Z","id":"c3e96878fce5d14c356b2af31b085d35fe0b65434cb443630aa433e9b3f05fe6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:878d299f","summary":"Obsolete: the merge of rust-worker-hosted into rust-int (878d299f) did not take bearer_session or harness_of; an agent token's adapter sessions are serve_agent's (one registered per initialize, named after clientInfo.name, answered as Mcp-Session-Id). git grep for bearer_session and harness_of in crates/clax-server/src finds nothing.","supersedes":"e71a21f9af8f5f49c908a5fa9361d1247ad8821ca4c5270cf418bb3fff5b48e7","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:21:53.844511Z","id":"d758754fcf5890e5428bc32ea59583d4ffa55a019b5ed48837cc2c7ee8d46a00","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:878d299f","summary":"Obsolete: the merge of rust-worker-hosted into rust-int (878d299f) did not take bearer_session or harness_of; an agent token's adapter sessions are serve_agent's (one registered per initialize, named after clientInfo.name, answered as Mcp-Session-Id). git grep for bearer_session and harness_of in crates/clax-server/src finds nothing.","supersedes":"0e23d200c7f54157ae8d9c0c926e1e9bde3769a38a6453c29fb24ed6584a7ae2","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139920Z","id":"333763cc59b1fa549297230385d7a12a4138d4df240e37ce6cf7ed68b5f909a9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a68a93d70e41809f796690d55f0de036795c22eb985b23fd08bfa3f81a77198b","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.140004Z","id":"3086f0beca31c085f8647afc9b999d717585484bff42fb65300722dd8a2c9107","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"37d30892699a4e25ea3c350e57ef8e649af977934c982eadd8b874b154508b04","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:20:21.074974Z","id":"19e50a77dd30b2df957e28a17230fa2930c58d1de1c3938e01fcacb8bf9bb3e3","body":{"detail":"Failure: cd web && npx playwright test comment-loop (alone, or with changelog, --workers=1) fails 3 of 3 runs at e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts:44: the feedback author is 'Alex (not connected)', not 'Alex'; the same test passes in the full suite (424 passed at ed54a5c2). The claim here runs only when the token request already carries one clax_viewer cookie; a browser whose viewer cookie is minted after its first token request (the shell's naming in setName, e2e/fixtures.ts:361) is never claimed until a later token request, so its comments meanwhile are unattributed to the owner and marked under spec 9.6. Not yet confirmed which request mints the cookie first in the full run; likely an ordering race between the shell's token fetch and the first viewer-minting request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"e15e63e666cb67b42099b41fb6a1779bb83fc0a03489d81fe4dd504d0fadd46a"},"summary":"An owner's browser on a fresh daemon can comment unclaimed: its comments reach agents as '<name> (not connected)'","tags":["tests","flaky","spec:9.6","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/git_token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:01.484573Z","id":"3eff68105009688ab103b1d50c678ae780147731a1d680496c51036236e07cbc","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md line 203: 'Cloning needs a signed-in person (a member or a guest) or their agent: a link alone gets no git token.' browser_asker maps every Caller::Viewer, hosted guests included, to sign_in_required, so a guest with a page's commenter or viewer link sees no Clone. Refusing is the narrower choice; allowing would map a guest's link access (MemberRights::allows_at with the link's rights) onto a read token and add guests to Holder and the recheck.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"c40c85f38520a360025181d015b9baf1992abc34cb56003643a4b6f7b243cb73"},"summary":"A hosted guest is refused a git token (403 sign_in_required), while the hosted spec's section 7 lets a signed-in person, member or guest, clone","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:18:42.802458Z","id":"7da93badce9e66efcee5f932d0e7a492fcfe266c921f03847d88963933fedba9","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.2 gives ask's result status as approved, declined or open. A request can also be withdrawn (its thread resolved or deleted, its artifact deleted, the asking session ended, a person revoked), and the poll then returns status withdrawn rather than waiting out its time on a request no one can decide. The MCP ask (plan Task 19) should say so to the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":442},"end":{"line":447},"content_hash":"75fb306564fcdecdeb3200d8a59920b83f2f0ba73a7dd2769d7dccf7dfce9aed"},"summary":"The ask poll answers status withdrawn, which spec §9.2 does not list","supersedes":"a9d11ae87a0598c4441bb9f4022a6245ae1789b8e54cfda09df9ecc58b86a578","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317116Z","id":"e544e92176386dfc55f78fa748de4a5713d8697f9affffd2be8feba373c2d564","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a daemon with the owner (Alex), connected people Sam and Mia, and a live agent of each watching artifact A, Sam's browser asks GET /api/artifacts/<A>/approves-first?threads=<Mia's one-comment thread> and gets [null, <Sam>]; after the owner allows Mia everywhere (POST /api/approvals from the owner's browser) the same request answers [<Sam>]. Likewise on the owner's one-comment thread Mia's ID drops out once Mia allows the owner, and on a LAN viewer's thread it reveals whether the owner's *unconnected switch is on. It works on artifacts where Sam has no agent (artifact B answered [null], then []), one thread at a time, with no request made and nothing in anyone's inbox, so it is a silent per-author oracle for every pair (approver, author). Spec 2026-10-08 section 18 gives a connected person 'People, approvals: self' and GET /api/approvals answers only their own; Store::approves_first (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1584-1640) evaluates every approver over every author for any caller that recipient_of accepts. LAN viewers, anonymous callers and agents are correctly refused (403).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":158},"end":{"line":210},"content_hash":"781e8554ed3056d10b92d3d695eac0c3e9c82387f3b8f7f766dd6e32fe6a5a00"},"suggested_fix":"For the owner's browser keep the current answer. For a connected person P: include P whenever P's agents would hold any author of the threads (their own approvals); include another person Q (the owner included) only when Q's agents would hold content P authored in those threads (P's comments, or a page P published), evaluating P-authored comments only. Others' content is never evaluated for Q != P; the card's 'waiting for Q's approval' after a send stays as it is. Add an api test: Sam asks on Mia's thread before and after the owner allows Mia and gets the same answer.","summary":"approves-first tells a connected person other people's approval decisions about third parties","tags":["review","security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:29:16.162004Z","id":"1db454339a9a63049228ec6a5a9f5be3410b4a919c41ca0a491227839e084652","body":{"detail":"session_header answers `<session ID>.<secret>` (spec 2026-10-08 §6.9). The MCP transport spec treats Mcp-Session-Id as an opaque session handle, not a credential, so a client's debug log or an HTTP proxy's access log may record it. A logged value lets whoever also holds the agent token act in that session with its rights (its narrowing still binds it); without the token it proves nothing, as the token is checked first (crate::agent::authenticate).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"a5b86af4cce22a916edb655426bdacd1f3d183eb47662b38b465087e446c91ba"},"summary":"An agent token's session secret travels in Mcp-Session-Id, which MCP clients and proxies treat as an ordinary header and may log","tags":["hosted","agent-token","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748762Z","id":"0728cf04053f5ad016502341b34a338ea13e3c11decdbe20b6c3d72acc65e2a7","body":{"detail":"The daemon tells an agent from the owner by the agent-channel marker and session headers, which an agent on the owner's machine can leave out; it can already delete artifacts or answer questions the same way (answers given with the daemon token count as answered_via cli, which the push approval refuses, crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs approval). Requiring the owner's browser (or the extension) for every push, as for answering, would close it at the cost of `clax push` by hand. Which does the owner want?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":363},"end":{"line":377},"content_hash":"eacbb6cbfd17c02fc6dfaf99821bea3d7d4b47596cf98bff351f6a229d184ca4"},"summary":"Only publish_public asks the owner: an agent that runs the CLI as the owner (CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, or curl with the daemon token) pushes without asking","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748796Z","id":"e59f28052a0ed7e2762cca842c48a8dcd565d711b9bdbd402eba2aeae61469de","body":{"detail":"The public Clax revokes agent tokens only from its People page (DELETE /api/hosted/agent-tokens/<id>, a member's browser). A bearer route for a token to revoke itself would let `clax remote remove` end it there too; clax remote remove prints the People address meanwhile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":221},"content_hash":"5d7ec0ce85e1ce9d815e390ad13e0981e2f9cb7f19a58d20b176c6d8ec1ad034"},"summary":"Removing a remote forgets its token here but does not revoke it on the public Clax","tags":["security","deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/snapshot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372160Z","id":"4b8b2d6baa82e6f191e5e21bf04b5a5270ca25e76b6e3ce64fee160628d10ea5","body":{"detail":"The hosted gate checks only (clax-artifacts, read) for a member on /a/<aid> and /api/artifacts/<aid>/... (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs member_need). GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads needs (clax-comments, read) (agent.rs ThreadsList), but the snapshot (this build, shared across callers by keep_snapshot), crates/clax-server/src/boot.rs assemble's thread list and the live-layers socket (crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs live_socket: comment drafts as they are typed, and broadcasting typing and draft text) check no comment right. Every preset includes comments read, so only custom rights set through set_person_rights are affected; a viewer-link guest is admitted to the live socket on (Artifacts, read) as well. Relay::clear_text exists for withholding draft text and has no caller.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"14b29d906190ed91dd94770abfd6558a16357a64c8ef5f6809dc171fcf97624d"},"suggested_fix":"Strip threads from the snapshot and the first-load data for a member without (Comments, read) (serve a thread-less copy of the shared build), and on the live socket drop typing and draft frames from senders without (Comments, write) and draft text to receivers without (Comments, read).","summary":"A member with clax-artifacts read but not clax-comments read gets every thread's text from the snapshot, the first-load data and the live socket","tags":["security","rights","hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372224Z","id":"f5b160eb0f4eb6b0832122112dab062b1b97ff764fe77db514034e54a9deedfa","body":{"detail":"The hosted gate admits GET /api/stream with no credential (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs, (GET, \"/api/stream\", None, Open)). open_stream caps nothing; crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs MAX_DETACHED bounds only detached streams. On the Worker each stream is a hibernatable WebSocket of the one instance object, so one client can hold thousands (the runtime's per-object socket limit, and each hub Conn's memory), crowding out every other viewer's stream and live socket.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"a3f13ff27c8566fb370caec03412da190f971fa585f35c13cd7ebd32a7a995f4"},"suggested_fix":"Count attached streams per client key (crate::hosted client_key of the peer, CF-Connecting-IP on the Worker) and per session; refuse past a small number (for example 16 per address without a session) with 429 limit_reached.","summary":"Anyone can open any number of /api/stream connections: no per-client or total cap on attached streams","tags":["security","hosted","worker","resource","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/git_token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.023859Z","id":"e4f92b14184ea17def422d82c387a797eb999bbdb429019f23bee8efa4f5661b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3eff68105009688ab103b1d50c678ae780147731a1d680496c51036236e07cbc","summary":"The owner's decision, asked 'What would GitHub do?': GitHub lets anyone who can view a repository clone it read-only, and a push always needs explicit permission. So anyone who can read an artifact through its share link (a named guest, or an anonymous visitor holding the link, on a page shared by link) gets a short-lived read token for that artifact alone, never write; fork lineage still applies (a link to a fork does not open its source).","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/git_token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.023970Z","id":"715d4f952baac21c39734bba659d1fc1bd15d3ca406bb3cd824ca514ddd613d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:72f54880","summary":"Implemented as decided: git_remotes::Asker::Link (read only, LINK_TTL_S 900 s, link holder in the RepoDO ledger, rechecked when a link stops sharing), the gate admitting GET/POST /api/artifacts/<id>/git-token on the link's read, Attempt::GitToken rate limit, and the Clone dialog for link readers. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_git_tokens: 16 passed, among them anyone_who_reads_a_page_through_its_link_clones_it_read_only, a_link_to_a_fork_does_not_open_its_source, a_links_tokens_are_limited_per_client_on_the_clock; crates/clax-worker npm run e2e:clone: ok, link visitors at 1280/390 light/dark clone with the dialog's command and are refused write.","supersedes":"3eff68105009688ab103b1d50c678ae780147731a1d680496c51036236e07cbc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:11:42.825824Z","id":"ddc04061cbe98b468ed71acf6cb01e2442e244f17348fce635c0f5a25ed7e07c","body":{"detail":"Natively the slot lives in stream::Conn, dropped when hyper drops the body, which it does once a write to the closed connection fails (the next event or keep-alive). A browser reconnecting many streams at once near crates/clax-server/src/socket_caps.rs MAX_PER_SESSION (32) may be refused 429 too_many_streams until then; a resume of a still-attached stream is exempt (slot_for). The Worker's sockets close promptly (websocket_close). Related: record 46a7bb0f.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"62e2ece88a59ae23e43e256e89988fad2f9cbd553303b8a3dff63b5b6d1364be"},"summary":"A closed SSE stream gives its place under the cap back only once the daemon notices its connection dropped","tags":["streams","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:11:42.825864Z","id":"40f37a3c964752e535e121e21a813e1f3c351144a96ac8a885c03d7c21353658","body":{"detail":"A person whose clax-comments read at the artifact is taken away keeps a loud artifact:<aid> topic (thread events with the newest comment) and a live socket that relays typing and drafts until the stream subscribes again or the socket reopens; one given the right later stays quiet until then. Rights narrowed end the person's streams only on revocation (Hub::end_streams_of). Same shape as record 2cd3748f for live sockets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":453},"content_hash":"1c7bddfab8649d3e5ddcae172be409394821195f1fbdc809a0cddbb289096b95"},"summary":"Whether an artifact topic or a live socket carries comment text is decided once, at subscription or upgrade","tags":["security","rights","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:13:38.684476Z","id":"88a1c87f939950137bede3725ebf141fad9d4bf42d01c71ed70dafaf61f9fe93","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f68d374b","summary":"Capped in f68d374b: /api/stream streams, live and room sockets count together per client address (128) and browser session (32), crates/clax-server/src/socket_caps.rs, refused 429 too_many_streams before the upgrade; Worker reopens counted again. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration a_browser_holds_at_most_its_cap_of_streams_and_sockets: 1 passed; socket_caps unit test passes; crates/clax-worker node e2e-hosted.mjs: ok. Left open: d566356c, 5235e90b.","supersedes":"f5b160eb0f4eb6b0832122112dab062b1b97ff764fe77db514034e54a9deedfa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/snapshot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:13:38.689869Z","id":"5225ce3b8301faf7127a3b62f5c6585842f56401457f530a3084d2c27a24f1d5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:378fd59b","summary":"Fixed in 378fd59b: without clax-comments read (hosted::reads_comments) the snapshot and the page's first-load data carry no threads, the stream's artifact topic is held without thread events (Topic::ArtifactQuiet), and the live socket sends no typing or drafts and relays none. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration a_person_who_may_not_read_comments_gets_no_comment_text: 1 passed; --test web_dist a_person_who_may_not_read_comments_gets_a_bootstrap_without_threads: 1 passed. A link guest's rights always include comments read (LinkAccess::rights). Left open: 32dcb8a0.","supersedes":"4b8b2d6baa82e6f191e5e21bf04b5a5270ca25e76b6e3ce64fee160628d10ea5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:46:48.116971Z","id":"88e417ddc5fae8e9990c9ba43ce8ee4c916d8838284c80c02dcf5cb593b92b71","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"19e50a77dd30b2df957e28a17230fa2930c58d1de1c3938e01fcacb8bf9bb3e3","summary":"web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts fails both modes on this: the piggyback feedback's author is 'Alex (not connected)', where the spec expects 'Alex' (npx playwright test e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts, run in the full suite and again alone, on rust-lane2 at 04295819; no commit since 0f603005 touches the label).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:13:52.492988Z","id":"f68168e1c4a1f2fc2b2189ac24c9f515d4abafacac816c0e9c3896871d156f9d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9677a693","summary":"Fixed. Cause: not a cookie race. A request log of web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts run alone shows the owner's browser never holds a clax_viewer cookie: /api/token sets the owner cookie before any viewer route, and every later request, the comment's POST included, carries it, so the comment is the owner's. The label came from Store::connected (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs), cached per visibility generation: on a fresh daemon the agent's view was read before the browser's first request made the owner's row, and Store::owner_viewer (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs) made it without bumping the generation, so the owner's public ID read as an unconnected author's. owner_viewer now bumps it. Evidence: store::viewers::tests::the_owners_row_made_after_agents_looked_is_connected_to_them fails before and passes after; cd web && npx playwright test e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts --workers=1 passed 2 of 2, three runs in a row (it failed both modes before).","supersedes":"19e50a77dd30b2df957e28a17230fa2930c58d1de1c3938e01fcacb8bf9bb3e3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T06:36:05.901617Z","id":"41c60b0e18ad0957087a10fb0d92c600d4614f03582971937fef8f048dfc01df","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f68168e1c4a1f2fc2b2189ac24c9f515d4abafacac816c0e9c3896871d156f9d","summary":"The bump is narrowed by e79e7ce0: it happens only once Store::connected has been read since the store opened (an agent's view that may be stale), so a fresh daemon's first owner request no longer moves the generation. Evidence: crates/clax-worker e2e.mjs failed 'after a write the alarm is set for the planner refresh, an hour on: 29997' with the unconditional bump (the generation move rechecked git tokens and set the 30 s retry alarm) and passes 19 of 19 at e79e7ce0; web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts alone passed 2 of 2 three times in a row at e79e7ce0; the core test also checks a fresh store's generation stays put.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f7838a6a57b586e9eddd9e0040ea063a26ec5704aec91985addcf33eb54cfab9","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1469},"end":{"line":1485},"content_hash":"e8aa8303fb670c121eef18732bf40e8e9c0ff14aa8c99f02db449d1bda02fa55"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"6f2e0d47b5216c0439c1c27e86ef0d6a29e88bd057009e420f94a07221db93ef","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"4bca6264c54b501d6b2b8bae51e0bb4a14d75b4d9c4736d92d22dca8319354c1","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1897},"end":{"line":1923},"content_hash":"e7f3eabf7c9c120c71fd347789f4e774b56d7120713e0ec78531b3c1b7cb4478"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"f9973cbc23cf8f9782e3134577bb46246e40cf5da694c41d7d6c92d42a8ee1cf","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"d1619874b392af10884baf4542d4c1108f72d2480841a86981a1e9cf2ca2ecf3","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"cd6ec52c5e4a965ff03542dae4dcdbc4703a284e731e2ee282ec145977252a08","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"71058648eb095f82c3cca44056cbafe8b2f4f370de9ad825db791c63c33aa6ff","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":460},"end":{"line":462},"content_hash":"6773133051e8fea59184e8c6cffa9d213b9291aaa9ba965640605d1ef17d568b"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"151d8b1caf89a4b706e0c8c731074150c2c3798a1abb22ec6836638200d12043","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"67b915cdb4cd981266b48044b42f2133e22df6d2ea346c4725c3bcb5354f97b1","body":{"detail":"The token reaches only people who may read the artifact: the listing and the live socket answer 404 to a member without read (the member gate) and 401 sign_in_required to a visitor who gave no name, and the drafts events ride the working topic of streams opened for a person or a hosted guest (Hub::open_with in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs). Tested by api_hosted::drafts_and_live_layers_reach_signed_in_people_who_may_read_the_page and web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts 'a guest on a page shared by link sees an agent drafting and shows the draft at its URL'. As with a content key (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:404:406), a person who loses the right keeps reading a revision whose token they hold, here until it is revised or ends.","kind":"comment","references":"2528170171e3ee76a8ad8b3efc7073f38e805da5d41088b02107a63824b92ac6","span":{"start":{"line":449},"end":{"line":499},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"On a hosted daemon too the draft URL is its token alone: the gate (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs content_path, Content::Draft) passes /c/<aid>/draft/… to these routes with Referrer-Policy: no-referrer and no content key","supersedes":"75888b64b1f150ac593ea17324eb0e82fb666195024048107badad95ab6b4eeb","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"08cd518f29ec9f1d66b25f1b6338d4e9d3c217ac77a9404d59fd974a0adbe300","body":{"detail":"Emits are nacked and presence is dropped for a spectator, but session() enters the lobby for every socket, so peers lists and peer frames on seated pages include spectators (with empty presence). A page that renders its peers shows spectators that the top bar does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"65443499bf5c59a241c5ab4f860cd305225d42129e1ebf8c2a447b67fae3b629"},"summary":"A spectator's room socket still enters the lobby, so seated peers hear a peer frame for them","supersedes":"6c1b5a90aec2231d0e308e6f0ad7a434b0eb17bd296b7070d0bd3c2357302522","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"60eb062157b15f46a5b3e66660fc5eaadd763505401923637ccc28a89d7d9e4f","body":{"detail":"RoomSocket::drain flushes presence the send budget held back, but drains run only after a request, socket message or alarm, so the last presence of a burst can wait for the next event. After a wake routes::room::reopen enters the lobby and the kept named rooms with empty presence; peers see each other again only once their pages send presence. No browser check covers the room capability on the Worker yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":633},"end":{"line":681},"content_hash":"4b32645d0befe2a421baa2ce73228bdf416eafbe691400bf1b0112cb5107d6c4"},"summary":"On the Worker a room's held-back presence goes out at the next drain, not on the 25 ms tick, and a woken room socket's presence and named rooms' state start empty","supersedes":"e71e01f57b4e4bfbebf4c1ef3616ae13f79f436c1ae86c14740dcac8adf0af8d","tags":["worker","room","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"c46b54a870be13f82edcb44ff38f203150ce7b9f8cd25f673afc370f0a4827c6","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a daemon with the owner (Alex), connected people Sam and Mia, and a live agent of each watching artifact A, Sam's browser asks GET /api/artifacts/<A>/approves-first?threads=<Mia's one-comment thread> and gets [null, <Sam>]; after the owner allows Mia everywhere (POST /api/approvals from the owner's browser) the same request answers [<Sam>]. Likewise on the owner's one-comment thread Mia's ID drops out once Mia allows the owner, and on a LAN viewer's thread it reveals whether the owner's *unconnected switch is on. It works on artifacts where Sam has no agent (artifact B answered [null], then []), one thread at a time, with no request made and nothing in anyone's inbox, so it is a silent per-author oracle for every pair (approver, author). Spec 2026-10-08 section 18 gives a connected person 'People, approvals: self' and GET /api/approvals answers only their own; Store::approves_first (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1584-1640) evaluates every approver over every author for any caller that recipient_of accepts. LAN viewers, anonymous callers and agents are correctly refused (403).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":215},"content_hash":"781e8554ed3056d10b92d3d695eac0c3e9c82387f3b8f7f766dd6e32fe6a5a00"},"suggested_fix":"For the owner's browser keep the current answer. For a connected person P: include P whenever P's agents would hold any author of the threads (their own approvals); include another person Q (the owner included) only when Q's agents would hold content P authored in those threads (P's comments, or a page P published), evaluating P-authored comments only. Others' content is never evaluated for Q != P; the card's 'waiting for Q's approval' after a send stays as it is. Add an api test: Sam asks on Mia's thread before and after the owner allows Mia and gets the same answer.","summary":"approves-first tells a connected person other people's approval decisions about third parties","supersedes":"e544e92176386dfc55f78fa748de4a5713d8697f9affffd2be8feba373c2d564","tags":["review","security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f700615fc0a3f8a1aee1956cf1cc843a0cea305467f8426880dcede5535550e1","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"fdef32ef55ec060aeebfe4fd3b77d7814bf6706887dea024f0f20ef0a60067d3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"52dfbde6b019fe6a5ee6066932f9afa8c15f394339d29cb476138147b7611250","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
