{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.140179Z","id":"d98b823326b05356d0e34f2265fe80a0e92ee64c84309796cb6fbe4459b4f8a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 151d8b1caf89a4b706e0c8c731074150c2c3798a1abb22ec6836638200d12043 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"e15f195fdba3d6a472d996f5634456849d425f85e0c45694756036017b9bd4f7","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.147703Z","id":"5d57bd4aad55bce779422f51d238f85105313b58a45157f30d27a58ca9a37ffe","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that 3bb78c5604c2a74284c3854b5c35670a474ad1aa46ff25451a171318c91e6f12 closed (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/live is routed on wasm32 (routes::live_layers::live_socket), its LiveSocket held and drained by the Durable Object. Evidence: node crat). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content.","supersedes":"9611159af60f119c23dfd9e17ab3aac0e91fba61811c8387c0daf5787bfe5223","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"6213635be19c356b2d9831790871738f8714a104f67dde0613e768f006669e14","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":486},"end":{"line":521},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"272212e0cc7d013c08e2bb9385138304f30821fc646629015be2a118ec618eb2","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"300ee61fe75092fdf8889355a930839fb6e30217ae18cbcdc2bf9f848e7084b8","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":507},"end":{"line":507},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"81aaaf6be9ce835f54139e36d50a33cf76cbc8d87fb6c3fcddcbf416d996abce","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"36c662a8d41a43133f4b3b6cd2a5a6ea8fb7efb6e4bdc250f4e7811229ca6070","body":{"detail":"session() checks the viewer and takes the seat when the socket opens, and then only watches for the seat's release for want of input, the artifact's deletion and the daemon's shutdown. Revoking a person (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs person_revoked_at) does not close it, unlike their /api/stream streams (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs listen ends them at the visibility generation's bump). In this daemon that grants nothing new: a revoked person is a LAN viewer, who may still read and comment on every artifact (docs/usage.md, 'LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them'), and could reopen the socket at once. Relay::clear_text (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs), meant for a person who may no longer comment, has no caller for the same reason. A port where access is per artifact (the hosted design's shares, spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.1) must re-admit on each visibility bump and close the socket (4403) when the check fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"2786b95a56d4cae4fd02a4548c25447fcfa620ba12d0d24e2f10f075da0f0dcc"},"summary":"A live socket is admitted once, at its upgrade, and not again when the viewer's access changes","supersedes":"2cd3748f963ec6473b53b6a8e979f3695aede1f24f324ac79ba222ac40916ad6","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"c031366b65888ea5945f83c653cbd2142c1f01b6f70524b84c6da0cf1be6668d","body":{"detail":"routes::live_layers::reopen joins the hub afresh (Relay::resend gives the rejoined socket everyone else's state at the next flush), but what this socket had shown others is gone with the old hub: a peer's arrow disappears after a wake until that person moves. Persisting the relay is not worth it; the page could resend its state on a second welcome.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":486},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"018ad9b2e50f9ed674cba78d726d678c501c99a3821e8d1fc4565205d3a38861"},"summary":"A woken live socket rejoins with nothing of its person's pointer, selection or draft, until the page sends again","supersedes":"16e07edce5685bec1491f8275813782fd622c55ef3a3abf4c8ca9e06e10f31be","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"f2e4c83e06f2e8ec11b0bd3cf52e202e0193a0d85b13bdde34252b5c60a63be5","body":{"detail":"Only agent tokens get a harness session per initialize; the daemon token's clients stay the sessionless agent, as on rmcp's /mcp, so the recorded Claude Code exchange and the shared /mcp suite keep answering alike. The owner's remote agents on a hosted daemon therefore cannot use working or wait_for_feedback through the daemon token; with an agent token of the owner's they can.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"240e78afcd7d7ab51d3ca72a818303d61a0d32b6033d0a8a94dd9d2abf251978"},"summary":"Sessions for the daemon token's MCP clients on the adapter too","supersedes":"12bc8dc2ee3b47c03da389b3177e083687ce2fafc8338589519130521a9e4e59","tags":["mcp","revisit:the owner's agents on a Durable Object connect with the daemon token rather than an agent token","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.242297Z","id":"2f3c49f59381903071a42a10a7443ae9cc600a012ecfc87a729628d54fd3183a","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"No longer true: the Worker takes subscription changes over POST /api/stream/{id} through the router (crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:184 is routed on both targets; crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs module docs, Sockets: 'A stream's subscriptions stay on POST /api/stream/<id>, through the router and its admission rules'), so routes::stream::update's admission rules apply on the Worker unchanged and no socket-message path needs them.","supersedes":"887be143ea8cd30c3309ea64a3e5ac814ddd31d9620fdded526d05bfd663550c","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T14:38:11.322382Z","id":"24fe742595ff5c527a584774757fc9e5e10ed54b5fd78c527804712bb565d390","body":{"detail":"GET /api/inbox?q= searches inbox_fts, whose text holds each reply's body (crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs insert_at). Since 60859f1e a person who may not read an artifact's comments gets its reply items without body or summary, but a search still returns or omits those items by their text, and total counts them, so the text can be probed word by word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"5f5a1bfceba39c7a1481ebe8360a90fc57ed780f72988b4d9e3b4aa245ea54bd"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, leave out of a text search the items of artifacts whose comments the recipient may not read (filter the matched rows with inbox::reads_comments before paging, or keep text searches to items whose artifact they read comments at).","summary":"A hosted person's inbox search matches reply text they may no longer read","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.418825Z","id":"dd537fbc60f3696f312b219b701f346cce12ba6131bab1b038708dabffbd609f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:799049c6","summary":"Fixed in 799049c6: POST /api/live/threads answers unresolved_mentions as the threads route does. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration a_live_threads_answer_names_the_at_names_that_reached_no_agent: 1 passed (failed before with the field missing); -- api_live: 75 passed.","supersedes":"425a80b2db5bcfd2355481b215252a0860405bc8125aecd1fcb6c67b8d05170a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.857897Z","id":"ceab0092a3d104049522cee0946fe9a06d8405a1770bff1dddc2a7160cbcdb2d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:444e2156","summary":"Removing a remote calls DELETE /api/hosted/agent-token (a new route that revokes the calling agent token) before forgetting it, and answers revoked: false when the remote could not; clax remote remove then names the People page. Evidence: api_remotes::removing_a_remote_revokes_its_token_there_or_says_it_could_not passes (grant no longer approved; a token revoked there first gives revoked false and the remote is still forgotten); crates/clax-cli/tests/remote_push.rs passes.","supersedes":"e59f28052a0ed7e2762cca842c48a8dcd565d711b9bdbd402eba2aeae61469de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.863892Z","id":"fbee94ff52578e35c10ac94bd15e2b98daab0ef70beeb2533edc6266de7ffbaf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0728cf04053f5ad016502341b34a338ea13e3c11decdbe20b6c3d72acc65e2a7","summary":"Restated for the decision: an agent on the owner's machine can publish to a public Clax without asking the owner by acting as the owner by hand (CLAX_CHANNEL=owner clax push, or curl with the daemon token from the home), as it can already delete artifacts. The cheap mitigation holds: `clax push` under a detected harness (CLAUDECODE, CODEX_*, PI_CODING_AGENT or CLAX_CHANNEL=agent) is refused 400 no_session before anything else, pointed at publish_public (api_remotes::an_agents_cli_push_is_refused_and_pointed_at_publish_public; crates/clax-cli/tests/remote_push.rs with CLAUDECODE=1). Options: (a) keep it so; (b) require the owner's browser or extension for every push, losing `clax push` by hand.","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.652677Z","id":"19d83a797d0cd912abf50a9b4b9f4ce7ccbfffa7702cb0c8b6d16333fed8d413","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e544e92176386dfc55f78fa748de4a5713d8697f9affffd2be8feba373c2d564","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-13): \"Only about their content\", as the suggested fix describes: the owner learns every approver; a connected person P learns P's own approvals and others' only about content P wrote; LAN viewers, anonymous callers and agents 403. Spec sections 10 and 18 amended; implemented in git:fb207faf.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.652781Z","id":"ee53476963c477edb2956f0d653b4b605e08431acde109aabeffbe47c69dd369","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"Store::approves_first takes the asker: for a connected person it weighs others' approvals only of the asker's own content. Evidence: api_approvals::a_connected_person_learns_who_approves_first_only_about_their_own_content passes (Sam probes Mia's, the owner's and a LAN viewer's threads before and after the owner allows Mia, Mia allows the owner and the owner's LAN switch turns off: the same answer, [Sam], each time; on his own thread he learns the owner and Mia), and fails when the asker's restriction is removed; who_approves_first_reaches_only_the_owner_and_connected_people passes.","supersedes":"e544e92176386dfc55f78fa748de4a5713d8697f9affffd2be8feba373c2d564","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:06:03.835506Z","id":"e78eddb03488b5dc19bcd35d202590080d59c65ddff77859a67df157b5249721","body":{"detail":"Failure: a connected person Sam who created nothing sends DELETE /api/agents/<Mia's agent handle>/elevate from his browser (same origin). set_elevation finds any live agent (agent_of(st, &handle, &None, true)), Store::elevate_agent succeeds with nothing to remove, and agent_view returns 200 with Mia's narrow, the owner's elevate and elevations (with access), rights and grant_id. Every reader of an artifact learns its participant agents' handles (participants.agents[].handle in GET /api/artifacts/<id>), so any person can read the rights configuration of any agent that touched an artifact they can read. Spec §7.4 says a granter sees only their own elevations, and §18 gives a person only others' agents' names and states (GET /api/agents nulls other persons' handles). Reproduced on a scratch daemon at 5a9a449d. Fix: for a person caller, answer with {handle, name, elevation: the caller's own} only, and 404 a DELETE when the caller holds no elevation of that agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":714},"end":{"line":733},"content_hash":"73751fe0ac1cf455a65cc0d42b30e603e728500bd5b3b06d5c2db6e35d3019f0"},"summary":"PUT|DELETE /api/agents/<handle>/elevate hand any connected person the full view of any live agent: its narrowing, every granter's elevation, effective rights and grant ID","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:42.131552Z","id":"a9c88187ba495ea98539f730f7ac932abcd434d11bea1c3aaebca384fe228f36","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7329a263","summary":"Fixed: set_elevation answers through granter_answer (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs): the owner, and a person raising their own agent, get the whole view; a person raising another person's agent gets only {handle, name, person, elevation}, their own raise; a DELETE with no raise of theirs is 404 not_raised. The People topic, which only the owner subscribes to (routes/stream.rs refuses it to others), still gets the whole view. The other new responses were checked: GET /api/people/me/raises names only agents the caller raised plus raisable handles the artifact's participants already carry; GET /api/people is owner-only. Evidence: api_people::a_raise_answers_a_person_with_their_own_raise_alone passes (Sam, with no raise, DELETEs on Mia's narrowed, owner-raised agent: 404, no narrow/rights/elevations/grant_id/harness or the owner's artifact in the body, no audit row; his PUT reads back exactly elevation/handle/name/person); the full-view-to-all mutation of granter_answer fails 4 tests. CLAX_TEST_BIN=<stable bin> cargo nextest run --workspace: 2198 passed, 10 skipped","supersedes":"e78eddb03488b5dc19bcd35d202590080d59c65ddff77859a67df157b5249721","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.451612Z","id":"fa24a2c3619a75bc4062fb9ddb3df8cb54b7295203487c301b03b3295624927d","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":436},"content_hash":"20fb897884082f66581aaae4c04a83c9d1e2c433b40aea73a1a440a9a722ac9f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"de5b2c0629cceb850f9e3f5828a266df5556d221d54f4f3f11a9f04229ced5e1","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.452800Z","id":"50b65795e983c231e0d15015bf9fd7fb5d01a9d4497b7daa6e5f6249abc62088","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":415},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"811a60c86d57be605eca88b08c8f0d5e22454b1bd83b1c9e7385e5a150893391","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.454094Z","id":"8f0d1353b4b033a9e1623e8369d277a49a9eeaf98918111ae00ac91bb8f77e44","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1753},"end":{"line":1779},"content_hash":"b10b976153597d51ca9c9e38ffd71c56521a63209bf872bc9508fdcd811d7d15"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"83e5a82d7f4de9122c0b162e16fdb3617319f1892487120904e36d6ebb8f4fea","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.455294Z","id":"639f95e4b77eba894f1947b4f4693806d319ce8d755513fa613650a2b3077d46","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.2 gives ask's result status as approved, declined or open. A request can also be withdrawn (its thread resolved or deleted, its artifact deleted, the asking session ended, a person revoked), and the poll then returns status withdrawn rather than waiting out its time on a request no one can decide. The MCP ask (plan Task 19) should say so to the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":453},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"03a9d61f87e1259617c1bf80109a21129cd9ff157b1dda0a83b028bcd6dd5a9d"},"summary":"The ask poll answers status withdrawn, which spec §9.2 does not list","supersedes":"7da93badce9e66efcee5f932d0e7a492fcfe266c921f03847d88963933fedba9","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271685Z","id":"4b1266089f5c203a13a7271975fc606018315071deabcde3cbb471110144707b","body":{"detail":"Failure: with the owner's and Sam's tabs open on an artifact, the owner (or Sam) posts a new thread '@claude ...'. announce_new_thread (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:539-573) calls apply (publish_states) before publish_thread, so each reader's stream gets feedback_state for a thread its client does not hold yet (recorded order: feedback_state 02:49:14.680, thread 02:49:14.681). The shell maps the state onto threads it holds (web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts:158), so it is dropped; the thread event carries no delivery state, so the card has feedback_state null and reads the visitor's label 'sent to claude' (seen in Chromium at 390 px for the owner and Sam), where a reload reads 'sent, waiting for the agent'. The hub records the dropped state as sent (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs project, ch.delivery), so an identical state is never sent again; the card stays wrong until the state changes. For a held @name (Mia's '@clax-multi-person' to Sam's agent) the approver's card would read 'sent to clax-multi-person' instead of 'waiting for your approval'. Before this round the thread event carried the state, so this did not happen. Fix: publish the thread event before apply in announce_new_thread (and wherever a thread's first event can follow its state), or have the shell keep a feedback_state for a thread it does not hold until the thread arrives; add a stream test for the order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":573},"content_hash":"f4a98e4b8cea2e177844a75783099c36b8cf454deed33bddfcdce479e800d2a1"},"summary":"A new thread's feedback_state reaches streams before its first thread event, so the shell drops it and the hub never sends it again: an @name thread reads 'sent to <agent>' to the owner and to its approver","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271743Z","id":"769e8ffa40084bf1e0cc980c87040df0d76e50a57bf568a283a2ba98b0c8cb79","body":{"detail":"The owner's codex (Handles::Of(None)) reads GET /api/agents with the owner's claude in full: blocked {approvals: 1, since} while Sam's thread to claude waits for the owner, and blocked null at the moment the owner declines. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md section 10's table gives any other agent no delivery state of a thread ('Own threads only'), and section 17 gives an agent its own agent in the roster. The count names no thread and no approver beyond the agents' own person, so it is a timing signal only. Options: null blocked.approvals for an agent caller reading another session; or accept it and say so in section 13.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"51d1e677415e08c708b99b58450b0acfc34dc98b0ae660ccfa6638cec8448c04"},"summary":"The roster's blocked field shows an agent the approval waits of its person's other agents, a held state of threads not sent to it","tags":["review","people","spec:10","spec:13","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271800Z","id":"cf9143881bdc11af7629b07c0203acb39e0bb7c177bc15d735c28dbdf2db5a5f","body":{"detail":"The doc says that when no delivered rows remain 'the thread event carries feedback_state: null'. Thread events now carry no feedback_state (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs thread_event_views), and publish (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs, 'let Some(d) = all.remove(tid) else { continue }') skips a thread with no rows. So an open card elsewhere keeps 'waiting for Sam's approval' or 'seen by the agent' after the thread is resolved, and shows it again if the thread is reopened, until it is fetched. Code reading; not exercised. Fix: publish a null state to the readers who held one (the owner and the thread's people) when a thread's rows are gone, and update the doc.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1272},"end":{"line":1274},"content_hash":"6177f06a219a1e350e68f8d0286d5a240c56615491d4180d386640185a689a65"},"summary":"A resolve that withdraws every row publishes no feedback_state and its thread event carries none, so clients keep the old state, against this doc comment","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.404205Z","id":"12a579b9ddd2f9e7654cdf1049f97fc6d93db17c8a44f5c5432d57dc906265f2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c84e0d7a","summary":"Fixed: announce_new_thread (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs) publishes the thread event before applying its sends' states, and the shell keeps a state heard for a thread it does not hold until the thread arrives (web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts, early). The hub forgets what it sent a person when a stream of theirs subscribes or resumes (Channel::forget_sent). api_threads::a_new_threads_event_precedes_its_delivery_state and api_approvals::a_new_held_name_thread_reaches_the_approver_thread_first pass (reordering is caught by both); vitest 'keeps a delivery state heard before its thread' passes (dropping it is caught); stream::tests::a_delivery_state_reaches_its_readers_streams_alone_and_never_twice_the_same covers the subscribe and resume reset. In Chromium at 1280 light and 390 dark, with every tab open, the owner's new @claude thread read 'sent, waiting for the agent' to the owner and 'sent to claude' to Sam, Mia and a LAN viewer, and Mia's new @sam-notes thread read 'waiting for your approval' to Sam, 'waiting for Sam's approval' to the owner and Mia, and 'sent to sam-notes' to the LAN viewer, all live with no reload.","supersedes":"4b1266089f5c203a13a7271975fc606018315071deabcde3cbb471110144707b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.405459Z","id":"cfe19973a52bfbd02183254b92ec6ed2fb144fc7aa0d8f3ffcb0a7a05b947106","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c84e0d7a","summary":"Fixed: GET /api/agents gives an agent the approval requests in blocked of its own session only; a sibling's blocked counts its questions alone (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs list_agents, RosterAgent::questions_since). api_approvals::an_agent_reads_no_siblings_approval_waits_in_the_roster passes: claude reads its own approvals: 1 while the owner's codex reads claude with no approval wait; letting siblings read it again is caught.","supersedes":"769e8ffa40084bf1e0cc980c87040df0d76e50a57bf568a283a2ba98b0c8cb79","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.406766Z","id":"afbf31bebbe7cfd72de2830f89094d0883ad1c186dff157b4cc377bdafca33fc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c84e0d7a","summary":"Fixed: when no row is left, publish sends state: null to the owner's and every connected person's streams (Gate::People, events::EVERY_PERSON), the shell and the extension take it as no state, and the resolve route's doc comment says so. api_threads::viewer_resolve_withdraws_undelivered_feedback passes, reading state null on the owner's stream after the resolve; removing the publish is caught.","supersedes":"cf9143881bdc11af7629b07c0203acb39e0bb7c177bc15d735c28dbdf2db5a5f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:07:02.775108Z","id":"4c2785d3cb776979fe92f3190238e7b815c92f623ded6f5a7d41ee2d5833a86a","body":{"detail":"Spec section 11 'Display' and section 19 item 1 say a reply's author line in payloads is `<name> (<person>'s agent, via <harness>)`, or `<name> (agent, via <harness>)` for the reader's own person's agents (`clax-claude (agent, via claude)`). The reply here is written with `author_name: sess.harness.clone()`, and nothing renders the named form (`grep -rn 'agent, via' crates` finds nothing), so comments_read's author_name and every payload carry the harness (`claude`). The comments_reply tool description (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs, plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json) and docs/contract.md still say the person sees the harness's name, matching the code.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":882},"end":{"line":889},"content_hash":"496a85966405b9438aba7fcd86af7ddf58d7a1a157d4879f35bb4c20272b9dbd"},"summary":"Code and spec disagree: an agent's reply is stored and shown under its harness name, never '<name> (agent, via <harness>)'","tags":["task:24","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.112567Z","id":"de6704a4b97c9703a061b07837096532ce975344b5025f46d66e755f090b76a4","body":{"detail":"An agent reply is stored with author_name = the harness (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:885), and crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs mark_comment renders '<name> (agent, via <harness>)' or '<name> (<person>'s agent, via <harness>)' only in what agent channels read. The shell (web/shell/src/threads.ts Comment.author_name) and people's thread views keep the harness, where spec section 11 'Display' says agents show as their name, with their person where several people's agents appear. A complete version gives people's views the agent's name and person (for example a served agent_name and agent_person_name beside via_harness) and has the shell show them; that is a UI change to verify in a browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":885},"end":{"line":885},"content_hash":"e9ddb49d31234d4fac8cb0115ac7c27e3a1822d9fe538d4bdf1b97b8e57a5f55"},"summary":"People's views still show an agent reply under its harness name; only agent payloads name the agent","tags":["people","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:30.022119Z","id":"143ace1e8a8b04a8736801034139e06edcc797d58c697f49b882167c79cd66f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2594ede0","summary":"Fixed in agent payloads: mark_comment (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs) renders '<name> (agent, via <harness>)' for the reader's own person's agents and '<name> (<person>'s agent, via <harness>)' otherwise; replies from sessions with no name keep the stored harness, so the single-owner golden is unchanged. comments_reply description and docs/contract.md updated. Evidence: api_visibility::an_agent_reply_names_the_agent_its_person_and_its_harness and api_threads::agent_replies_need_the_token_and_a_sent_thread pass; golden_single_owner::the_golden_differs_only_as_section_19_lists (ignored, run by hand with CLAX_TEST_BIN) passes. People's views keeping the harness is recorded as de6704a4.","supersedes":"4c2785d3cb776979fe92f3190238e7b815c92f623ded6f5a7d41ee2d5833a86a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.270808Z","id":"5631aa8c511b4d035c82cd7d802a87f2c2fa24a6cc648af99dc32ec711a4ab83","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:81d11194","summary":"Fixed: people's views carry an agent comment's agent {name, person, person_name}, and the shell's thread cards (also the extension's panel) and the inbox name a reply '<name> (agent, via <harness>)' for the viewer's own person's agent and '<name> (<person>'s agent, via <harness>)' otherwise, as text. Evidence: web/e2e/agent-replies.spec.ts passes (owner and connected person, cards and inbox); e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts 'comment on a dev server page' reads the panel's reply line; vitest 1562+ passed (sidebar-model, inbox-model, Panel tests); full e2e 415 passed; bundle gate artifact 64062 of 64069; checked in Chromium at 1280 and 390 px, light and dark, as the owner and as Sam.","supersedes":"de6704a4b97c9703a061b07837096532ce975344b5025f46d66e755f090b76a4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.538619Z","id":"02ebe21e22e64783d02594d1a9e057386db9b2aa682bfc16572608ab9c9dae47","body":{"detail":"route_table marks a Denied route as refusing the owner's agents only when its handler source contains `.refuse_agents()?`. POST /api/approvals, POST /api/approvals/requests/{rid}/decide and DELETE /api/approvals/{id} refuse every agent with 403 browser_required (crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs:86-97), yet docs/contract.md:2976-2978 lists them as 'no', which reads as 'the owner's agents may call this'. The prose at docs/contract.md:2867-2870 says the opposite.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2063},"end":{"line":2072},"content_hash":"9ade6fe008c06fb88e5b1e71796bf48ecee93ebcf04bc2225ddb1419be7a41e0"},"suggested_fix":"Give the column a third value for browser-only routes (for example 'yes: 403 `browser_required`'), detected from the handler's use of the browser gate, or rename the column to name not_for_agents only.","summary":"The route table says 'no' under 'Refuses the owner's agents' for routes that refuse them with 403 browser_required","tags":["review","task:24","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.118054Z","id":"8e242c6a0961c2dc09d719d611115f9d6cbd7aa3220a7b1126171563820936b6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8ed8c65f","summary":"Fixed: route_table reads 'yes: 403 `browser_required`' for Denied routes whose handler gates on browser_approver, browser_person, owner_browser or require_browser on the caller; the three approvals rows in docs/contract.md now say so. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server --lib -E 'test(browser_only_routes_say_they_refuse_the_owners_agents) | test(the_contract_route_table_is_the_declared_one)' passes.","supersedes":"02ebe21e22e64783d02594d1a9e057386db9b2aa682bfc16572608ab9c9dae47","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.537874Z","id":"58014460770808acbe27ecd079b82834f25f4f9d0930e81b89e1e9d19015872d","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":429},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"03461796f42a4caaafb7403f510841b3ef9f0129ed6dfb6f95dd2f2084ce5819"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"a85b57f21058a1916e2cbc245683920df85e69bc3e8f528027a360bc8254ec1d","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.539648Z","id":"04c719932bca1a4f628bc4e8f6ee5a4494de2062931f30d79a969230e9aae1be","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1358},"end":{"line":1374},"content_hash":"6ec9bc8ee81272d9f46890e14be86cddb3beafb6cac1fd945514d5e593b4f5dc"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"b3768606271bd380607bf3197a84556cee7a55c281de3d08307c56d8729ef074","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.541429Z","id":"b191b747efdf526f66500e1f5b84193a805536a92e9729b67d104477c569a2eb","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1755},"end":{"line":1781},"content_hash":"b10b976153597d51ca9c9e38ffd71c56521a63209bf872bc9508fdcd811d7d15"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"8f0d1353b4b033a9e1623e8369d277a49a9eeaf98918111ae00ac91bb8f77e44","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:16:26.661532Z","id":"572ed3c64445cd001d3c6d2b1e26d9df24f27b2cea0bba816b64182e66544c76","body":{"detail":"Probed at e5eca81b on a home built by main 579bdc8b (schema 23) and upgraded (26): four parallel GET /api/viewers/me with LAN viewer Name-v2's legacy cookie returned Name-v2 (u_c346…) once and three new viewers with display_name null (u_b05e…, u_2a64…, u_7332…), each with its own Set-Cookie. reissue_viewer_cookie deletes the legacy hash in the first transaction; the others find no viewer and fall to mint(). The browser keeps whichever Set-Cookie it processes last, so with two or more Clax tabs restored after the upgrade the viewer likely continues as a fresh anonymous viewer: its name, seen marks and private db documents stay with the old public ID, which no cookie names any more. The same gap catches any in-flight request with the old cookie (seen, presence, a comment): ensure_viewer -> upsert_viewer creates an orphan viewer bound to the dead ULID (legacy=1). Main never minted for a request that carried a cookie, so this is new with R1. The owner's decision (swap on next visit) assumed the viewer keeps its identity across the swap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"e50039f8aa88f441ab2fe134a10c4c862c4505b2e55a52b4a473d34b55944516"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the swapped legacy hash as a short-lived tombstone (e.g. superseded_at, still naming the same non-person viewer for a few minutes, and answering /me with another fresh secret for that viewer), or keep the legacy cookie until the new secret is first presented; test with parallel /me calls on one legacy cookie.","summary":"Concurrent GET /api/viewers/me calls carrying one legacy cookie swap it once and give every other caller a new, nameless viewer, so a migrated LAN viewer with several tabs can lose its identity","tags":["review","final-rereview","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:55:21.646099Z","id":"f0ef9b15cbbde881a1dc38049e8f6779f32ded6d2560d85d2fca19a50ea99c65","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:25c71077","summary":"Fixed in 25c71077: reissue_viewer_cookie keeps the replaced legacy hash as a tombstone (viewer_cookies.replaced_at) naming the same non-person viewer for LEGACY_SWAP_GRACE_SECS (600 s), each /me in that time getting another fresh secret; expired tombstones are removed. Evidence: api_people::parallel_swaps_of_one_legacy_cookie_keep_one_viewer (four parallel GET /api/viewers/me on one legacy cookie: one viewer, name Name-v2 each time, four fresh secrets naming it, no new viewer row) passes; with the previous viewers.rs, routes/viewers.rs and identity.rs it fails with a new viewer whose display_name is null. api_people::a_legacy_viewer_cookie_is_replaced_and_never_names_a_person checks the window with a manual clock (names the viewer at 599 s, no one at 601 s).","supersedes":"572ed3c64445cd001d3c6d2b1e26d9df24f27b2cea0bba816b64182e66544c76","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:11:39.204705Z","id":"bd2323b2fafb69c09ea235edc8be2947e8e594a89231cf1e08a2752f34f24b89","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":416},"end":{"line":451},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"50b65795e983c231e0d15015bf9fd7fb5d01a9d4497b7daa6e5f6249abc62088","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:11:39.211330Z","id":"b89e41e2907ba4212e4064c6aaee7e9c20224d9ea9974b1c4c4370e9a7dda768","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":437},"end":{"line":437},"content_hash":"20fb897884082f66581aaae4c04a83c9d1e2c433b40aea73a1a440a9a722ac9f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"fa24a2c3619a75bc4062fb9ddb3df8cb54b7295203487c301b03b3295624927d","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:11:39.214072Z","id":"44dbe35d3b73d146bfa46e9dd885f00e90cde46a73709ae5cc5220ff543069f5","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":248},"end":{"line":255},"content_hash":"c999e8def53d154c4c3b3e4130701a6ba8fd9b6ed4134f44a7686b641ea38f24"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"591b42b8e96be7d14bfd583fa75f6fa9f613e65ddcf089e8c17ff793dc7f7d91","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:11:39.216709Z","id":"807d0be8be1482df52895dcbf0536064fbdf9bbd5b501848ca56a7bbcc19964a","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"b84cedbde6b64e16a70d66d11ffa402d3264208dd58d0dc94f6b215155b477cf"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"52dfbde6b019fe6a5ee6066932f9afa8c15f394339d29cb476138147b7611250","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.618696Z","id":"8cee3a29ea1a2c69da0d77a9322cb40af0a4aad9461c626ed16cd05e6111ac3a","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":430},"content_hash":"bfaf8057ddd6385c4983c312b440d45f882d993c5f8b1a4affd0ee392daab664"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"58014460770808acbe27ecd079b82834f25f4f9d0930e81b89e1e9d19015872d","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.626962Z","id":"be33235104521309d47195c8f4eb9c9e9929c89bfe6c54e31e33e2f8ff839ded","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1360},"end":{"line":1376},"content_hash":"e8e894285282e6228c9536c810324c474978159e3e71a6ca25b69b333466c739"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"04c719932bca1a4f628bc4e8f6ee5a4494de2062931f30d79a969230e9aae1be","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.630130Z","id":"67937f34f39fab81c3946c77dca44a2bb3e97a221b4c1f3b1c413f5dbe57dd1f","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1757},"end":{"line":1783},"content_hash":"56e69b31b877f2dc9ec0f1d862fd843d7d39b788968f7d3ee231ee6c885eb074"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"b191b747efdf526f66500e1f5b84193a805536a92e9729b67d104477c569a2eb","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.632904Z","id":"117da46f1f33124e145236fed1d1e23988477396aababec5139b6105b2ac8df6","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":248},"end":{"line":255},"content_hash":"aa460ed45f107cc922152128a69008f17e45a87f03bb78bd1aadd4b8dfa56ea9"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"44dbe35d3b73d146bfa46e9dd885f00e90cde46a73709ae5cc5220ff543069f5","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.635785Z","id":"d74b3b3ffffe611cf2c9472447d1ec559706a634d2909f85ed6d2c908e98890c","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"488788d1be522605a832513c2bc5a1678bd094c12ce782d53eab83705379c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"807d0be8be1482df52895dcbf0536064fbdf9bbd5b501848ca56a7bbcc19964a","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.860776Z","id":"860877c50da4fa69bab0eb46c8815a6e0deee379a37f191f95ed606cb11944a7","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.2 gives ask's result status as approved, declined or open. A request can also be withdrawn (its thread resolved or deleted, its artifact deleted, the asking session ended, a person revoked), and the poll then returns status withdrawn rather than waiting out its time on a request no one can decide. The MCP ask (plan Task 19) should say so to the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":451},"end":{"line":456},"content_hash":"03a9d61f87e1259617c1bf80109a21129cd9ff157b1dda0a83b028bcd6dd5a9d"},"summary":"The ask poll answers status withdrawn, which spec §9.2 does not list","supersedes":"639f95e4b77eba894f1947b4f4693806d319ce8d755513fa613650a2b3077d46","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.863695Z","id":"7dbbfa9399e4261661304919bf444ee464f13ba25f7a4ae90cef576e8adc37c4","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":460},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"951ad5f5efc1832ae06efe1d11fb5641065e27f2b7f937c01e21d4e7863a0c5a"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","supersedes":"f289f0be001d302174789179713a9e3eb684658a5cb5712238dc5c279313d746","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.866722Z","id":"7cd528618b578b4e3f18cb04471932ccb9b9f7adfa0f335aa818ac9953b05f36","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":417},"end":{"line":452},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"bd2323b2fafb69c09ea235edc8be2947e8e594a89231cf1e08a2752f34f24b89","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
