{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.479132Z","id":"f737b1a400255e4b35b29da9457e3d9538c3e84d461bf6718436f5bd3393cd4f","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.2 gives ask's result status as approved, declined or open. A request can also be withdrawn (its thread resolved or deleted, its artifact deleted, the asking session ended, a person revoked), and the poll then returns status withdrawn rather than waiting out its time on a request no one can decide. The MCP ask (plan Task 19) should say so to the agent.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":450},"end":{"line":455},"content_hash":"03a9d61f87e1259617c1bf80109a21129cd9ff157b1dda0a83b028bcd6dd5a9d"},"summary":"The ask poll answers status withdrawn, which spec §9.2 does not list","supersedes":"860877c50da4fa69bab0eb46c8815a6e0deee379a37f191f95ed606cb11944a7","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:06:18.493053Z","id":"4e6eee34c4cb9733ddac594d4e1caf64a17add6be31329a7096904e368ff9b15","body":{"detail":"create (line 835) and comment (line 1091) call record_comment_key after the write has committed. If the daemon stops between them, a resend under the same Idempotency-Key makes a second thread or comment. Two concurrent requests with one key both miss the lookup too (the local sync sends serially).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":835},"end":{"line":835},"content_hash":"2e4a8fa166c14f8edc258908866bb5a136a7e46b876edfe41b5e4c7f31604833"},"suggested_fix":"Record the key inside the transaction that writes the comment.","summary":"A keyed thread or comment and its comment_keys row are written in separate transactions","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.718488Z","id":"edb8beb353c0230e1f8351d9da2f2ae133d4a656ace689cc1c7d1036c68332c4","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1130},"end":{"line":1168},"content_hash":"7693c4df4615731751c4af05990a46d8953679703556241c78896827d043ad56"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","supersedes":"39e7ea887339101b87d0432e04a4627966991261922048a95057644b0ab9ac99","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.730610Z","id":"1f3bf3b083ae1359d9bd7feec0e6911b2cda9d2a0398cce83087fce246d3548a","body":{"detail":"GET /api/inbox?q= searches inbox_fts, whose text holds each reply's body (crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs insert_at). Since 60859f1e a person who may not read an artifact's comments gets its reply items without body or summary, but a search still returns or omits those items by their text, and total counts them, so the text can be probed word by word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":302},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"5f5a1bfceba39c7a1481ebe8360a90fc57ed780f72988b4d9e3b4aa245ea54bd"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, leave out of a text search the items of artifacts whose comments the recipient may not read (filter the matched rows with inbox::reads_comments before paging, or keep text searches to items whose artifact they read comments at).","summary":"A hosted person's inbox search matches reply text they may no longer read","supersedes":"24fe742595ff5c527a584774757fc9e5e10ed54b5fd78c527804712bb565d390","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.742959Z","id":"421abeee4eaaa480188e5b9dc62819f47bd4a79c8c125a09228caebc9c131cff","body":{"detail":"with_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"c9cb67acbf610798cd5947c52fe23d53362f2923e5adea4a53d8673a8df4037b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"d1619874b392af10884baf4542d4c1108f72d2480841a86981a1e9cf2ca2ecf3","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.755260Z","id":"d029b9970c060c8838cc746297affb3983aabe743c943196a999864d40dedee3","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":478},"content_hash":"03461796f42a4caaafb7403f510841b3ef9f0129ed6dfb6f95dd2f2084ce5819"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"58014460770808acbe27ecd079b82834f25f4f9d0930e81b89e1e9d19015872d","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.767479Z","id":"7f99fd622d560ff8a15695771d8efa25570edc723ee6c376165de5bb24522fb1","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":684},"end":{"line":684},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"54a094bac923d1c120730ceb85aa55b7bc08e7d13ddcfbfd5a542bb54bf63ade","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.779699Z","id":"16293258bc7748739fbf62dc7f4ec95e5af08e121fc44eeb095625de96c399bf","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":519},"end":{"line":554},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"50b65795e983c231e0d15015bf9fd7fb5d01a9d4497b7daa6e5f6249abc62088","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.791984Z","id":"ede1c137c61df7ef3808273ab3f05bd98d3172fad7fc0641c510157e0aaab4dd","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":540},"end":{"line":540},"content_hash":"20fb897884082f66581aaae4c04a83c9d1e2c433b40aea73a1a440a9a722ac9f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"fa24a2c3619a75bc4062fb9ddb3df8cb54b7295203487c301b03b3295624927d","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.804208Z","id":"5e607d118cc7f013f1ac2dcbbebeec0617ca994d68a33dc100d8de05ef9aad77","body":{"detail":"create (line 835) and comment (line 1091) call record_comment_key after the write has committed. If the daemon stops between them, a resend under the same Idempotency-Key makes a second thread or comment. Two concurrent requests with one key both miss the lookup too (the local sync sends serially).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":893},"end":{"line":893},"content_hash":"2e4a8fa166c14f8edc258908866bb5a136a7e46b876edfe41b5e4c7f31604833"},"suggested_fix":"Record the key inside the transaction that writes the comment.","summary":"A keyed thread or comment and its comment_keys row are written in separate transactions","supersedes":"4e6eee34c4cb9733ddac594d4e1caf64a17add6be31329a7096904e368ff9b15","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.816450Z","id":"32769653a05b120daf3c1eb81c07c32c20b2b94fa0bc3d74a3665b255883eff8","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"fdef32ef55ec060aeebfe4fd3b77d7814bf6706887dea024f0f20ef0a60067d3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"f700615fc0a3f8a1aee1956cf1cc843a0cea305467f8426880dcede5535550e1","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.919084Z","id":"96b68dd07eee21d3624f615e74d2a0d1d3a3c1d8a2052569300b8b36ecc2d5ae","body":{"detail":"The token reaches only people who may read the artifact: the listing and the live socket answer 404 to a member without read (the member gate) and 401 sign_in_required to a visitor who gave no name, and the drafts events ride the working topic of streams opened for a person or a hosted guest (Hub::open_with in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs). Tested by api_hosted::drafts_and_live_layers_reach_signed_in_people_who_may_read_the_page and web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts 'a guest on a page shared by link sees an agent drafting and shows the draft at its URL'. As with a content key (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:404:406), a person who loses the right keeps reading a revision whose token they hold, here until it is revised or ends.","kind":"comment","references":"1895c9b55a6a878db96a5fd76e5e6273b894e2d7095dae4d1dddc2c143fa63af","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":504},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"On a hosted daemon too the draft URL is its token alone: the gate (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs content_path, Content::Draft) passes /c/<aid>/draft/… to these routes with Referrer-Policy: no-referrer and no content key","supersedes":"67b915cdb4cd981266b48044b42f2133e22df6d2ea346c4725c3bcb5354f97b1","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.406655Z","id":"7f936847ad91890fa1938f81112b8eeefcb37209ffab5bdd4a0915850251bfde","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1000},"end":{"line":1038},"content_hash":"40fe5bd49c9bedfd0cc9e32fbc96f95347e71b7eb3d7f6b06ea15446dca7af0b"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","supersedes":"edb8beb353c0230e1f8351d9da2f2ae133d4a656ace689cc1c7d1036c68332c4","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.425797Z","id":"a7ee35dc3afdf794ba1d5c48d45581ee44fd0f01207bfe8ea8e55fd08a00cad2","body":{"detail":"blob reads the bytes with Store::asset_bytes inside store_call and answers Body::from(bytes); before ContentStore it streamed the file with tokio::fs. Same response, more memory per request and a store worker held for the read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":169},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"b0bceb440a27349c53fc6b900e603075c22b7957ab45d8ca558e69e49915cf06"},"summary":"An asset's bytes (up to MAX_ASSET_BYTES, 20 MiB) are read whole on a store worker before /_blob serves them","supersedes":"633749096d181675349e3d771970d9552d6b3db7c28599b25f3ae491a97c5caa","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.445189Z","id":"ce3cfffe0890516f2cb223d3c73de3d1298f4e3be9a71aca962307e00588b4be","body":{"detail":"lookup reads the file's bytes through ContentStore::read_file (Vec<u8>) inside store_call, and file/raw_file answer Body::from(bytes) (lines 262, 337); before ContentStore they opened the file with tokio::fs and streamed it. Responses are the same, but each request holds the whole file in memory and spends a store worker on the read. A streaming read on the interface (a body or chunk stream per backend) would restore streaming natively.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"9235976499b9515bbe2a53744bf1881463b983c8f62b3d2f24f87d397d3250e3"},"summary":"Version files are read whole into memory on a store worker before they are served, where they were streamed from disk","supersedes":"3d651998b825490fc2e0a24e5347b0e9e81666525ba86f0a06f258caf94904f2","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.464466Z","id":"b0f23739def46d112231fc91bc08239b397382ee66ef5782b1abcb35e02b2406","body":{"detail":"The hosted prototype's draft tool also watches the artifact (hosted/src/mcp/tools.ts draft), so comments made while a draft shows route to the drafting session. Here only the working record is kept: a draft precedes a publish, and publishing watches. A comment made during a draft on an artifact no session watches waits untargeted until a session publishes or watches it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"a030bf7cba7c91a045b3d4163c4021182cd464de0290d8178b2464350f2bf86f"},"summary":"Drafting marks the session working but does not watch the artifact","supersedes":"37d30892699a4e25ea3c350e57ef8e649af977934c982eadd8b874b154508b04","tags":["drafts","revisit:people comment on an artifact while it is drafted and the comments wait untargeted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.483143Z","id":"b9771021b54e06eac0000cff4acaec3addb9fd6d6a7aefc45f030bbff10fca91","body":{"detail":"Visibility filters agent channels only (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs header): a person's browser reads every file at /c/<id>/v/<n>/, ACAO *, and the content policy (routes/content.rs content_policy) restricts no connections. A drafting agent's page script can fetch the base version's files withheld from that agent (which the draft URL itself never serves) and send them to a host the agent reads. A published page can do the same; a draft adds that its script runs for viewers with no version recorded (drafts::delete is unaudited, put records only working.start). The shell no longer welcomes a draft page's greeting (ec3d3724), so it gets no page capability.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":504},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"A draft page's script runs in people's browsers unrecorded and can carry files withheld from its agent off the machine","supersedes":"34da92851974e18a31fe4e026d33299c8f297bf4fb9c15080b089893959baae1","tags":["drafts","visibility","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.503118Z","id":"808970a34b7d615fa6d554edd9441c966ecf19f538387f8c30523d73606f1400","body":{"detail":"serve sends drafted HTML marked and tinted but not wrapped (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page), so a draft never greets the shell: no pins, no comment mode, and no window capabilities (db, comments, room, sample). A page that needs a capability to render shows its fallback in a draft. Wrapping it would make the shell treat the draft as the base version's page (its hello names a version).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"eca1e26d7d420907fa242391f29ad9e801264b3909753b325e2d537ad065d5dd"},"summary":"A draft page is served without the bridge, so its page capabilities do not run in a draft","supersedes":"e425401487e4deb34fcb9c95063cc69dbe9ea3af919991b44475fdf07cfb7264","tags":["drafts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.521947Z","id":"550e635f0920ee5bd91dc6d9ecca1ac9d86f800a88cee7ac36053089d6ff3de1","body":{"detail":"serve refuses agents but checks no cookie: a frame on the artifact origin (<id>.localhost) carries none. So a token that reached a person later revoked, or that the draft page itself leaks (its own <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"unsafe-url\"> overrides the Referrer-Policy: no-referrer header, and the content policy limits no connections), reads the revision from any client that reaches the daemon, for at most DRAFT_IDLE_SECS after its last revision. The token is 128 random bits, compared in constant time (clax_core::drafts::Drafts::file), and logged nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":504},"content_hash":"e0cb4005de23fc65519fcd9f6ddffe672e808c3fb3d4c12e129da01b534604e3"},"summary":"A draft URL is its token alone: whoever holds a revision's token reads the draft until it is revised or ends","supersedes":"1895c9b55a6a878db96a5fd76e5e6273b894e2d7095dae4d1dddc2c143fa63af","tags":["drafts","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.540821Z","id":"12e45a31044836310cd745b632533ae5cb3b502bb75033e2e79073c0b1649093","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1360:1376, record be332351. CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1212},"end":{"line":1253},"content_hash":"81457863f5a6f37f002514515cebebced86ea812b3069431a7be337d750945e9"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"fcaedbd03ae5b40747f2a0524b66e790a7b32b8b2fbbf602a31254b3b528c2f2","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.559491Z","id":"2278fadd7d83cab8cc47d67cf920517b0b7ff55c09942c4e431b12d4d590e464","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1757:1783, record 67937f34. Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1801},"end":{"line":1828},"content_hash":"6cce876e324df5229bc43d9cb8fef99778d482642c51a693a6f98c18e4f83838"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"2bb59e057fa61f4087ed1f3026d4beabc135fb771a24579c02421494f7a3f629","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.578184Z","id":"8041ddee9c1876808121d61d1688ada80b7691321d0936ae14b3205d226a7b13","body":{"detail":"GET /api/inbox?q= searches inbox_fts, whose text holds each reply's body (crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs insert_at). Since 60859f1e a person who may not read an artifact's comments gets its reply items without body or summary, but a search still returns or omits those items by their text, and total counts them, so the text can be probed word by word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":306},"content_hash":"5f5a1bfceba39c7a1481ebe8360a90fc57ed780f72988b4d9e3b4aa245ea54bd"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, leave out of a text search the items of artifacts whose comments the recipient may not read (filter the matched rows with inbox::reads_comments before paging, or keep text searches to items whose artifact they read comments at).","summary":"A hosted person's inbox search matches reply text they may no longer read","supersedes":"1f3bf3b083ae1359d9bd7feec0e6911b2cda9d2a0398cce83087fce246d3548a","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.596862Z","id":"fb6f1151e4f556e05d975d2b926ad9ce815e952b2cd116c44335f41121b85653","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":469},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"951ad5f5efc1832ae06efe1d11fb5641065e27f2b7f937c01e21d4e7863a0c5a"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","supersedes":"7dbbfa9399e4261661304919bf444ee464f13ba25f7a4ae90cef576e8adc37c4","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.615910Z","id":"79a77c127fb45fbb878e03de38bfdb564accaf849ba9bba48c0fdf2d72a05180","body":{"detail":"session() checks the viewer and takes the seat when the socket opens, and then only watches for the seat's release for want of input, the artifact's deletion and the daemon's shutdown. Revoking a person (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs person_revoked_at) does not close it, unlike their /api/stream streams (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs listen ends them at the visibility generation's bump). In this daemon that grants nothing new: a revoked person is a LAN viewer, who may still read and comment on every artifact (docs/usage.md, 'LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them'), and could reopen the socket at once. Relay::clear_text (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs), meant for a person who may no longer comment, has no caller for the same reason. A port where access is per artifact (the hosted design's shares, spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.1) must re-admit on each visibility bump and close the socket (4403) when the check fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"8338b9a4139be4d85a567419878643836bdaddf66e9fbaf430d2ff2da0832379"},"summary":"A live socket is admitted once, at its upgrade, and not again when the viewer's access changes","supersedes":"36c662a8d41a43133f4b3b6cd2a5a6ea8fb7efb6e4bdc250f4e7811229ca6070","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.634473Z","id":"df3e5f73810aa99ef38709d3ad1ae2116fe64bd18a7537d482aafaa823f4ea72","body":{"detail":"routes::live_layers::reopen joins the hub afresh (Relay::resend gives the rejoined socket everyone else's state at the next flush), but what this socket had shown others is gone with the old hub: a peer's arrow disappears after a wake until that person moves. Persisting the relay is not worth it; the page could resend its state on a second welcome.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":486},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"c29cb5af2f5aa9cc137265695d688d3b9b5b654e32cb64b2008cddb10e813f65"},"summary":"A woken live socket rejoins with nothing of its person's pointer, selection or draft, until the page sends again","supersedes":"c031366b65888ea5945f83c653cbd2142c1f01b6f70524b84c6da0cf1be6668d","tags":["worker","live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.653190Z","id":"e91e543ada23ee0ce0e22a8eeb37ef8edd2a5015936a3d669dbd654b89dcb448","body":{"detail":"session_header answers `<session ID>.<secret>` (spec 2026-10-08 §6.9). The MCP transport spec treats Mcp-Session-Id as an opaque session handle, not a credential, so a client's debug log or an HTTP proxy's access log may record it. A logged value lets whoever also holds the agent token act in that session with its rights (its narrowing still binds it); without the token it proves nothing, as the token is checked first (crate::agent::authenticate).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"a5b86af4cce22a916edb655426bdacd1f3d183eb47662b38b465087e446c91ba"},"summary":"An agent token's session secret travels in Mcp-Session-Id, which MCP clients and proxies treat as an ordinary header and may log","supersedes":"1db454339a9a63049228ec6a5a9f5be3410b4a919c41ca0a491227839e084652","tags":["hosted","agent-token","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.672447Z","id":"12db18b83147f579fce6a873699cf31d595d074d95f56f3cc3f8b671855570c2","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":683},"end":{"line":683},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"7f99fd622d560ff8a15695771d8efa25570edc723ee6c376165de5bb24522fb1","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.691713Z","id":"860dd2e388c485cd60e2833d44d26dcb0862a8df5bebc3c27cd530335f256e8f","body":{"detail":"Natively the slot lives in stream::Conn, dropped when hyper drops the body, which it does once a write to the closed connection fails (the next event or keep-alive). A browser reconnecting many streams at once near crates/clax-server/src/socket_caps.rs MAX_PER_SESSION (32) may be refused 429 too_many_streams until then; a resume of a still-attached stream is exempt (slot_for). The Worker's sockets close promptly (websocket_close). Related: record 46a7bb0f.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":235},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"72e96a8e84bd50a8b081efd81a60454bf4e93d67b55592c689a0bc0efaecdfa2"},"summary":"A closed SSE stream gives its place under the cap back only once the daemon notices its connection dropped","supersedes":"ddc04061cbe98b468ed71acf6cb01e2442e244f17348fce635c0f5a25ed7e07c","tags":["streams","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.710585Z","id":"a1955db9786b3d0221a84fbcf4c9afe6126756f1e4c1f366504a92437617cac5","body":{"detail":"A person whose clax-comments read at the artifact is taken away keeps a loud artifact:<aid> topic (thread events with the newest comment) and a live socket that relays typing and drafts until the stream subscribes again or the socket reopens; one given the right later stays quiet until then. Rights narrowed end the person's streams only on revocation (Hub::end_streams_of). Same shape as record 2cd3748f for live sockets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"4a98e1f5011bf0f240ec4911c25f89c0663d93193d805efbf2aa27c29e9f71c3"},"summary":"Whether an artifact topic or a live socket carries comment text is decided once, at subscription or upgrade","supersedes":"40f37a3c964752e535e121e21a813e1f3c351144a96ac8a885c03d7c21353658","tags":["security","rights","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.730537Z","id":"4bcee31c53ee284af81f2edbab4e6b85bc8fac5365539f1b7085e6b383105429","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":521},"end":{"line":556},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"7cd528618b578b4e3f18cb04471932ccb9b9f7adfa0f335aa818ac9953b05f36","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.749456Z","id":"aef3f856844bacab7163b938bad4285ada7ae6d166b567661b6aa5c940a347f3","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":542},"end":{"line":542},"content_hash":"20fb897884082f66581aaae4c04a83c9d1e2c433b40aea73a1a440a9a722ac9f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"98f9273f4c445f23f55b627ed148cd8b9973391abc5846c4907b9b294dc1868f","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.768275Z","id":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","body":{"detail":"create (line 835) and comment (line 1091) call record_comment_key after the write has committed. If the daemon stops between them, a resend under the same Idempotency-Key makes a second thread or comment. Two concurrent requests with one key both miss the lookup too (the local sync sends serially).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":895},"end":{"line":895},"content_hash":"2e4a8fa166c14f8edc258908866bb5a136a7e46b876edfe41b5e4c7f31604833"},"suggested_fix":"Record the key inside the transaction that writes the comment.","summary":"A keyed thread or comment and its comment_keys row are written in separate transactions","supersedes":"5e607d118cc7f013f1ac2dcbbebeec0617ca994d68a33dc100d8de05ef9aad77","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.787106Z","id":"2a28edef7edf953f3c2c6071659e74dd56bea53946280cb3e337dc1b4b00f924","body":{"detail":"ChunkWriter (toolpath.rs:146-160) blocks the store job's thread on the response body's room (Handle::block_on), and on a Worker the store job runs inline on the only thread, so ChunkWriter, stream_export, export and the route are cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")). A hosted export needs a writer that buffers within a bound or an async export in clax-core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"e1be6dcc3808fd8eeee4556f4bec26441db83a04790990b10fc950f28a9e3f4e"},"summary":"The audit export is native only: no /api/toolpath/export on wasm32","supersedes":"af92a5c2c3d75fdd2781cd5b782cda569ad2eeaebb7bae91879b9b310bd7fc34","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.805951Z","id":"0794174e74b06c9a49f08176b94517b51dafbb926f1fd0b777a3ca745cf70d0c","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":263},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"aa460ed45f107cc922152128a69008f17e45a87f03bb78bd1aadd4b8dfa56ea9"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"117da46f1f33124e145236fed1d1e23988477396aababec5139b6105b2ac8df6","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.825032Z","id":"7c699d113ed2c33d4ea1fbc506df4653546f362127c1653cd34a5eaf3cbab872","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":116},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"488788d1be522605a832513c2bc5a1678bd094c12ce782d53eab83705379c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"d74b3b3ffffe611cf2c9472447d1ec559706a634d2909f85ed6d2c908e98890c","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.854670Z","id":"c1348876a19285bedf4127671e31080c6efa46cc6bac15ebefe1686d9f78db8e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:acb06db94cb825ed096dfe96b9336cb4c05b6de8","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:468:470 as f4bc239e in git:acb06db9","supersedes":"d029b9970c060c8838cc746297affb3983aabe743c943196a999864d40dedee3","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
